Sangpenpa = (t:n) (w:Most High) (d:title of God, the Most High One; sangpen highest with pa for a male person, written with a capital) (e:~ in a aw hong gingsak hi) (b:sangpenpa) (r:10.22.14/19.91.1) (q:draft)
Titu = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Titus) (e:~ tawh kong sawl khawm uh hi) (r:47.8.18/48.2.3) (q:draft)
aam = (t:v) (w:be jealous/jealous) (d:not willing to share what is one's own with a rival; in the verses of God toward his people) (e:a ~ Pasian ka hi a) (r:2.20.5/26.16.42) (q:draft)
beng = (t:v) (w:hunt/fish) (d:go after animals or fish to catch them; sa beng hunt game, nga beng catch fish) (e:kei adingin sa va ~ in) (r:1.27.3/33.5.8) (q:draft)
beng = (t:v) (w:slap/strike/clap) (d:hit with the open hand; paang beng slap the cheek) (e:ka paang a ~ dingin) (r:18.16.10) (q:draft)
bukkongah = (t:adv) (w:at the entrance of the tent/at the tent door) (d:bukkong tent entrance with the place marker ah; kikhopna bukkongah is at the entrance to the tent of meeting) (e:kikhopna ~ mihonte kikhawm hi) (b:bukkong) (r:3.8.4/3.16.7) (q:draft)
citengah = (t:adv) (w:in every/at every/everywhere) (d:citeng every with the place marker ah, after a noun; mun citengah is in every place, in all directions) (e:mun ~ ka thehthang ding a) (b:citeng) (r:26.12.14/26.16.31) (q:draft)
dawimangpa = (t:n) (w:devil) (d:the devil, chief of the evil spirits; dawi evil spirit and mang chief, with pa for a male person) (e:~ in Topa kiang pan paikhia a) (r:40.4.11/42.4.5) (q:draft)
deeng = (t:v) (w:throw at/pelt/stone) (d:throw something at a person; suang tawh deeng is stone someone) (e:suang tawh ~ dingin suang a tawm) (r:43.10.31/40.21.35) (q:draft)
donga = (t:prep) (w:until/up to/to) (d:dong until with a, joining the phrase to what follows; tu ni donga a om, which is there to this day) (e:tu ni ~ a om suang honpi) (b:dong) (r:6.7.26/1.19.38) (q:draft)
gakin = (t:v) (w:gird/tie round/fasten) (d:gak tie round the waist with the linking ending in, tying or having tied a belt or sash) (e:kawnggakte tawh amaute ~) (b:gak) (r:3.8.13/11.18.46) (q:draft)
gennate = (t:n) (w:words/sayings/things said) (d:plural of genna; what someone has said) (e:Khuamial lakah no kiangah ka ~) (b:genna) (r:40.10.27/23.48.6) (q:draft)
gentheih = (t:v) (w:be able to tell/be able to say/can be told) (d:gen tell with theih can; gentheih loh is beyond telling) (e:Lungdamna Thu na ~ nading uh hunhoih) (b:gen) (r:42.21.13/28.9.9) (q:draft)
gentheih = (t:v) (w:suffer/be in trouble/be in distress) (d:form of genthei used before hun and na; ka gentheih hunin, in my time of trouble) (e:ka ~ hunin keima belh na hi hi) (b:genthei) (r:19.59.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
guahpi = (t:n) (w:heavy rain/downpour/rainstorm) (d:guah rain with pi great) (e:Tu-in ~ ka zusak ding a) (b:guah) (r:26.13.11/18.37.9) (q:draft)
gualzosak = (t:v) (w:give victory/make victorious/cause to triumph) (d:gualzo win with causative sak) (e:David a paina peuhpeuhah ~ hi) (b:gualzo) (r:13.18.13/18.17.4) (q:draft)
gunei = (t:adj) (w:poisonous/venomous) (d:gu poison with nei have; gul gunei is a poisonous snake, a viper) (e:gamlakah gul ~ leh mom-ai lak) (r:5.8.15/23.11.8) (q:draft)
gupkhiatna = (t:n) (w:salvation/deliverance/rescue) (d:the act of saving or setting free) (e:Topa in ama ~ kitheisak khin zo a) (r:19.98.2/58.1.14) (q:draft)
hah = (t:v) (w:prune/clear/cut back) (d:cut back vines or clear land of its growth) (e:na leenggui lo uh ~-in a gahte) (r:3.25.3) (q:draft)
hah = (t:adv) (w:earnestly/carefully/urgently) (d:before a verb, doing it with effort or insistence; hah gen is urge) (e:lo khat a nget ding ~ gen hi) (r:6.15.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
hah = (t:v) (w:open/be open/be awake) (d:of the eyes, form of hak open; mit hah is the open eyes or their look, a glance; na hah sungin is while you are awake) (e:a mit a ~ hangin) (r:44.9.8/20.6.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
hamsia = (t:n) (w:curse) (d:evil called down on someone, the opposite of thupha blessing; also the act of cursing) (e:thupha khat leh ~ khat ka koih hi) (r:5.11.26/5.28.19) (q:draft)
hanciamin = (t:v) (w:strive/try hard/make every effort) (d:hanciam with the linking ending in, striving, with great effort) (e:nakpi takin ~ ka lungsim ka pia a) (b:hanciam) (r:21.7.25/27.6.14) (q:draft)
hanna = (t:n) (w:courage/bravery/boldness) (d:from hang brave with na; lungsim hanna is courage of heart) (e:amau’ lungsim ~ a bei hi) (r:19.107.26/18.23.16) (q:draft)
hausak = (t:v) (w:make rich/enrich/prosper) (d:hau rich with causative sak; hausak kik is make rich again, restore the fortunes of) (e:Kei hong itte ka ~ a) (b:hau) (r:20.8.21/24.49.6) (q:draft)
hehnep = (t:v) (w:comfort/console/encourage) (d:form of hehnem used before bangin, nading, na and sawm) (e:A nu in a ta a ~ bangin) (r:23.66.13/49.6.22) (q:draft)
hi'ng = (t:v) (w:am/I am) (d:hi be with the first person singular ending ing shortened, at the end of a sentence) (e:kei in ama aa ~) (r:22.2.16/33.7.1) (q:draft)
hihnate = (t:n) (w:deeds/doings/actions) (d:plural of hihna; the things someone does or has done) (e:ka ~ khempeuh a kilawm mah ahihna) (b:hihna) (r:26.14.23/42.9.43) (q:draft)
kalsuan = (t:v) (w:walk/step/take a step) (d:move forward on foot; also of the way one lives, Kha deih bangin kalsuan, walk according to the Spirit) (e:Ka ~ nading mun tanzau nong pia a) (r:19.18.36/45.8.1) (q:draft)
kampaunate = (t:n) (w:words/speech/utterances) (d:plural of kampauna, the things a person says; English versions often have lips) (e:na ~ in na pil lam tak) (b:kampauna) (r:20.5.2/20.15.26) (q:draft)
kamtaipa = (t:n) (w:messenger) (d:kamtai with -pa, a male messenger) (e:a ~ in laikhak khat hong pia hi) (b:kamtai) (r:16.6.5/10.11.22) (q:draft)
keimahmah = (t:pron) (w:I myself/myself) (d:emphatic form of keimah, I and no other) (e:~ in ka tuute ka zong ding) (b:keimah) (r:26.34.11/5.18.19) (q:draft)
khaguh = (t:n) (w:jawbone/jaw) (d:the bone of the jaw; la khaguh is the jawbone of a donkey) (e:la ~ thak khat mu a) (r:7.15.15/18.41.2) (q:draft)
khahkhong = (t:v) (w:let go unpunished/spare/tolerate/acquit) (d:leave someone alone without punishing or stopping them; mostly used with a negative) (e:amah ~ loin, amah na iim kei) (r:5.13.8/33.6.11) (q:draft)
khauhin = (t:adv) (w:stubbornly/stiffly/firmly) (d:khauh with the suffix -in; after lung or lungsim it means being hard-hearted, stubborn) (e:hih mite lungsim ~ hong langpan’ zen uh) (b:khauh) (r:24.5.23/18.40.17) (q:draft)
khuttum = (t:n) (w:fist) (d:the closed hand; khuttum zial is to clench the fist, khuttum cia is the size of a fist) (e:Pasian langpangin a ~ a lahsan) (r:18.15.25/11.18.44) (q:draft)
kidamsak = (t:v) (w:be healed/be cured/recover) (d:ki- form of damsak; often with a negative, of a wound or of anger that cannot be healed) (e:Samaria’ meima ~ thei lo a) (b:damsak) (r:33.1.9/14.22.6) (q:draft)
kigingsa = (t:adj) (w:ready/prepared/alert/steadfast) (d:kiging with -sa, already made ready; mostly in a kigingsa-in om, be ready, be on the alert) (e:a ~-in om tawntung un) (b:kiging) (r:60.3.15/6.8.4) (q:draft)
kihen = (t:v) (w:be bound/be tied/be chained) (d:ki- form of hen, to bind or tie) (e:Na khutte ~ lo hi) (b:hen) (r:10.3.34/40.16.19) (q:draft)
kihisakte = (t:n) (w:the proud/the arrogant/the haughty) (d:plural of kihisak; people who think highly of themselves) (e:mi ~ bang mahin sim lo a) (b:kihisak) (r:20.3.34/20.18.12) (q:draft)
kikaihkhop = (t:v) (w:be gathered/gather together/assemble) (d:ki- form of kaihkhop, of people or flocks drawn together in one place) (e:tuuhonte khempeuh a ~ khit ciangin) (b:kaihkhop) (r:1.29.3/13.11.13) (q:draft)
kikeek = (t:v) (w:be torn/tear/rip) (d:ki- form of keek, of cloth or a net that tears) (e:ngen a ~ hi) (b:keek) (r:42.5.6/42.23.45) (q:draft)
kikep = (t:v) (w:keep oneself/refrain/abstain) (d:ki- form of kep; with pan or panin, keep oneself away from something) (e:thuciamna bawl ding pan na ~ uh leh) (b:kep) (r:5.23.22/59.1.27) (q:draft)
kikep = (t:v) (w:be careful/take care) (d:in kikep nading, so as to be careful; kikep nading thu hilh is to warn) (e:ci-in ~ nading thu a hilh hi) (b:kep) (r:44.27.10/52.5.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
kikupna = (t:n) (w:consultation/discussion/deliberation) (d:noun from kikup, talking a matter over together; kikupna nei is to hold a consultation) (e:makai khempeuh tawh ~ khat nei hi) (b:kikup) (r:13.13.1/11.12.28) (q:draft)
kiphasakin = (t:v) (w:be proud/boast/exalt oneself) (d:kiphasak with the linking suffix -in, being proud and then doing the next action; also proudly) (e:na lungsim uh ~ kei nong mangngilh) (b:kiphasak) (r:28.13.6/1.16.4) (q:draft)
kiphatsak = (t:v) (w:boast/be proud/be arrogant) (d:praise oneself; before pau or gamtat it means speak or behave proudly) (e:na ~ gamtat nawn kei ding uh) (b:kiphat) (r:33.2.3/19.17.10) (q:draft)
kiphatsak = (t:v) (w:cause to be praised) (d:ki- form of phatsak, let someone or something be praised) (e:mi cimawhte nangma min ~ in) (b:phatsak) (r:19.74.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisehte = (t:n) (w:appointed ones/those appointed/those assigned) (d:kiseh with plural -te, the ones that are appointed or set; pawi a kisehte are the appointed feasts) (e:pawi a ~ a gen hi) (b:kiseh) (r:3.23.44/13.6.48) (q:draft)
kisimmawh = (t:v) (w:be despised/be scorned/be shamed) (d:ki- form of simmawh) (e:ka mite hong ~ nawn lo ding hi) (b:simmawh) (r:29.2.26/19.119.141) (q:draft)
kituh = (t:v) (w:be sown/be planted) (d:ki- form of tuh, of seed put in the ground) (e:khaici ~ kik ding hi) (b:tuh) (r:26.36.9/46.15.44) (q:draft)
kituh = (t:v) (w:contend/compete/dispute) (d:strive against one another over something, as for a throne, in a court case or to be the first) (e:kumpigam khat leh khat kumpi-za ~ ding hi) (r:23.19.2/24.50.8) (q:draft)
koihsa = (t:adj) (w:laid up/stored up/set/placed) (d:koih with -sa, already put; a koihsa before a noun is that which someone has put, set or laid down) (e:Nangma ~ ngeina kipte in) (b:koih) (r:19.119.138/19.31.19) (q:draft)
kongkhakah = (t:n) (w:at the door/at the entrance) (d:kongkhak with the place marker ah) (e:~ dingin kong ka hong kiu hi) (b:kongkhak) (r:66.3.20/2.29.11) (q:draft)
laksa = (t:adj) (w:taken/captured/seized) (d:lak, take, with -sa, already taken; a laksa before a noun is what someone has taken or captured) (e:David in Amalekte’ ~ khempeuh ngah kik hi) (b:lak) (r:9.30.18/14.17.2) (q:draft)
laktel = (t:v) (w:show clearly/make plain/prove/point out) (d:make something plainly known, as the truth of a word or the fault of a person) (e:nang’ khialhna hong ~ kik leh) (r:20.25.8/23.43.26) (q:draft)
lapa = (t:n) (w:taker/one who takes/one who gathers) (d:la, take, with -pa: the man who takes or gathers something) (e:A hun-a an ~ in mipil hi a) (b:la) (r:20.10.5/26.18.7) (q:draft)
lawnin = (t:v) (w:throw/cast/hurl/toss) (d:lawn with the linking suffix -in, throwing and then doing the next action) (e:~ Filistiapa’ taltang kha hi) (b:lawn) (r:9.17.49/5.9.17) (q:draft)
lawnsuk = (t:v) (w:throw down/cast down/hurl down) (d:lawn with suk, downward) (e:amaute in Jezebel ~ uh hi) (b:lawn) (r:12.9.33/14.25.12) (q:draft)
leengkhia = (t:v) (w:fly away/fly out) (d:leeng with khia, out) (e:mei-ek ~ zaizai hi) (b:leeng) (r:18.41.19/19.55.6) (q:draft)
leengkhia = (t:v) (w:revolt/rebel/break away) (d:break free from the rule of another country) (e:Judah gam ukna panin Edom mite ~ hi) (b:leeng) (r:12.8.22/14.21.8) (q:draft)
lehheekpa = (t:n) (w:betrayer/traitor) (d:lehheek with -pa, the man who betrays) (e:Kei hong ~ hong nai zo hi) (b:lehheek) (r:40.26.46/43.12.4) (q:draft)
lohte = (t:part) (d:negative loh with plural -te: those that are not, the things not done or not approved, as in hoih sak lohte, things not found good, evil) (e:Pasian’ hoih sak ~ hong sem hi) (b:loh) (r:24.52.2/5.13.13) (q:draft)
luahte = (t:n) (w:inheritance/heritage/possessions) (d:plural of luah; in the Psalms the luahte of God are the people who belong to him) (e:na ~ thupha pia in) (b:luah) (r:19.28.9/19.94.14) (q:draft)
lungnemna = (t:n) (w:gentleness/meekness/humility) (d:noun from lungnem, a soft and gentle heart; also patience in waiting) (e:Khazih’ ~ leh hehpihna tawh) (b:lungnem) (r:47.10.1/49.4.2) (q:draft)
mangkhin = (t:adv) (w:completely/away/utterly) (d:placed after a verb to show that the action is finished and the thing is gone, as in bei mangkhin, come to an end altogether) (e:Lungnopna khempeuh bei ~ ta a) (b:mang) (r:25.5.15/35.1.6) (q:draft)
mangmu = (t:n) (w:tribute/tax/levy) (d:a payment required by a ruler or for the house of God, named beside siah, tax) (e:siah leh ~ leh losapte) (r:15.4.20/14.24.9) (q:draft)
mangmu = (t:v) (w:see a vision/fall into a trance) (d:mang, dream, and mu, see: see something as in a dream while awake) (e:~ a kisa hi) (r:44.12.9/44.10.10) (q:draft)
manphazaw = (t:adj) (w:more valuable/more precious/worth more) (d:manpha with -zaw, the comparative; used with sangin, than) (e:kham sangin ~ hi) (b:manpha) (r:20.3.14/40.10.31) (q:draft)
meiphualpi = (t:n) (w:furnace/kiln) (d:meiphual with -pi, great: a large enclosed fire for burning or smelting) (e:~ khu bangin kahto hi) (b:meiphual) (r:1.19.28/27.3.19) (q:draft)
misia = (t:n) (w:bad person/evil person/the wicked) (d:mi, person, and sia, bad; the opposite of mipha, a good person) (e:~ in siatna thaman ngah a) (r:20.14.14/20.15.3) (q:draft)
muhte = (t:n) (w:things seen/what one has seen) (d:muh with plural -te; ka muhte is the things I saw) (e:na ~ uh kuamah kiangah gen kei un) (b:muh) (r:41.9.9/43.3.11) (q:draft)
namdangte = (t:n) (w:foreigners/other nations/Gentiles) (d:plural of namdang; mi namdangte are people of other nations) (e:mi ~ lakah kong thehthang ding hi) (b:namdang) (r:16.1.8/28.7.8) (q:draft)
nan = (t:v) (w:withstand/resist/hold out against) (d:stand firm against an enemy or an attack; written with a final apostrophe before zawh and nading) (e:gal ~’ nading kulh nei loin) (r:26.38.11/49.6.11) (q:draft)
nan = (t:v) (w:support/prop up) (d:hold something up from below; the noun form with -na is a support or prop, as under a basin stand) (e:a ~’na li om ciat hi) (r:11.7.34) (q:draft, low confidence)
nem = (t:adj) (w:soft/gentle/weak/tender) (d:not hard or strong: of a voice or words, gentle; of strength or eyes, weak) (e:aw ~ neu khat a ging hi) (r:11.19.12/7.16.7) (q:draft)
neukha = (t:adv) (w:a little/a bit/slightly) (d:a small amount; neukha beek with a negative means not even a little, not at all) (e:Kilamdan’na ~ beek a om kei hi) (r:45.3.22/47.11.1) (q:draft)
ngente = (t:n) (w:those who ask) (d:ngen, ask, with plural -te: the people who ask or pray; hong ngente is those who ask you) (e:A hong ~ na pia un) (b:ngen) (r:40.5.42/19.86.5) (q:draft)
ngente = (t:n) (w:nets) (d:plural of ngen, a fishing net) (e:~ a sawp uh hi) (b:ngen) (r:42.5.2/35.1.16) (q:draft)
ngia = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wolf/fox) (d:wild animal of the dog kind; the Bible uses it for the wolf that attacks sheep and also for the fox) (e:~ in tuute manin a kithehthangsak hi) (r:43.10.12/7.15.4) (q:draft)
noptuam = (t:n) (w:benefit/good/relief/advantage) (d:what makes someone better off; noptuam nading is for the good of) (e:midangte’ ~ nadingin khat leh khat) (r:50.2.4/18.30.16) (q:draft)
noptuam = (t:v) (w:get better/improve/recover) (d:become better, of a sick person or a sore) (e:Bang hunin a ~ a kipan hiam) (r:43.4.52/41.5.26) (q:draft)
nungakna = (t:n) (w:virginity) (d:nungak with -na, the state of being a virgin; nungakna lim is the sign or proof of it) (e:numei’ sungah ~ lim a kimuh kei leh) (b:nungak) (r:5.22.20/26.23.8) (q:draft)
paipa = (t:n) (w:one who comes/one who goes) (d:pai with -pa, the man who goes; hong paipa is he who comes) (e:min tawh hong ~ in thupha ngah ta hen) (b:pai) (r:41.11.9/43.6.46) (q:draft)
paipihna = (t:n) (w:bringing/leading/taking along) (d:noun from paipih; kong paipihna is my bringing you, and before a noun the place to which one is brought) (e:Note kong ~ gamah tungin) (b:paipih) (r:4.15.18/2.19.4) (q:draft)
palsatin = (t:v) (w:transgress/violate/break) (d:palsat with the linking suffix -in, breaking a law or covenant and so doing the next thing) (e:ka thukhamte ~, ka thupiaknate mang lo uh a) (b:palsat) (r:26.20.21/5.17.2) (q:draft)
panna = (t:n) (w:testimony/witness) (d:noun from pan, used in teci panna, the bearing of witness) (e:Hih thumte’ teci ~ kibang kim hi) (b:pan) (r:62.5.8/43.5.36) (q:draft)
panna = (t:n) (w:position/battle line/station) (d:noun from pan, take a stand: the place or line where fighters take their stand for battle) (e:galdona ding ~ a bawl uh hi) (b:pan) (r:14.14.10/7.20.22) (q:draft, low confidence)
paupau = (t:v) (w:keep talking/babble/talk on) (d:pau, speak, said twice: talk on and on, often with mawk or pheng, without thought) (e:Job aw, mawk ~ kei in) (r:18.15.2/20.29.20) (q:draft)
penah = (t:ppm) (d:pen, marking the highest degree, with the place marker ah: at or in the most, as in a tawpna penah, last of all, and lei hoihna penah, in the best of the land) (e:inn sung tawngnung ~ kherubte koih hi) (b:pen) (r:11.6.27/46.15.8) (q:draft)
phawkkha = (t:v) (w:notice/be aware of/consider/remember) (d:phawk with kha: have something come to mind, take notice of it) (e:kuamah in amah ~ nawn lo hi) (r:18.18.17/42.6.41) (q:draft)
phe = (t:n) (w:fin) (d:the fin of a fish; phe leh lip is fins and scales) (e:~ leh lip a nei lo peuhmah) (r:5.14.10/3.11.12) (q:draft)
phe = (t:v) (w:wave/flutter/flash) (d:move quickly to and fro, said of flowing hair, flashing swords and swarming people; followed by words such as velvel, zaizai and zalzal) (e:namsau ~ zalzal) (r:34.3.3/22.4.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
phelkhia = (t:v) (w:tear down/break down/pull apart) (d:phel with khia, out: take a building or wall apart) (e:a paktat pawlte’ innte ~ hi) (b:phel) (r:12.23.7/33.5.11) (q:draft)
pom = (t:v) (w:embrace/hold fast/clasp) (d:take or hold in the arms; also hold on to a teaching) (e:nangma thuhilhnate ka ~ hi) (r:19.119.31/1.33.4) (q:draft)
puankhai = (t:n) (w:curtain/hanging) (d:cloth that is hung up, as at the entrance of the tent of meeting) (e:kikhopna buk kongkhak ~) (r:4.3.25/2.35.17) (q:draft)
puankhai = (t:n) (w:sail) (d:the cloth hung on a ship; puankhai khuam is a mast) (e:na ~ khuam dingin Lebanon-a taamtaak singte) (r:26.27.5/26.27.7) (q:draft)
puteek = (t:n) (w:old man/aged man/elder) (d:a man of great age) (e:Kei ~ ka hi hi) (r:42.1.18/1.43.27) (q:draft)
