khangkhia = (t:v) (w:arise/spring up/grow out) (d:khang grow with khia, out: come up or come forth from) (e:leitang panin bangmah ~ zo lo hi) (b:khang) (r:37.1.10/27.7.17) (q:draft)
khanlawh = (t:v) (w:wake up/awake) (e:Josef zong a ~ ciangin) (r:40.1.24/19.17.15) (q:draft)
khawhsa = (t:n) (w:produce/crops/harvest) (d:khawh farm with sa, already done: what one has grown; khawhsa tawh biakna, offering of produce) (e:na ~ uh sehsawm suah sehkhat) (b:khawh) (r:5.26.12/18.31.8) (q:draft)
kheek = (t:v) (w:change/exchange) (e:na puante uh ~ un) (r:1.35.2/45.1.25) (q:draft)
kheek = (t:v) (w:spin/twist) (d:twist fibre into thread or cord) (e:Amah in khau ~-in) (r:20.31.19/40.6.28) (q:draft)
khentel = (t:v) (w:discern/distinguish/tell apart) (d:tell one thing clearly from another; khentel theihna is discernment) (e:a nuam lo ~ thei nawn ka hi hiam) (r:10.19.35/46.12.10) (q:draft)
khetphim = (t:n) (w:peg/tent peg/nail) (d:pin driven in with a hammer; puanbuk khetphim is a tent peg) (e:puanbuk ~ khat la a) (r:7.4.21/2.38.31) (q:draft)
khiasak = (t:v) (w:send out/drive out/let out) (d:khia out with the causative sak, placed after a verb: make someone or something go out or away, as ciah khiasak send on the way) (e:Moses in a sungpa ciah ~ a) (b:khia) (r:2.18.27/30.5.24) (q:draft)
khihin = (t:v) (w:tying/binding/fastening) (d:khih tie with in, the linking form before a following verb) (e:sumngo khau tawh ~ Babilon ah paipih uh hi) (b:khih) (r:14.33.11/1.49.11) (q:draft)
khikhe = (t:adv) (w:quietly/silently/still) (d:after a verb: om khikhe keep silent, ngak khikhe wait quietly) (e:mite pau loin a om ~) (r:30.5.13/19.4.4) (q:draft)
kholhnate = (t:n) (w:predictions/divinations/warnings) (d:kholh beforehand with na and the plural te, after a verb of speaking: things said in advance, as thugen kholhnate predictions and hilh kholhnate warnings) (e:a thugen ~ uh zong thu zuau ahi hi) (b:kholhna) (r:26.13.6/24.42.19) (q:draft)
khongkhai = (t:n) (w:astrology/sorcery/enchantment) (d:occult art; khongkhai siamte and khongkhai theite, those skilled in it, stand for the astrologers and enchanters of Babylon and Egypt) (e:leh ~ siamte a samsak hi) (r:27.2.2/27.2.10) (q:draft, low confidence, exact kind of art not clear from the verses)
khuadakin = (t:v) (w:looking/looking up/looking around) (d:khuadak look with in, the linking form before a following verb) (e:Filistiapa ~ David a muh ciangin) (b:khuadak) (r:9.17.42/9.6.13) (q:draft)
kialin = (t:v) (w:being hungry/hungering) (d:kial be hungry with in, the linking form; usually gil kialin, going hungry) (e:a tawpna-ah gil ~ sih lawh uh hi) (b:kial) (r:21.4.5/46.4.11) (q:draft)
kidem = (t:v) (w:compete/contend/vie) (d:dem with ki-, each other: strive against one another; tai kidem, run a race) (e:mite tawh tai ~ a) (b:dem) (r:24.12.5/55.2.5) (q:draft)
kigawh = (t:v) (w:be slaughtered/be sacrificed/be killed) (d:gawh slaughter with ki-, here passive: of animals killed for food or sacrifice) (e:Paisan tuuno a ~ ni) (b:gawh) (r:41.14.12/24.12.3) (q:draft)
kigin = (t:v) (w:prepare/get ready/be ready) (d:make oneself ready; kigin kholh, prepare beforehand; Kigin-ni, the Day of Preparation) (e:Judah mite ~ kholh ni nai ahih ciangin) (r:43.19.42/40.27.62) (q:draft)
kiguan = (t:v) (w:be given/be supplied/be assigned) (d:guan put, give with ki-, here passive: be provided for or laid on someone) (e:numeite tungah paknamtui tuamtuamte ~ hen) (b:guan) (r:17.2.3/13.9.27) (q:draft)
kiheina = (t:n) (w:turning/turn/conversion) (d:kihei turn with na: a turning, the place one turns to, a turn of events, or a turning to God) (e:Gentailte ~ thu a zaksak uh ciangin) (b:kihei) (r:44.15.3/9.14.47) (q:draft)
kihona = (t:n) (w:conversation/talk/talking together) (d:kiho talk together with na: the talking, or with mun the place where they talked) (e:kumpipa tawh a ~ a za sim kuamah) (b:kiho) (r:24.38.27/1.35.14) (q:draft)
kihotkhiat = (t:v) (w:be saved/be rescued/be redeemed) (d:hotkhiat save with ki-, here passive; the form used before words such as theih and ding) (e:Kote hong ~ theih nadingin na maitang) (b:hotkhiat) (r:19.80.19/42.21.28) (q:draft)
kiimnai = (t:n) (w:vicinity/surrounding area/neighbourhood) (d:the area around and near a place) (e:Minnith ~ ciang dong khuapi sawmnih) (r:7.11.33/40.14.15) (q:draft)
kikhaisukte = (t:n) (w:hangings/curtains) (d:things that are hung down, the curtains hung around the courtyard of the tabernacle) (e:ading a ~ in tong sawm-le-nga) (b:kikhaisuk) (r:2.38.14/2.38.16) (q:draft)
kikhumcip = (t:v) (w:be confined/be shut up/be shut in) (d:be kept shut in a place so that one cannot leave) (e:ni sagih sung Miriam ~ hi) (b:kikhum) (r:4.12.15/19.88.8) (q:draft)
kikup = (t:v) (w:discuss/consult/talk together) (d:talk a matter over with one another, often as thu kikup) (e:mite tawh thu a ~ khit ciangin) (r:14.20.21/42.24.15) (q:draft)
kilaktoh = (t:v) (w:be taken up/be lifted up) (d:be taken upward, used of Jesus being taken up to heaven) (e:a tunglam a ~ ni dong) (b:kilak) (r:44.1.2/42.9.51) (q:draft)
kilehngatin = (t:adv) (w:contrary/in opposition/hostilely) (d:facing against someone, used with tawh and pai: walk contrary to, be hostile toward) (e:kei tawh ~ na pai lai uh leh) (r:3.26.27/3.26.24) (q:draft)
kipiate = (t:n) (w:those given/things given) (d:people or things that are given, handed over or allotted to someone) (e:ama tungah a ~ ahi hi) (b:kipia) (r:4.3.9/6.21.40) (q:draft)
kipna = (t:n) (w:firmness/steadfastness/stability) (d:being firm and lasting; lung kipna or lungsim kipna is firmness of heart; also what builds a person up) (e:Lung ~ tawh nuntakna na ngah ding) (b:kip) (r:42.21.19/58.6.19) (q:draft)
kisatna = (t:n) (w:beating/striking/lash) (d:the act of beating or being struck; kisatna ciang is a rod for beating) (e:zavei a ~ sangin) (b:kisat) (r:20.17.10/18.9.34) (q:draft)
kisit = (t:v) (w:be tried/be examined/be tested) (d:be examined, of a case heard in court as thu kisit, or of a person tested as by fire) (e:Amah thu a ~ ciangin) (r:19.109.7/60.4.12) (q:draft)
kisuang = (t:v) (w:be set on/be placed upon) (d:be set or mounted on top of something, as gold on silver or a wreath on the head) (e:kham tang khat a ~ tawh kibang hi) (r:20.25.11/23.28.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuang = (t:v) (w:blush/feel shame) (d:feel shame or guilt; lungsim kisuang het loin is with a clear conscience) (e:~ thei beek lo uh hi) (r:24.8.12/1.20.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitanh = (t:v) (w:be redeemed/be ransomed/be bought back) (e:tua pen ~ lo ding hi) (b:tanh) (r:3.27.33/3.27.29) (q:draft)
kithuhilh = (t:v) (w:be disciplined/be corrected/be instructed) (d:receive teaching or correction; kithuhilh ding ut is to love discipline) (e:~ ding a utte pil semsem hi) (b:thuhilh) (r:20.15.32/20.12.1) (q:draft)
kituahna = (t:n) (w:meeting/meeting place/junction) (d:the meeting of persons or things, with mun the place where they meet) (e:nang tawh i ~ munah) (b:kituah) (r:4.17.4/44.27.41) (q:draft)
kivei = (t:v) (w:be waved) (d:be waved to and fro, of the part of a sacrifice presented as a wave offering) (e:a ~ sa-iik le a taklam phei) (r:4.18.18/2.29.27) (q:draft)
kivei = (t:v) (w:swing/sway/shake) (d:move to and fro; kivei suk kivei to is swing down and up) (e:leitung kipumpei-in ~ a) (r:19.18.7/18.28.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizuih = (t:v) (w:be followed/be obeyed/be kept) (d:be followed or observed, of a word, law or agreement) (e:a thuciam bawlna uh a ~ nading) (b:zuih) (r:26.17.14/27.6.8) (q:draft)
koihte = (t:n) (w:those placed/things set aside) (d:people or things that someone has put, stationed, kept or set aside) (e:kulhnei khuapite ah a ~ banah) (b:koih) (r:14.17.19/13.29.3) (q:draft)
kumpilukhu = (t:n) (w:crown) (d:royal headdress, from kumpi king and lukhu head covering) (e:A lu tungah ~ tampi a om hi) (r:66.19.12/66.3.11) (q:draft)
lahtel = (t:v) (w:show clearly/prove/demonstrate) (d:make something plain; lahtel nading is evidence or proof) (e:kilawm mi ahihna a ~ theih leh) (r:11.1.52/2.22.13) (q:draft)
laigelhna = (t:n) (w:writing/letter/what is written) (d:the act of writing or the thing written) (e:Mordekai’ ~ tawh kizui-in) (b:laigelh) (r:17.9.23/46.5.11) (q:draft)
laigelhna = (t:n) (w:writing kit/inkhorn) (d:the tool for writing carried by a scribe) (e:~ a tawi mipa in) (b:laigelh) (r:26.9.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamdung = (t:n) (w:street/roadside/along the road) (d:the length of the road, the streets where people pass) (e:~ tengah vak tawntung hi) (r:20.7.11/20.7.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamka = (t:n) (w:crossroads/fork in the road/road junction) (d:the place where roads part or meet) (e:~ lai-ah na ding kei ding hi) (r:31.1.14/26.21.21) (q:draft)
langpanna = (t:n) (w:opposition/rebellion/protest) (d:the act of standing against someone) (e:Paul in ~ tawh ama puan singkhia-in) (b:langpan) (r:44.18.6/24.33.8) (q:draft)
leenggahzute = (t:n) (w:wines/wine) (d:plural form of leenggahzu, used when wine is listed with other produce) (e:an leh ~ ka pia nawn kei ding) (b:leenggahzu) (r:28.2.9/14.2.15) (q:draft)
leikang = (t:n) (w:lime/whitewash) (d:white lime made by burning limestone, used to plaster and whiten walls) (e:~ tui tawh a kizut kaang bangin) (r:26.22.28/23.33.12) (q:draft)
leisa = (t:adj) (w:bought/purchased) (d:that someone has bought, from the verb lei buy with sa marking a finished action) (e:Abraham in a ~ han sungah) (r:44.7.16/3.27.22) (q:draft)
letsongin = (t:adv) (w:as a gift/as an offering) (d:letsong, gift, with the ending in: given or sent as a gift) (e:Assiria kumpipa tungah ~ a puak hi) (b:letsong) (r:12.16.8/4.18.7) (q:draft)
lianpipite = (t:adj) (w:very great/huge) (d:plural form of lianpipi, said of several very large things; inn lianpipite, great houses, stands for palaces and fortresses) (e:a inn ~ uh luh gawp ding uh hi) (b:lianpipi) (r:30.3.11/19.71.20) (q:draft)
liingsak = (t:v) (w:shake/make tremble) (d:cause to shake or quake) (e:Pasian in mualte ~ a) (b:liing) (r:18.9.5/19.60.2) (q:draft)
linna = (t:n) (w:trembling/shaking) (d:trembling from fear, often paired as launa le linna, fear and trembling) (e:launa le ~ kei tungah hong tung a) (b:lin) (r:18.4.14/19.55.5) (q:draft)
lipkhap = (t:v) (w:be horrified/shudder at/dread) (d:feel horror at something; mite’ lipkhap ding is an object of horror to people, lipkhap huai is dreadful) (e:~ huai-in a thupi mahmah hi) (r:27.7.7/24.48.39) (q:draft)
lokgawp = (t:v) (w:shake violently/shake) (d:lok, shake, with gawp marking a thorough or violent action) (e:Amah in leitung ~ a) (b:lok) (r:18.9.6/37.2.6) (q:draft)
luak = (t:n) (w:vomit) (d:what has been vomited) (e:Ui in a ~ a zuat kik bangin) (b:lua) (r:20.26.11/61.2.22) (q:draft)
luak = (t:v) (w:scoop out/empty out/remove) (d:take out loose matter such as ashes, used with khia) (e:a vutte ~ khia ding uh a) (r:4.4.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
luhgawp = (t:v) (w:plunder/pillage/raid) (d:luh, raid, with gawp marking a thorough or violent action) (e:amau’ teen’na inn ~ kei in) (b:luh) (r:20.24.15/24.50.11) (q:draft)
lumlum = (t:v) (w:keep sleeping/lie around/keep lying down) (d:doubled form of lum, lie down, for an action that goes on and on) (e:Mi thadahte inn-ah ~ a) (r:20.22.13/20.6.9) (q:draft)
lungka = (t:v) (w:hesitate/waver/falter) (d:be of two minds, be unsteady in heart; lungka loin is without wavering) (e:~ loin Topa muang ka hih manin) (r:19.26.1/1.19.16) (q:draft)
lungngaih = (t:v) (w:meditate/ponder/reflect) (d:think deeply about something; lungngaih kik is come to one’s senses) (e:Ka ~ ciangin ka lung so semsem hi) (b:lungngai) (r:19.39.3/42.15.17) (q:draft)
lungngaih = (t:n) (w:thought/intention) (d:what a person thinks or plans in the heart) (e:Ama ~ hoih lo pen ama lu tungah) (b:lungngai) (r:19.7.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
lutangin = (t:adv) (w:as head/as leader/as chief) (d:lutang, head, with the ending in: in the position of head over others) (e:note’ ~ amaute ka koih ding hi) (b:lutang) (r:5.1.13/10.22.44) (q:draft)
maiah = (t:prep) (w:before/in front of/in the presence of) (d:mai, face, with the place ending ah) (e:tua gam mite’ ~ kun hi) (b:mai) (r:1.23.12/40.27.53) (q:draft)
maimom = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:spider) (d:maimom khau is a spider’s thread or web, maimom bu a spider’s nest or web) (e:ama ki-upna ~ bu bang hi lel hi) (r:18.8.14/23.59.5) (q:draft)
maingatin = (t:adv) (w:facing/with the face toward) (d:with the face turned toward something; lei maingatin is face to the ground) (e:lei ~ puksuk uh hi) (b:maingat) (r:3.9.24/14.18.34) (q:draft)
mangthangsak = (t:v) (w:lose/destroy/make vanish) (d:cause to be lost or to perish) (e:ama nuntakna ~ leh) (b:mangthang) (r:41.8.36/63.1.8) (q:draft)
matsak = (t:v) (w:have arrested/cause to be captured/seize from) (d:mat, seize, with sak: have someone seized, or seize what belongs to another) (e:Johan a ~ khit ciangin) (b:mat) (r:40.14.3/18.24.3) (q:draft)
matte = (t:n) (w:captives/those seized/things seized) (d:people or things that were captured; gal matte are captives taken in war) (e:A gal ~ uh tam mahmah a) (b:mat) (r:35.1.9/27.1.2) (q:draft)
melhoihna = (t:n) (w:beauty/good looks) (e:Na ~ hangin kumpipa in hong deih ding hi) (b:melhoih) (r:19.45.11/20.6.25) (q:draft)
mette = (t:n) (w:shearers) (d:those who shear or shave, used after mul, hair or wool: tuumul mette, sheepshearers) (e:tuumul ~ khawm a) (b:met) (r:10.13.23/9.25.11) (q:draft)
misuamte = (t:n) (w:robbers/bandits/rebels) (d:plural form of misuam, men who attack and rob) (e:gutate leh ~ a hong pai a) (b:misuam) (r:31.1.5/42.10.36) (q:draft)
mithagolte = (t:n) (w:giants) (d:big and strong people; in the Bible the race of giants, where English has Rapha and Rephaites) (e:~ sung pana hong piang ahi uh hi) (r:13.20.8/13.20.4) (q:draft)
muatna = (t:n) (w:decay/corruption/rot) (d:the rotting of a body, also ruin as the result of sin) (e:~ a thuak kei hi) (b:muat) (r:44.13.37/48.6.8) (q:draft)
mulkiatna = (t:n) (w:razor) (d:tool for shaving hair, from mul hair and kiat shave) (e:ama lu-ah ~ kitah lo ding hi) (r:9.1.11/19.52.2) (q:draft)
mundang = (t:n) (w:another place/other place/elsewhere) (d:mun, place, with dang, other) (e:Tua nung ciangin ~ ah ka pai ciangin) (r:46.16.6/19.87.2) (q:draft)
natnate = (t:n) (w:diseases/pains/sicknesses) (d:plural form of natna; lungsim natnate are pains of the heart) (e:Ka lungsim ~ hong damsak in la) (b:natna) (r:19.25.17/5.28.60) (q:draft)
nawksak = (t:v) (w:let pass through/allow to cross) (d:nawk, pass through, with sak: permit someone to go through a land) (e:na gam sung hong ~ in) (b:nawk) (r:7.11.17/5.2.27) (q:draft)
nawtin = (t:adv) (w:onward/forward/pressing on) (d:nawt, push on, with the linking ending in; mai nawtin pai is go forward) (e:Israel mite mai lam ~ pai uh hi) (b:nawt) (r:2.40.36/6.6.7) (q:draft)
neek = (t:v) (w:eat) (d:form of ne, eat, used before ding, theih and nading; neek ding is something to eat, food) (e:~ ding, puansilh ding a om zah tawh) (r:54.6.8/45.14.2) (q:draft)
neihte = (t:n) (w:possessions/what one has/things had) (d:the things someone has, of goods and also of plans or disputes; thu neihte are cases people have) (e:nang’ ~ nangma adingin kem in) (b:neih) (r:1.33.9/24.29.11) (q:draft)
neihtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to have/can have) (d:neih, have, with theih, be able; often followed by nading, so that one may have) (e:Sarah a ta ~ ding hun beikhin napi-in) (b:neih) (r:58.11.11/47.9.8) (q:draft)
neksak = (t:v) (w:eat up/devour) (d:eat what belongs to someone else, to that person’s loss) (e:na tate uh hong ~ ding) (b:nek) (r:3.26.22/20.23.6) (q:draft)
neksak = (t:v) (w:let eat/let drink/serve) (d:allow or cause someone to eat or drink) (e:amau’ duh zahzah bek a ~ nading uh) (b:nek) (r:17.1.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngahzo = (t:v) (w:be able to get/obtain/attain) (d:ngah, get, with zo, be able or succeed) (e:a deih khempeuh ~ hi) (b:ngah) (r:20.13.4/42.18.26) (q:draft)
ngaknate = (t:n) (w:rests/stands/supports) (d:things on which something rests; ban ngaknate are armrests, the ngaknate of a basin its stand) (e:ban ~ pangah humpinelkai nih ding a) (b:ngakna) (r:11.10.19/3.8.11) (q:draft)
ngaknate = (t:n) (w:waiting/perseverance) (d:plural form of ngakna, the times one waits patiently) (e:lungduai takin a ~ uh) (b:ngakna) (r:46.13.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
ngamna = (t:n) (w:boldness/daring/courage) (d:being bold enough to do something, placed after the verb: gen ngamna, daring to speak) (e:thutang gen ~ lungsim ka nei hi) (b:ngam) (r:33.3.8/1.18.27) (q:draft)
ngo = (t:adj) (w:white/bright white) (d:white or bright in colour, of snow, wool, cloth, skin or cloud) (e:vuk paak bangin ahi zongin a ~ hi) (r:66.1.14/40.17.2) (q:draft)
niamkhiatin = (t:v) (w:humbling/bringing low) (d:niamkhiat, humble or bring low, with the linking ending in, joining it to the next verb) (e:amah in note hong ~ hong gilkial sak a) (b:niamkhiat) (r:5.8.3/5.8.16) (q:draft)
nungzang = (t:n) (w:back) (d:the back of the body) (e:ka ~ kuikeek uh a) (r:19.129.3/20.10.13) (q:draft)
omcip = (t:v) (w:remain/stay still/keep silent) (d:om, be, with cip, firmly: stay as one is without moving, answering or changing) (e:Jesuh pau loin a ~ hi) (b:om) (r:41.14.61/42.14.4) (q:draft)
omom = (t:v) (w:keep on being/still remain/go on) (d:doubled form of om, be, for a state that continues, often followed by lai, still) (e:a nu sung mahah ~ lai hi) (r:28.13.13/19.94.3) (q:draft)
opa = (t:todo) (q:draft, not a word of its own, the rest of Topa where the 1932 text prints T opa with a space)
paipel = (t:n) (w:basket) (d:large carrying basket) (e:~ sawm le nih a dim hi) (r:40.14.20/41.8.8) (q:draft)
papite = (t:n) (w:grown men/older men/married men) (d:plural form of papi, a grown or married man; set beside nupite, married women, and beside tangvalte, young men, where English has old men) (e:tangvalte leh ~ zong a nuam ding uh hi) (b:papi) (r:24.31.13/24.6.11) (q:draft)
pauban = (t:n) (w:blemish/defect/fault) (d:a flaw in body or character, mostly in the form pauban’na and with a negative: without blemish, blameless) (e:ama tungah ~’na om lo hi) (r:10.14.25/20.28.6) (q:draft)
peka = (t:adv) (w:far away/far off/long ago) (d:pek, far, with the ending a: far in place as gam peka, or far in time as tanglai peka, long ago) (e:Tua gam in tanglai ~ a om sa) (b:pek) (r:24.5.15/26.38.6) (q:draft)
penpa = (t:part) (d:pen marks the highest degree and pa a man: placed after a describing word it names the man who is most so, as masa penpa the first one, lian penpa the greatest one) (e:ci-in a masa ~ a dong hi) (r:42.16.5/23.20.1) (q:draft)
phelkhat = (t:n) (w:half/one half) (d:one of two parts of a whole, from phel part and khat one) (e:ka kumpi gam ~ ciang dong nangawn) (r:17.5.6/16.3.9) (q:draft)
pholak = (t:v) (w:expose/reveal/uncover) (d:bring something hidden, such as sin, into the open) (e:na gamtatnate ka ~ ding a) (r:23.57.12/18.20.27) (q:draft)
phuahtawm = (t:v) (w:make up/invent/fabricate) (d:make something up out of one’s own head; thu phuahtawm or tangthu phuahtawm is a made-up story) (e:tangthu ~ peuh ngaihsutpi-in nei ding uh hi) (r:55.4.4/16.6.8) (q:draft)
phuan = (t:v) (w:foam/bubble/sparkle) (d:of water or wine, rise in foam or bubbles) (e:tui lianpite ~ zuazua hi) (r:35.3.15/19.75.8) (q:draft)
phuan = (t:v) (w:set up/proclaim/declare) (d:set up or announce publicly, here of a people setting up their own king) (e:amau’ kumpi tuam ~ uh hi) (r:14.21.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
phunna = (t:n) (w:grumbling/complaint/murmuring) (e:Israel mite’ ~ ka za khin hi) (b:phun) (r:4.14.27/18.7.13) (q:draft)
piakkhong = (t:n) (w:gift/free gift) (d:something given freely; also placed before letsong or na: a freely given gift or thing) (e:Pasian’ ~ na pen sum tawh lei) (r:44.8.20/47.9.15) (q:draft)
piathei = (t:v) (w:be able to give/can give) (d:pia, give, with thei, be able) (e:lametna a hong ~ Pasian in) (b:pia) (r:45.15.13/43.6.52) (q:draft)
piathuah = (t:v) (w:give in addition/give more/give also) (d:pia, give, with thuah, add: give on top of what was given) (e:tul sawm a nei pa tungah ~ un) (r:40.25.28/20.3.16) (q:draft)
piazaw = (t:v) (w:give rather/give more) (d:pia, give, with zaw, more or rather: give to one instead of, or more than, another) (e:midang khatpeuh ~ in) (b:pia) (r:27.5.17/1.48.22) (q:draft)
pihte = (t:n) (w:companions/fellows) (d:pih with plural -te: those who do something together with someone; follows a verb or noun, as kipawl pihte, allies or friends, and innkuan pihte, fellow citizens) (e:Ka kipawl ~ ka sapsap hangin) (b:pih) (r:25.1.19/24.29.16) (q:draft)
pilvang = (t:v) (w:be alert/keep watch/be sober) (d:stay watchful and ready) (e:khua phawkin ~ ni) (r:52.5.6/41.13.33) (q:draft)
pona = (t:n) (w:growing place/growth) (d:noun of po, sprout or grow; with mun, the place where a plant grows, as lingkung pona mun, a place overgrown with thorn bushes) (e:lingkung ~ mun tawh kibang ding a) (b:po) (r:23.17.9/26.31.4) (q:draft)
puate = (t:n) (w:bearers/carriers) (d:pua, carry, with plural -te: those who carry what is named before it) (e:si ~ zong a khawlpah uh hi) (b:pua) (r:42.7.14/10.6.13) (q:draft)
sakhituihup = (t:n) (w:rainbow) (e:meii sungah ~ a kimuh leh) (r:1.9.14/1.9.13) (q:draft)
sangsakin = (t:v) (w:raising/lifting up) (d:sangsak, make high, with the linking ending -in; aw sangsakin is raising the voice, lu sangsakin is lifting the head to look up) (e:ka aw ~ ka kiko phetin) (b:sangsak) (r:1.39.18/1.24.64) (q:draft)
satlum = (t:v) (w:strike down/kill/cut down) (d:strike a person so that he falls dead) (e:namsau tawh amah ~ uh hi) (r:14.32.21/41.14.27) (q:draft)
sawlte = (t:n) (w:senders) (d:sawl, send, with plural -te: those who send someone, as amah a sawlte, those who send him) (e:Amah a ~ tungah a citak kamtaipa) (b:sawl) (r:20.25.13/20.22.21) (q:draft)
sawlte = (t:n) (w:commands/orders) (d:the things someone commands, as Topa hong sawlte, what the Lord requires) (e:hong ~ na hih ding uh hi) (b:sawl) (r:3.8.35) (q:draft, low confidence)
sawlte = (t:n) (w:messengers/men sent) (d:the people who were sent, as a mi sawlte, the men he sent) (e:A mi ~ hong tun’ ciangin) (b:sawl) (r:9.19.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
selkeu = (t:n) (w:dry branch/brushwood/dry twigs) (d:dry branches or twigs used as firewood) (e:~ kikhul khu tawh kibang hi) (r:18.41.20/7.9.49) (q:draft)
semnen = (t:v) (w:cut into pieces/chop up/hack to pieces) (e:a vun hawk-in ~ ding hi) (r:3.1.6/9.15.33) (q:draft)
siamnate = (t:n) (w:skills/abilities/gifts/arts) (d:plural of siamna; with Kha Siangtho, gifts of the Spirit; with mitphial or aisan, magic arts) (e:ngaihsut ~ tawh gualzawhna kingah hi) (b:siamna) (r:20.24.6/46.14.12) (q:draft)
siangin = (t:adv) (w:clean/cleanly/clearly) (d:siang, clean, with the ending -in; after a verb it gives the result, as kiphiat siangin, swept clean, and hah siangin, clearing away) (e:hoihtakin kiphiat ~ a hoih linlianin) (b:siang) (r:42.11.25/6.17.18) (q:draft)
sikha = (t:n) (w:ghost/spirit of a dead person) (e:amaute in ~ sa uh a) (r:42.24.37/41.6.49) (q:draft)
silhsakin = (t:v) (w:clothing/dressing/putting on) (d:silhsak, put clothing on someone, with the linking ending -in) (e:puan siangthote Aaron ~) (b:silhsak) (r:2.40.13/3.8.7) (q:draft)
simto = (t:v) (w:count off/count up/reckon) (d:count upward one after another; of a family line, reckon back through the forefathers) (e:Nipi kal sagih na ~ ding uh hi) (b:sim) (r:5.16.9/13.6.39) (q:draft)
sucip = (t:v) (w:crush/oppress/press down) (e:Pasian in kei hong ~ hen la) (b:su) (r:18.6.9/19.73.8) (q:draft)
sungtum = (t:v) (w:come in/go in/enter) (d:go inside, the opposite of pusuah or paikhiat, go out) (e:Na ~ ciangun hamsia na ngah ding) (r:5.28.19/12.11.8) (q:draft)
taanglai = (t:adj) (w:ancient/of old) (d:placed before a noun: of long ago) (e:~ mualte tunga piang a hoihpente) (r:5.33.15/20.23.10) (q:draft)
taanglai = (t:n) (w:ancient times/long ago) (d:the far past, as taanglai pek panin, from long ago) (e:~ pek panin na tokhom a kipsa) (r:19.93.2) (q:draft)
taltangah = (t:adv) (w:on the forehead) (d:taltang, forehead, with the place marker ah) (e:a ~ ciamtehna a nei peuhmah) (b:taltang) (r:26.9.6/66.9.4) (q:draft)
tamasak = (t:v) (w:fail/forsake/abandon) (d:fail someone by leaving him without help; in the verses always negated) (e:nang kong ~ kei ding a) (r:6.1.5/5.4.31) (q:draft)
tamasak = (t:v) (w:run out/run dry) (d:of a supply such as oil, come to an end) (e:um sunga sathau in zong ~ lo hi) (r:11.17.16/11.17.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangdingin = (t:prep) (w:in place of/instead of/for/on behalf of) (d:placed after the person or thing that is replaced or represented) (e:tuute ~ ka nuntakna ka paai hi) (b:tangding) (r:43.10.15/4.8.18) (q:draft)
tatsiatna = (t:n) (w:evil deed/crime/wickedness) (d:noun of tatsiat: a wicked or destructive act; in 2 Samuel 24:16 the destruction itself) (e:ama ~ in puksak a) (r:20.14.32/24.41.11) (q:draft)
tawldam = (t:v) (w:rest/be refreshed/be at ease) (d:be relieved of tiredness or worry; with sak, refresh someone) (e:a gim mite ka ~ sak ding a) (r:24.31.25/18.3.26) (q:draft)
tawngnung = (t:n) (w:innermost part/inner part/far end) (d:the part furthest in, of a house, prison or cave; often followed by sungah) (e:thong ~ sungah khumin) (r:44.16.24/9.24.3) (q:draft)
tawsak = (t:v) (w:blind/make blind) (d:taw, blind, with the causative sak; used with mit, eye) (e:sumgolh in uliante mit ~ a) (b:taw) (r:2.23.8/1.19.11) (q:draft)
teelkhiat = (t:v) (w:choose/choose out/select) (d:form of teelkhia used before a noun or in a dependent clause, as a teelkhiat mite, the people he chose) (e:a ~ khuapi Jerusalem ah) (b:teelkhia) (r:11.14.21/60.1.2) (q:draft)
tehlop = (t:n) (w:trap/snare) (e:kei hong siahna-in ~ koihsim uh a) (r:19.140.5/19.69.22) (q:draft)
tektek = (t:adv) (w:more and more/steadily/step by step) (d:placed after a verb or describing word: the state increases or continues by degrees) (e:nungzui mite a tam ~ uh a) (r:44.6.1/26.42.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
tektek = (t:adv) (w:very/own) (d:emphasises the word before it: the very one, one's own, as keima mit tektek tawh, with my own eyes) (e:Keima mit ~ tawh amah ka mu ding a) (r:18.19.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
thakhatthu = (t:adv) (w:suddenly/all at once/by surprise) (d:written with the ending -in, thakhatthu-in) (e:Joshua in ~-in amaute simgawp hi) (r:6.10.9/18.22.10) (q:draft)
thehthangna = (t:n) (w:scattering/dispersion) (d:noun of thehthang, scatter; before gam or with panin it names the place to which people were scattered, as note kong thehthangna gamte, the lands where I scattered you) (e:Amaute ka ~ gam panin khawm kikin) (b:thehthang) (r:26.11.17/24.46.28) (q:draft)
theikhol = (t:v) (w:know beforehand/know in advance/foreknow) (d:thei, know, with khol, ahead of time) (e:inn neipa in ~ leh) (r:40.24.43/43.13.11) (q:draft)
thuhilhpa = (t:n) (w:teacher/preacher/overseer) (d:thuhilh, teach, with -pa for a man: the man who teaches or corrects; in 1 Timothy 3:1 the office of overseer) (e:adingin a pil ~ in) (b:thuhilh) (r:20.25.12/54.3.1) (q:draft)
thukhual = (t:v) (w:have regard/be considerate/show mercy) (d:care about what is right and about other people; in the verses only negated, thukhual lo, ruthless) (e:~ lo mite’ la sakna kitawpsak hi) (r:23.25.5/23.25.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
thuneu = (t:n) (w:small matter/trifle/easy thing) (d:thu, matter, with neu, small: something of little weight or difficulty) (e:Topa muhna ah a ~ khat ahi hi) (r:12.3.18/9.18.23) (q:draft)
thutelna = (t:n) (w:understanding/discernment/insight) (e:ngaihsut pilna leh ~ nang tungah) (r:13.22.12/20.2.11) (q:draft)
thuthak = (t:n) (w:news/new message/new thing) (d:thu, word or matter, with thak, new; thuthak hoih is good news) (e:~ hoih khat note a’ ding) (r:42.2.10/12.7.9) (q:draft)
top = (t:v) (w:pick up/gather/glean) (d:pick up things left lying; of grain, glean; van top is taking plunder) (e:ama ~ dingin nusia un la) (r:8.2.16/34.3.1) (q:draft)
tuahkhak = (t:v) (w:meet/encounter/come upon/fall into) (d:happen to meet a person or meet with an event; a tuahkhak peuh is whoever one happens to meet) (e:Ze-etna na ~ loh nadingun thu ngen un) (r:42.22.40/20.17.12) (q:draft)
tuasan = (t:adv) (w:there/in that place) (d:used in tuasan takah, in that very place) (e:~ takah a om hi) (b:tua) (r:43.10.40/43.5.5) (q:draft)
tukin = (t:v) (w:falling/falling down) (d:tuk, fall, with the linking ending -in; after another verb, as sat tukin, striking down) (e:amaute ~ kitamzan gawp ding uh hi) (b:tuk) (r:23.8.15/10.2.23) (q:draft)
uum = (t:v) (w:surround/encircle/crowd around) (d:be all around a person or place; ki-uum is walled, enclosed) (e:mi tampite in amaute ~ uh a) (r:41.9.14/58.11.30) (q:draft)
vakna = (t:n) (w:feeding/provision/relief) (d:giving of food or support; misiangthote vakna is the service of supplying the saints, an vakna a feast) (e:Misiangthote’ ~ thu note kiangah kong gelh) (r:47.9.1/42.12.36) (q:draft, low confidence)
vakna = (t:n) (w:light/lighting) (d:noun of vak, give light; mei vakna is giving light by a lamp) (e:Mei ~ meivak khuam pen) (b:vak) (r:4.4.9) (q:draft)
vanvan = (t:adv) (d:placed after a verb for hurried, restless or rushing movement: rushing, pounding) (e:Ka lungtang kisai ~ a) (r:24.4.19/20.1.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
vanvan = (t:v) (w:stretch out/spread out) (d:doubled form of van, stretch out the hands, again and again) (e:amaute in a khut uh ~ ding uh a) (r:23.25.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
vatgawpin = (t:v) (w:striking down/attacking/defeating) (d:vatgawp, strike down, with the linking ending -in) (e:la-in amaute ~ that hi) (b:vatgawp) (r:6.11.17/6.15.16) (q:draft)
vilna = (t:n) (w:watch/vigil/guard duty) (d:noun of vil, watch over: keeping watch; with mun, the place of watching) (e:amaute tungah ~ nasep leh zingsang simin) (b:vil) (r:13.9.27/23.21.8) (q:draft)
zahpihna = (t:n) (w:mockery/ridicule/reproach/taunt) (e:simmawhna leh ~ ka thuak lawh hi) (b:zahpih) (r:24.20.8/16.2.19) (q:draft)
zaneite = (t:n) (w:officials/officers) (d:za nei, hold a rank or title, with plural -te: those who hold office) (e:khuapi sung ~ khawmin) (r:14.29.20/12.24.15) (q:draft)
zawngin = (t:v) (w:being poor/becoming poor) (d:zawng, poor, with the linking ending -in: being or becoming poor and so) (e:sanggampa ~ a neihsa leitang khenkhat a zuak leh) (b:zawng) (r:3.25.25/3.14.21) (q:draft)
zazo = (t:v) (w:have heard/heard) (d:za, hear, with zo, which marks the action as done or achieved) (e:Israel mite’ thumna ka ~ a) (b:za) (r:2.6.5/23.37.11) (q:draft)
zen = (t:part) (d:emphatic word after a verb: even, really, to such a degree) (e:na lampi na hilh ~ hi) (r:24.2.33/24.2.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
ziin = (t:n) (w:earthquake/earth tremor) (d:used with liing, shake: ziin liing, the earth quakes) (e:~ hong liing ding hi) (r:40.24.7/42.21.11) (q:draft)
zineipa = (t:n) (w:bridegroom) (d:zi nei, take a wife, with -pa for a man) (e:~ a kipaikhiatpih hun hong tung ding) (b:zinei) (r:42.5.35/40.25.5) (q:draft)
