Shimea = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Shimea) (r:13.2.13/13.20.7) (q:draft)
Si = (t:adj) (w:dead) (d:si, die, written with a capital in the name Si Tuipi, the Dead Sea) (e:nisuahna lama om ~ Tuipi ah luang ding a) (b:si) (r:38.14.8/26.47.8) (q:draft)
Sin = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Sin) (d:desert on the way from Egypt to Sinai, Sin gamlak, the Desert of Sin) (e:~ gam lakah giahphual sat uh hi) (r:4.33.11/2.17.1) (q:draft)
Sin = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Sinites) (d:in Sin mite, the Sinites, a people descended from Canaan) (e:Hiv mite, Arki mite, ~ mite) (r:1.10.17/13.1.15) (q:draft)
Tui = (t:n) (w:water) (d:tui written with a capital in the name Tui Kongpi, the Water Gate of Jerusalem) (e:nisuahna lam manawhin ~ Kongpi dongah pai uh hi) (b:tui) (r:16.12.37/16.8.3) (q:draft)
Tulak = (t:n) (w:forest/woods) (d:tulak written with a capital in the name Lebanon Tulak Inn, the Palace of the Forest of Lebanon) (e:Lebanon ~ Inn sungah tuate koih hi) (b:tulak) (r:11.10.17/23.22.8) (q:draft)
Ur = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Ur) (d:city of the Chaldeans from which Abram came) (e:Khaldea gam ~ khua panin) (r:1.15.7/1.11.28) (q:draft)
Ur = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ur) (d:father of Eliphal, one of David's warriors) (r:13.11.35) (q:draft)
akipanin = (t:prep) (w:from/since/beginning with) (d:a kipanin written as one word; follows the time or thing that is the starting point) (e:tua hun ~ naupang a dam hi) (b:akipan) (r:40.17.18/43.9.32) (q:draft)
apha = (t:adj) (w:good) (d:a pha written as one word; also stands alone as that which is good) (e:thuman leh ~ lungsim tawh thu) (b:pha) (r:42.8.15/42.14.34) (q:draft)
arah = (t:todo) (q:draft, lowercase only as the second part of the hyphenated woman's name Na-arah, Naarah; the capitalised Arah is a man's name; a lowercase keyword cannot take type name)
arba = (t:todo) (q:draft, lowercase only as the second part of the hyphenated place name Kiriath-arba, Kiriath Arba; the capitalised Arba is a man's name; a lowercase keyword cannot take type name)
asia = (t:adj) (w:evil/bad/wrong) (d:a sia written as one word: that which is bad; asia-a gamta is to act wickedly) (e:~ gamtatna in khialhna lianpi ahi hi) (b:sia) (r:20.14.22/20.11.19) (q:draft)
atin = (t:v) (w:reaping/cutting) (d:at, reap or cut, with the linking ending -in; in ki-atin, being cut or circumcised) (e:kum thumna ciangin khai tuhin ~) (b:at) (r:12.19.29/40.6.26) (q:draft)
atkhia = (t:v) (w:cut off/cut away) (d:at, cut, with khia, out or off) (e:a selte ~ ding a) (b:at) (r:23.18.5/19.12.3) (q:draft)
atsak = (t:v) (w:circumcise/have cut) (d:at cut with sak; with vun skin it is the expression for circumcise) (e:ama vun a ~ hi) (b:at) (r:44.16.3/1.17.23) (q:draft)
attan = (t:v) (w:cut off/sever) (d:cut through so that a part comes off, as thumbs, a tail or a tongue; ngawng attan is break or cut the neck) (e:a khepite ~ uh hi) (r:7.1.6/5.21.4) (q:draft)
baihzaw = (t:adj) (w:easier/more bearable) (d:baih easy with zaw more) (e:kalaoh khat a lut ding ~ lai hi) (b:baih) (r:41.10.25/40.11.22) (q:draft)
balkeekin = (t:v) (w:tear/rend) (d:balkeek with the linking suffix in; in the verses of tearing one's clothes in grief) (e:a puante ~ lei lakah lum hi) (b:balkeek) (r:10.13.31/1.37.34) (q:draft)
behlapin = (t:v) (w:add/add to) (d:behlap with the linking suffix in) (e:hih mawhna ~, Johan thong sungah) (b:behlap) (r:42.3.20/3.22.14) (q:draft)
bengin = (t:v) (w:clap/slap) (d:beng with the linking suffix in: strike with the open hand, khut beng clap the hands, paang beng slap the cheek) (e:Mikaiah a paang ~) (b:beng) (r:11.22.24/12.11.12) (q:draft)
biingta = (t:n) (w:log) (d:a small measure of oil, used for the Hebrew measure log in Leviticus 14) (e:sathau ~ khat la ding hi) (r:3.14.10/3.14.15) (q:draft)
bilngongte = (t:n) (w:the deaf/deaf people) (e:~ in laibu sunga thute za ding a) (b:bilngong) (r:23.29.18/23.42.18) (q:draft)
buai = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be in turmoil/riot) (d:be disturbed or confused, of a person's mind or of a crowd or city) (e:Susa khuapi sung ~ mahmah hi) (r:17.3.15/41.14.2) (q:draft)
buai = (t:v) (w:contend with/be occupied with) (d:with tawh, be taken up or entangled with someone) (e:tawh ~ paisuak lo ding hi) (r:1.6.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
buhvui = (t:n) (w:head of grain/ear of grain) (e:a nungzuite in ~ zut uh a) (r:42.6.1/1.41.5) (q:draft)
ciamin = (t:v) (w:swear/promise/vow) (d:ciam with the linking suffix in) (e:kiciamna khat tawh kam ~) (b:ciam) (r:4.30.10/58.7.21) (q:draft)
ciamin = (t:v) (w:taste) (d:ciam taste with the linking suffix in) (e:vantung hehpihna ~, Kha Siangtho tawh) (b:ciam) (r:58.6.4) (q:draft)
ciamnuih = (t:n) (w:mockery/ridicule/jest) (d:ciamnuih bawl is mock or make fun of someone, ciamnuih-a neih is treat as a laughing stock) (e:kei nong ~ bawl uh hi) (r:18.12.5/18.30.1) (q:draft)
ciangkangte = (t:n) (w:rods/sticks/branches) (d:plural; the rods, peeled to show white, that Jacob set before the flocks; probably ciang stick with kang white) (e:mai-ah tua ~ koih lo hi) (b:ciangkang) (r:1.30.42/1.30.38) (q:draft)
ciangtan = (t:n) (w:limit/set measure/fixed extent) (d:a fixed limit, especially of time; hun ciangtan is an appointed length of time) (e:ka mong leh ka hun ~ zah) (r:19.39.4/25.5.22) (q:draft)
ciangtan = (t:v) (w:set a limit/determine/fix) (e:Nangmah in na ~ khin a) (r:18.14.5) (q:draft)
ciap = (t:v) (w:taste) (d:try the taste of food or drink) (e:Leii in an a ~ mah bangin) (r:18.12.11/43.2.9) (q:draft)
cidamte = (t:n) (w:the healthy/healthy ones) (e:a ~ zong an vak lo hi) (b:cidam) (r:38.11.16/42.5.31) (q:draft)
cimtak = (t:v) (w:be weary of/be tired of/loathe) (d:be fed up with something or someone) (e:Ka nuntakna ka ~ ta hi) (b:cim) (r:18.10.1/53.3.13) (q:draft)
cingsing = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:algumwood/almugwood/sandalwood) (d:a precious wood brought from Ophir) (e:Ofir panin ~ leh suang manpha) (r:11.10.11/14.9.10) (q:draft)
cingtakin = (t:adv) (w:fully/completely/in detail) (d:in full measure, leaving nothing out) (e:a banbanin a ~ a gen hi) (r:44.21.19/47.1.14) (q:draft)
daih = (t:v) (w:be quiet/be silent/calm down) (d:form of dai used in dependent clauses and before nouns) (e:hih mite a ~ uh leh) (b:dai) (r:42.19.40/32.1.11) (q:draft)
dangtakte = (t:n) (w:the thirsty/thirsty ones) (e:amah in a ~ phasak a) (b:dangtak) (r:19.107.9/18.22.7) (q:draft)
deihluatna = (t:n) (w:zeal/strong desire/eagerness) (d:deih want, luat too much, with na: a very strong desire for something) (e:Topa’ ~ in hih thu hong tungsak ding hi) (r:23.37.32/19.69.9) (q:draft)
dipkuat = (t:v) (w:be terrified/be struck with dread) (d:in the verses always followed by huai: dipkuat huai is awesome, terrifying) (e:a ~ huai mang ka mu hi) (r:27.4.5/24.5.30) (q:draft)
dipkuathuai = (t:adj) (w:awesome/terrifying/dreadful) (d:causing dread or awe, used of God's deeds and of disasters) (e:Amah in a ~ siatna piangsak ding a) (r:27.8.24/19.66.5) (q:draft)
doin = (t:v) (w:fight/attack) (d:do with the linking suffix in) (e:David in amah ~ zo hi) (b:do) (r:13.18.3/12.17.3) (q:draft)
duhna = (t:n) (w:appetite/craving/hunger/thirst) (d:desire for food or drink) (e:~ in mi na semsak a) (b:duh) (r:20.16.26/30.8.11) (q:draft)
eh = (t:intj) (d:exclamation of surprise or of correcting oneself, as between two numbers in the sayings of Proverbs 30: three, no, four) (e:thum om a, ~! li hizaw) (r:20.30.18/46.1.16) (q:draft)
emerald = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:emerald) (d:loanword from English; in Exodus the NIV has turquoise for this stone) (e:~ suang, sapfeiros suang leh diamond suang) (r:2.39.11/66.4.3) (q:draft)
gakcip = (t:v) (w:bind fast/entangle/hold fast) (d:gak tie with cip tightly) (e:thangkhau in amah ~ hi) (b:gak) (r:18.18.9/19.116.3) (q:draft)
galtaite = (t:n) (w:fugitives/refugees) (e:Efraim ~ na hi uh hi) (b:galtai) (r:7.12.4/23.21.14) (q:draft)
gamdaihna = (t:n) (w:solitary place/lonely place/desolate place) (d:quiet country where no one is; often followed by mun place) (e:~ mun a zuan dingin a pai uh hi) (r:41.6.32/25.5.18) (q:draft)
gerah = (t:n) (w:gerah) (d:small Hebrew unit of weight, twenty to a shekel) (e:~ sawmnih ciangin shekel khat hi ding hi) (r:3.27.25/26.45.12) (q:draft)
giloin = (t:adv) (w:wickedly/cruelly) (d:gilo evil with the suffix in: a giloin gamta is act wickedly; also being wicked or cruel, linked to a following description) (e:~ hehpihna lungsim nei lo uh hi) (b:gilo) (r:24.50.42/18.31.5) (q:draft)
gimin = (t:v) (w:be weary/be tired/be exhausted) (d:gim with the linking suffix in) (e:note ~ lungkhamin na om) (b:gim) (r:5.25.18/10.17.29) (q:draft)
gimpih = (t:v) (w:toil for/labour for/take trouble over) (d:gim be weary with pih: weary oneself over something or someone) (e:themkhat zong a ~ het lo mi) (b:gim) (r:21.2.21/32.4.10) (q:draft)
gitta = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:sparrow) (e:~ tampi sangin na manpha zaw uh hi) (r:40.10.31/40.10.29) (q:draft)
golhguk = (t:n) (w:bribe) (d:golhguk pia is give a bribe, golhguk la is take a bribe) (e:zum nasemte ~ pia uh hi) (r:15.4.5/19.15.5) (q:draft)
golin = (t:adj) (w:large/big/thick) (d:gol with the linking suffix in, followed by a second description) (e:tua hai ~ thuk mahmah hi) (b:gol) (r:26.23.32/26.31.5) (q:draft)
guahzuk = (t:n) (w:rain/rainfall) (d:the falling of rain; form of guahzu used before nading and before nouns) (e:Kua in ~ nading tuilam bawlsak a) (b:guahzu) (r:18.38.25/19.135.7) (q:draft)
guktakna = (t:n) (w:theft/stealing) (e:ama' ~ hangin amah kizuak ding hi) (r:2.22.1/41.7.21) (q:draft)
hangte = (t:n) (w:the brave/mighty ones/warriors) (d:plural of hang brave, strong; follows a noun as in galkap hangte brave soldiers) (e:A galkap ~ khempeuh uh thahsak un) (r:24.50.27/10.11.16) (q:draft)
hante = (t:n) (w:tombs/graves) (e:mual tunga om ~ mu hi) (b:han) (r:12.23.16/19.49.11) (q:draft)
hate = (t:n) (w:teeth) (e:amau kam sunga ~ sutan in la) (b:ha) (r:19.58.6/1.49.12) (q:draft)
henna = (t:n) (w:bond/binding) (d:hen bind with na; henna khau is a cord that binds) (e:migilote’ ~ khaute su-tat khin hi) (r:19.129.4/24.5.5) (q:draft)
henna = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:henna) (d:loanword, the henna shrub with fragrant flowers) (e:~ leh nard sing namtuite) (r:22.4.13) (q:draft)
huaite = (t:part) (d:the suffix huai, worthy of or causing a feeling, with plural te: those who are, or things that are, fearsome, trustworthy and so on; written joined to the word before or separate) (e:ka gal kihtak ~ kiang panin) (b:huai) (r:19.17.8/47.12.12) (q:draft)
hualte = (t:n) (w:waves/breakers) (d:plural; with tuipi the waves of the sea) (e:tuipi ~ sangin vanglian zaw hi) (r:19.93.4/19.107.25) (q:draft)
husia = (t:adj) (w:fierce/violent/raging/severe) (d:fierce and destroying, of fire, a weapon, a quarrel or an earthquake; follows mei fire, and is also used as a verb, grow fierce) (e:a kam panin mei ~ pusuak hi) (r:19.18.8/44.23.10) (q:draft)
