deda = (t:adv) (d:follows a word for something flat or wide, such as peek, zai or kizal, and stresses how broadly it spreads; a peek deda is the wide sheet of Acts 10, lupna zai deda a wide bed) (e:na lupna zai ~ tungah) (r:23.57.8/44.10.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
diktan'sakna = (t:n) (w:justification/being made righteous) (d:the act of declaring or making someone righteous; with ngah, receive, it means be justified) (e:upna hangin ~ i ngah nadingin) (r:48.3.24/56.3.7) (q:draft)
ekte = (t:n) (w:dung/offal) (d:ek, dung, with the plural ending -te: the dung or waste matter of an animal) (e:a vun leh a ~) (b:ek) (r:2.29.14/39.2.3) (q:draft)
ekte = (t:n) (w:splitters) (d:as the second part of sing-ekte, those who split wood: ek, split, with the plural ending -te) (e:sing-~, sing ehna mah-ah liam ding hi) (r:21.10.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
gahin = (t:n) (w:by the fruit) (d:gah, fruit, with the marker -in showing means: by its fruit) (e:a kung a ~ kithei hi) (b:gah) (r:40.12.33/40.7.20) (q:draft)
gahin = (t:v) (w:bearing fruit/yielding) (d:in gah gahin: gah used as a verb, bear, with the linking ending -in, after the noun gah, fruit) (e:Leitang in gah ~) (b:gah) (r:3.25.19/51.1.6) (q:draft)
galdalna = (t:n) (w:fortification/stronghold/defence) (d:something that keeps the enemy out; galdalna kulhpi is a fortress and galdalna inn a citadel) (e:a ~ kulhpite khempeuh balzan gawpin) (r:25.2.2/16.7.2) (q:draft)
gamhte = (t:n) (w:inheritances/inherited lands) (d:plural of gamh: the shares of land handed down in a tribe or family) (e:Israel mite’ ~ minam khat pan) (b:gamh) (r:4.36.7/6.14.2) (q:draft)
gamkhingin = (t:adv) (w:desolate/as a wasteland) (d:gamkhing, desolate place, with the ending -in: in a desolate state; with om, lie desolate, with bawl, make desolate) (e:~ a om sung teng leitang in) (b:gamkhing) (r:3.26.43/26.35.9) (q:draft)
gamtatin = (t:v) (w:acting/behaving) (d:gamtat with the linking ending -in: acting in the way named before it, as in hai gamtatin, acting foolishly) (e:kote hai ~ ka khialhna hangun) (b:gamtat) (r:4.12.11/19.14.1) (q:draft)
gamtatzia = (t:n) (w:conduct/way of acting/example/practice) (d:the manner in which someone acts; gamtatzia zui means follow the example of) (e:keima ~ hong zui ta un) (r:46.11.1/9.2.13) (q:draft)
gannote = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young animals/animals) (d:plural of ganno, the young of sheep, goats or cattle; in Proverbs 12:10 a person's own animals in general) (e:Midikte in a ~ hoihtak don a) (b:ganno) (r:20.12.10/9.15.9) (q:draft)
geelnate = (t:n) (w:plans/purposes) (d:plural of geelna: things that have been planned) (e:Na ~ khempeuh Topa ap in) (b:geelna) (r:20.16.3/23.19.3) (q:draft)
genkhin = (t:v) (w:have told/have spoken) (d:gen, tell, with khin, already or completely: the telling is finished) (e:A hun ma-in kong ~ hi) (b:gen) (r:41.13.23/23.24.3) (q:draft)
genthang = (t:v) (w:proclaim/spread abroad/publish) (d:tell something widely so that it becomes known everywhere, of good news or of slander) (e:Ashkelon kongzing ah ~ kei in) (r:10.1.20/3.25.10) (q:draft)
ginat = (t:adj) (w:sound/proper/worthy) (d:form of gina used before loh; in the verses always ginat lohna, not being sound, which covers weakness, unfaithfulness, a weak point and worthless conduct) (e:ka ~ lohna hong kilangsak nate hangin) (b:gina) (r:47.11.30/4.14.33) (q:draft, low confidence)
goin = (t:v) (w:slaughtering/killing) (d:go, slaughter an animal, with the linking ending -in before the next verb) (e:Moses in ~ a si tawmkhat la-in) (b:go) (r:3.8.23/26.34.3) (q:draft)
guallelhna = (t:n) (w:defeat) (d:the state of being beaten by an opponent) (e:na ~ uh a kilang mahmah hi) (b:guallelh) (r:46.6.7/7.20.36) (q:draft)
gulgu = (t:n) (w:snake venom/venom) (d:gul, snake, with gu, poison; gulgu nei is a venomous snake such as a viper or cobra) (e:a thugente uh ~ bang hi) (r:19.140.3/18.20.16) (q:draft)
haih = (t:v) (w:winnow/sift) (d:toss or shake grain to separate it from the chaff; also used of sifting people) (e:ancilna-ah mangbuhham ~ hi) (r:8.3.2/42.22.31) (q:draft)
haksatnate = (t:n) (w:troubles/hardships/difficulties) (d:plural of haksatna) (e:a beisa huna ~ kimangngailh khin a) (b:haksatna) (r:23.65.16/55.4.5) (q:draft)
hanginah = (t:prep) (w:because of/on account of) (d:hangin with the ending -ah, placed after a noun to give the reason; tua thu hanginah means that is why) (e:Tua thu ~ note lakah thanem) (b:hangin) (r:46.11.30/44.26.6) (q:draft)
hanginah = (t:conj) (w:although/even though) (d:after a verb: although that was done, what follows is contrary to what might be expected) (e:amah ka dot ~) (b:hangin) (r:42.23.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
hansuahna = (t:n) (w:exhortation/encouragement/urging) (d:words that stir someone up to act or to stand firm) (e:~ kam na thuak siam un) (b:hansuah) (r:58.13.22/46.14.3) (q:draft)
hehlua = (t:v) (w:be very angry/be furious/rage) (d:heh, be angry, with lua, too much: be angry beyond measure) (e:~ loin kei hong hilh in) (b:heh) (r:24.10.24/4.11.10) (q:draft)
hiathiat = (t:adv) (w:calmly/quietly/at ease) (d:follows a verb, often of speaking, to show that the action goes on in a calm, even and unhurried way) (e:mipilpa in dam taka a gen ~) (r:21.9.17/30.6.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
hihzo = (t:v) (w:be able to do/accomplish/manage) (d:hih, do, with zo, be able: succeed in doing; hihzo kei means cannot do) (e:Pasian in a ~ hi) (r:45.8.3/32.1.13) (q:draft)
hilhsak = (t:v) (w:teach/instruct/have someone teach) (d:hilh, teach, with sak: teach for the good of someone, or cause someone to be taught) (e:thukhamte amaute ~ un) (b:hilh) (r:12.17.27/7.13.8) (q:draft)
hithiatin = (t:adv) (w:quietly/at rest/peacefully/still) (d:hithiat with the ending -in, after verbs such as lum, lie, and tu, sit: staying calmly in that position) (e:a tanu nuamtakin lum ~ a om) (b:hithiat) (r:41.7.30/23.17.2) (q:draft)
hoihnono = (t:adj) (w:fine/good/excellent) (d:hoih, good, with nono, said of several things each of which is fine: puan hoihnono, fine clothes) (e:puan ~ a silhte pen kumpi inn sungah) (r:40.11.8/44.14.17) (q:draft)
huanin = (t:v) (w:cooking/boiling) (d:huan, cook food by boiling, with the linking ending -in before the next verb) (e:tui tawh ~ ahi zongin ne loin) (r:2.12.9/12.6.29) (q:draft)
huanpipa = (t:n) (w:chief baker/chief cook) (d:used as an huanpipa: the head of those who cook or bake food; -pi marks the chief and -pa a male person) (e:an piapipa leh an ~ la khia hi) (r:1.40.20/1.40.2) (q:draft)
huzo = (t:v) (w:save/preserve/rescue) (d:hu, protect or defend, with zo, be able: succeed in saving) (e:ama pilna tawh tua khua a ~ hi) (r:21.9.15/20.14.25) (q:draft)
innkhumzangah = (t:n) (w:on the roof/on the housetop/to the roof) (d:innkhumzang, the flat roof of a house, with the place ending -ah) (e:~ Peter a kahto hi) (b:innkhumzang) (r:44.10.9/10.16.22) (q:draft)
innteek = (t:n) (w:house owner/householder/master of the house) (d:the person to whom a house belongs; innteek pa is the man who owns the house, also the master for whom someone works) (e:a ~ pa kiangah) (r:42.22.11/42.14.21) (q:draft)
innvengte = (t:n) (w:neighbors) (d:plural of innveng: people who live in the houses nearby) (e:a ~’ zite mawhpih uh a) (r:24.29.23/24.9.8) (q:draft)
itluat = (t:n) (w:darling/beloved/dearly loved one) (d:it, love, with luat, very much: one who is greatly loved; a word of address in love poetry, as itluat aw) (e:hong zui in, ~ aw) (r:22.2.10/22.4.10) (q:draft)
kahin = (t:v) (w:climbing/going up/mounting) (d:kah, climb or go up, with the linking ending -in before the next verb; also of taking the throne) (e:a leeng tungah ~ Jezre-el ah pai hi) (b:kah) (r:12.9.16/35.2.1) (q:draft)
kahin = (t:v) (w:weeping/mourning) (d:kah, weep, with the linking ending -in) (e:Jesuh ~ a tamlawh numei pawlkhat) (b:kah) (r:42.23.27) (q:draft)
kalun = (t:conj) (w:while/during the time that) (d:kal, interval of time, with the ending -un, after a verb: while something is going on; a phawk loh kalun means while they are unaware, by surprise) (e:Mite ihmut ~ a galpa pai a) (r:40.13.25/16.4.11) (q:draft)
kamkhat = (t:n) (w:one word/a single word) (d:kam, word, with khat, one; kamkhat beek with a negative verb means not even one word) (e:Zeisu in ~ beek a dawng kei hi) (r:40.27.12/40.22.46) (q:draft)
kamkhat = (t:n) (w:mouthful/morsel/bite) (d:one mouthful of food, as in khomun kamkhat, a piece of bread) (e:khomun ~ a san’ khit ciangin) (r:43.13.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
kamsan = (t:v) (w:prophesy) (d:form of kamsang written with a final apostrophe before ding or the ending -na: speak a message from God; with -na it means prophecy or prophesying) (e:~’ ding na ut takpi ta un) (r:46.14.39/42.1.67) (q:draft)
kankan = (t:v) (w:search out/investigate/ponder/study) (d:kan, search or examine, doubled to show continued careful searching) (e:Thu ka ~ ciangin) (r:21.7.27/19.111.2) (q:draft)
kankan = (t:adv) (d:follows liing, tremble, to picture continued shaking: liing kankan, trembling all over) (e:liing ~ kawmin ka ding to hi) (r:27.10.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
keen = (t:n) (w:cliff/precipice/steep place) (d:a steep rock face or height; keen sang is a high cliff and keen hawm a cleft in the crags) (e:vok hon in ~ sang tung pan) (r:40.8.32/21.12.5) (q:draft)
keising = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:owl/little owl) (d:a kind of owl, listed among the unclean birds) (e:Tua munah ~ in bu tomin) (r:23.34.15/3.11.17) (q:draft)
kengin = (t:v) (w:carrying/taking along/bringing) (d:keng, have a thing with one, with the linking ending -in before a verb of going or coming) (e:Letsong khat ~ Pasian’ mipa dawn dingin) (b:keng) (r:12.8.8/14.17.9) (q:draft)
khatpeuhah = (t:det) (w:in any/at any/at every) (d:khatpeuh, any one, with the place ending -ah, after a noun of place: in or at any such place; mun khatpeuhah means anywhere, wherever) (e:a siangtho mun ~ na ne ding) (b:khatpeuh) (r:3.10.14/20.7.12) (q:draft)
khauhna = (t:n) (w:hardness/stubbornness/firmness) (d:the quality of being hard or unyielding; lungsim khauhna is stubbornness of heart, and in Philippians 3:6 zeal) (e:amau lungsim ~ bangin ka tasak hi) (b:khauh) (r:19.81.12/5.9.27) (q:draft)
khawhna = (t:n) (w:cultivating/tilling) (d:khawh, work the soil, with the ending -na; lo khawhna tu is the tool for tilling a field, a plowshare or hoe) (e:Lo ~ tuute namsau-in seek un la) (b:khawh) (r:29.3.10/9.13.20) (q:draft)
khawhna = (t:n) (w:spearing/piercing) (d:in ngasa khawhna teipi, a spear for spearing fish, a harpoon) (e:Ngasa ~ teipi tawh a vun khawhlet) (r:18.41.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
khekna = (t:n) (w:exchange/substitute/substitution) (d:khek, put one thing in the place of another, with the ending -na: the act of exchanging or the thing given instead; khekna-in means in exchange for) (e:na ganhing ~-in an kong pia ding hi) (b:khek) (r:1.47.16/3.27.33) (q:draft)
khemte = (t:n) (w:deceivers/those who deceive/the treacherous) (d:khem, deceive, with the plural ending -te; mi khemte are people who deceive others) (e:mi ~ leh khemna a thuakte) (b:khem) (r:18.12.16/23.24.16) (q:draft)
khong = (t:n) (w:sorcery/soothsaying) (d:used with khai: khong khai means practise sorcery or soothsaying, and khong khaite are those who do so) (e:~ khaite leh ai saante’ thu ngai) (r:5.18.14/5.18.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
khong = (t:adv) (d:after a verb: merely staying in that state without doing anything more, as in bu khong, stay hidden, and en khong, only look on) (e:nang bu ~ na hi hiam) (r:19.10.1/19.35.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuakulh = (t:n) (w:city wall/wall) (d:khua, town, with kulh, wall: the wall built round a town for its defence) (e:~ khat ka kan thei hi) (r:19.18.29/10.22.30) (q:draft)
khuaphialepte = (t:n) (w:lightnings/flashes of lightning) (d:plural of khuaphialep) (e:Ama ~ in leitung taang sak a) (b:khuaphialep) (r:19.97.4/66.16.18) (q:draft)
khuisatna = (t:n) (w:sighing/groaning/sigh) (d:the act of breathing out heavily in grief or pain) (e:ka ~ nang kiang pan kiseel lo hi) (r:19.38.9/23.35.10) (q:draft)
khung = (t:v) (w:set/place/put up) (d:put something in position before or around: set a choice before people, put up a parapet round a roof) (e:na innkhum zangah tangban na ~ ding hi) (r:5.22.8/24.21.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
khung = (t:n) (w:top/upper end) (d:the upper end of something, opposite of taw, the bottom; in Ezekiel 40:6 the top of the steps of a gateway, where the NIV has threshold) (e:kahto-in a ~ a tun’ ciangin) (r:26.40.6/26.20.47) (q:draft, low confidence)
khutlekhezaw = (t:adj) (w:paralyzed/paralytic) (d:khut le khe, hand and foot, with zaw, weak or lame: unable to move the limbs; khutlekhezaw mi is a paralyzed person) (e:~ mi khat a lupna pheek tawh) (r:42.5.18/41.2.3) (q:draft)
kibanga = (t:adj) (w:like/alike/similar) (d:kibang, be alike, with the linking ending -a before another verb; tawh kibanga kibawl means made to be like, as in ngen tawh kibanga kibawl, made like a net, the network on the temple pillars) (e:Pasian tawh a ~ kibawl mi thak) (b:kibang) (r:49.4.21/11.7.41) (q:draft)
kibangsak = (t:v) (w:make equal/make like/make the same) (d:kibang, be alike, with sak, cause: make or treat one as the same as another) (e:nisa thuak kote tawh hong ~ hi) (b:kibang) (r:40.20.12/19.35.5) (q:draft)
kiciangtan = (t:v) (w:be fixed/be set/be determined/be limited) (d:of an amount, a number or a limit: be laid down beforehand; a kiciangtan zah is the fixed or allotted amount) (e:a nuntak ding kha phazah ~ khin hi) (b:ciangtan) (r:18.14.5/1.47.22) (q:draft)
kigalsai = (t:v) (w:be opposite/face each other) (d:lie facing something across a space, tawh marks what is faced; kigalsai-in is used like the English preposition opposite) (e:sabuai tawh a ~-in) (r:2.40.24/2.30.4) (q:draft)
kihaamsiatna = (t:n) (w:curse/object of cursing) (d:a person or place that people name when they curse, another spelling of kihamsiatna) (e:mite’ ~ suakin kuamah teeng nawn lo hi) (b:haamsiatna) (r:24.44.22/24.26.6) (q:draft)
kihamsiatna = (t:n) (w:curse/object of cursing) (d:a person or place that people name when they curse; kihamsiatna-in zang is use as a curse) (e:mite in ~-in a zat dingun) (b:hamsiatna) (r:24.24.9/24.26.6) (q:draft)
kihawl = (t:v) (w:be driven/be driven out/be banished) (d:passive of hawl, usually with khia, be driven out; hong kihawl gawpgawp is be driven hard) (e:khuamialna-ah ~ khia ding hi) (b:hawl) (r:18.18.18/32.2.4) (q:draft)
kiheikhiat = (t:v) (w:turn away/turn aside) (d:form of kiheikhia used before loh, theih and nading: turn away from a person, or of anger, turn away from those it rested on) (e:Kei’ kiang panin a ~ loh nadingun) (b:kiheikhia) (r:24.32.40/14.29.10) (q:draft)
kiheisak = (t:v) (w:turn/make turn/turn back) (d:kihei with causative sak: cause a person, a heart or an animal to turn toward or away from something; kiheisak kik is bring back) (e:a pumpi khempeuh i ~ thei hi) (b:kihei) (r:59.3.3/19.105.25) (q:draft)
kihut = (t:v) (w:defend oneself/protect oneself) (d:form of kihu used before nading; kihut nadingin means for defense, for protection, panin marks the danger) (e:~ nadingin Judah gam sungah khuapite) (b:kihu) (r:14.11.5/17.9.16) (q:draft)
kikaikhia = (t:v) (w:be dragged away/be pulled out/be led away) (d:passive of kaikhia) (e:A tangeekte nangawn uh ~ ding hi) (b:kaikhia) (r:24.49.20/18.18.14) (q:draft)
kikalin = (t:conj) (w:while/meanwhile) (d:placed after a clause, during the time that something else goes on; tua kikalin means meanwhile) (e:Zipipa a tun’ma ~ tua nungakte) (b:kikal) (r:40.25.5/1.24.62) (q:draft)
kikawm = (t:v) (w:be borrowed/be hired) (d:of an animal or a tool taken for use from its owner, on loan or for payment) (e:a ~ bangin pai ding hi) (r:2.22.15/12.6.5) (q:draft)
kikhawlin = (t:v) (w:keep company/be together/associate) (d:kikhawl with the linking ending in: being together with, tawh marks the companion) (e:Thu um khempeuh ~ omkhawm uh a) (b:kikhawl) (r:44.2.44/20.16.19) (q:draft)
kikhihin = (t:v) (w:be tied/be tethered/be fastened) (d:kikhih with the linking ending in: being tied, having something tied on) (e:suang lianpi khat ~ tuipi sungah) (b:kikhih) (r:41.9.42/12.7.10) (q:draft)
kikhol = (t:v) (w:be stored/be laid up/be kept) (d:passive of khol, of grain or goods put by for later) (e:na tampi a ~ zo hi) (b:khol) (r:42.12.19/3.26.10) (q:draft)
kilah = (t:v) (w:show oneself/appear/be shown/be revealed) (d:form of kilak used before khit, ni, leh and ciangin) (e:siampipa kiangah a ~ khit ciangin) (b:lah) (r:3.13.7/42.1.80) (q:draft)
kilawmna = (t:n) (w:fittingness/seemliness/beauty) (d:the quality of being fitting or presentable; a kilawmna om lo means it is not fitting) (e:mihaite’ adingin a ~ om lo hi) (b:kilawm) (r:20.26.1/46.12.23) (q:draft)
kilawn = (t:v) (w:be thrown/be cast) (d:passive of lawn; with suk be thrown down, with khia be thrown out) (e:meiphualpi sungah ~ hi) (b:lawn) (r:66.20.15/10.20.21) (q:draft)
kimawhsakna = (t:n) (w:accusation/charge/blame) (d:accusation made against someone, also the condemning of oneself in the heart) (e:a ~ lai pia loin paisak leng) (b:mawhsakna) (r:44.25.27/40.5.11) (q:draft)
kimawl = (t:v) (w:play/sport/perform) (d:play, as children do; also perform or hold a contest for others to watch) (e:gulgilo’ kuavangah ~ ding a) (r:23.11.8/7.16.25) (q:draft)
kimudah = (t:v) (w:be hated/be detested) (d:passive of mudah) (e:ngaihsutna hoih lo a neite ~ hi) (b:mudah) (r:20.14.17/23.60.15) (q:draft)
kimudah = (t:v) (w:hate one another/loathe oneself) (d:with khat leh khat, hate each other; with tawm, loathe oneself) (e:khat leh khat a ~ ding uh hi) (b:mudah) (r:40.24.10/26.36.31) (q:draft)
kingakna = (t:n) (w:stand/base) (d:a stand on which a thing rests, said of the wheeled stands that held the basins of the temple) (e:amah in a ~ sawm bawl hi) (b:ngakna) (r:11.7.37/11.7.43) (q:draft)
kinialna = (t:n) (w:argument/dispute/quarrel/controversy) (d:arguing between people; Topa a kinialna thu is the case the Lord brings against his people) (e:~ khempeuh kiciamna in a beisak hi) (b:kinial) (r:58.6.16/54.2.8) (q:draft)
kiniamkoih = (t:v) (w:be brought low/be humbled) (d:be put in a low and helpless state by enemies or hardship) (e:kei hong ~ ciangin amah in hong huh hi) (r:19.116.6/7.6.6) (q:draft)
kininsakin = (t:v) (w:defile oneself/be defiled/be desecrated) (d:kininsak with the linking ending in: making oneself unclean, or of a holy place, being made unclean) (e:tua nu amahmah ~ a pasal tungah) (b:kininsak) (r:4.5.27/26.25.3) (q:draft)
kiphatna = (t:n) (w:praise/commendation) (d:praise that someone receives; kiphatna lai is a letter of recommendation) (e:nangmah hong ~ in zong a zel hi) (b:phatna) (r:19.48.10/47.3.1) (q:draft)
kiphatsakpih = (t:v) (w:take pride in/boast of) (d:kiphatsak with pih: be proud on account of something; before a noun or standing alone, the thing one is proud of, the pride) (e:a ~ uh kizepna a manphate) (b:kiphatsak) (r:26.7.20/3.26.19) (q:draft)
kipiasak = (t:v) (w:make give/impose/let give) (d:have something given: of tribute, impose it on a land; with lo, not be allowed to give) (e:kham talen khat siah ~ hi) (b:kipia) (r:12.23.33/4.9.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisate = (t:n) (w:those who consider themselves) (d:kisa with plural te, placed after a describing word: people who think themselves so, as mipil a kisate, those who think themselves wise) (e:siam a ~ in gimna ngah ta hen) (b:kisa) (r:23.5.21/18.37.24) (q:draft)
kisate = (t:n) (w:songs sung) (d:in la kisate, the songs that are sung) (e:la ~ za thei nawn loin) (b:kisa) (r:21.12.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
kisuah = (t:v) (w:be made into/be divided into/be split into) (d:after a number with phel or khen: be torn or divided into that many parts) (e:a nuai lam dongin phel nih ~ hi) (b:suah) (r:41.15.38/40.27.51) (q:draft)
kisuksiatna = (t:n) (w:destruction/ruin) (d:the destroying of people or things, also people destroying one another) (e:ngongtatna leh ~ ka za ngitnget a) (b:suksiatna) (r:24.6.7/35.1.3) (q:draft)
kithawisa = (t:adj) (w:ready/prepared/made ready) (d:kithawi with sa, already done: having been made ready, also appointed and standing ready for a task) (e:galdo dingin ~-in Izipt leitang panin) (b:kithawi) (r:2.13.18/66.19.7) (q:draft)
kithawisak = (t:v) (w:make ready/get ready/prepare) (d:kithawi with causative sak: have people or things made ready, of a chariot hitch up) (e:amaute in a leeng ~ uh hi) (b:kithawi) (r:12.9.21/44.23.23) (q:draft)
kithokiksak = (t:v) (w:be raised/be raised to life) (d:passive of thokiksak, be made to rise again from death) (e:Pasian’ mi a sisa tampite zong ~ hi) (b:thokiksak) (r:40.27.52/51.1.18) (q:draft)
kithuah = (t:v) (w:be attached/be fitted with/be joined) (d:of a thing that has another thing fastened to it, tawh marks what is attached) (e:Savun khau tawh a ~ hakkol bawl in) (b:thuah) (r:24.27.2/10.20.8) (q:draft)
kithuah = (t:v) (w:accompany/keep company with/join) (d:of people, be together with someone, tawh marks the companion) (e:Kei tawh a ~ Titus nangawn) (b:thuah) (r:48.2.3/20.23.20) (q:draft)
kithuaksak = (t:v) (w:be made to suffer/be afflicted) (d:thuaksak with ki; gimna hong kithuaksak is suffering is laid on me) (e:amah gimna a ~ hangin) (b:thuaksak) (r:23.53.7/23.38.13) (q:draft)
kithun = (t:v) (w:be put into/be poured into/be filled) (d:passive of thun, of wine put into a skin or a container being filled) (e:savun um thak sungah a ~ ding hi) (b:thun) (r:42.5.38/40.9.17) (q:draft)
kizahtakna = (t:n) (w:fear/reverence) (d:the fear or reverence in which someone is held; Topa a kizahtakna is the fear of the Lord) (e:tungah Topa a ~ hong om hi) (b:zahtakna) (r:14.20.29/19.19.9) (q:draft)
koilai = (t:adv) (w:where/whereabouts/which place) (d:question word for place; koilai panin is from where, and repeated as koilai mun koilai gam it means in whatever place) (e:thumu pa’ inn ~ ahi hiam) (r:9.9.18/42.13.25) (q:draft)
kuak = (t:n) (w:hollow/cavity) (d:a hollow or bowl-shaped space: khut kuak is the hollow of the hand, lo kaihna kuak a furrow; a kuak-in means hollow inside) (e:ama khut ~ sungah tuite tehin) (r:23.40.12/2.38.7) (q:draft)
kuangsak = (t:v) (w:kindle/set on fire/make burn) (d:kuang burn with causative sak; also of anger, make it blaze) (e:sing in mei ~ a) (b:kuang) (r:20.26.21/42.12.49) (q:draft)
kumsukin = (t:v) (w:come down/go down/descend) (d:kumsuk with the linking ending in: coming down and then doing something else) (e:meii khuam hong ~ puanbuk kongkhak-ah ding a) (b:kumsuk) (r:2.33.9/44.20.10) (q:draft)
lahkhiat = (t:v) (w:reveal/show forth/bring out) (d:form of lakkhia used before loh, ding, nading and nouns: show openly, make known, bring a person out before others) (e:i Pasian in hong ~ loh thusim om a) (b:lah) (r:5.29.29/44.12.4) (q:draft)
laikung = (t:n) (w:pen/marker) (d:a tool for writing or for marking a line) (e:~ leh laitui tawh gelh ding) (r:64.1.13/23.44.13) (q:draft)
lamkal = (t:n) (w:way/journey) (d:the stretch between setting out and arriving; lamkal-ah om is be on the way) (e:Amaute ~-ah a om lai takin) (r:10.13.30/12.2.1) (q:draft)
lauhuaite = (t:adj) (w:terrible/fearsome/cruel/fierce) (d:lauhuai with plural te, after a noun: mi lauhuaite the cruel, ganhing lauhuaite fierce beasts) (e:tua lai-ah ganhing ~ kimu lo ding hi) (b:lauhuai) (r:23.35.9/24.15.21) (q:draft)
lehdote = (t:n) (w:rebels/the rebellious) (d:lehdo with plural te, those who rebel, often as mi lehdote) (e:mi ~ in langpan’ kei uh hen) (b:lehdo) (r:19.66.7/19.68.6) (q:draft)
liamnate = (t:n) (w:wounds/injuries) (e:Ka haina hangin ka ~ nai-in uih a) (b:liamna) (r:19.38.5/28.6.1) (q:draft)
liangin = (t:adv) (w:to the point of/even) (d:placed after a verb phrase to show how far a thing goes: so much that; ihmu lo liangin, even going without sleep) (e:pau thei lo ~ a om uh hi) (b:liang) (r:44.9.7/21.8.16) (q:draft)
liangin = (t:n) (w:shoulder) (d:liang shoulder with in; a phei a liangin, by leg and shoulder, means limb by limb) (e:a phei a ~ seh sawm-le-seh-nih suahin) (b:liang) (r:7.19.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
liau = (t:v) (w:pay/pay a fine) (d:pay what is owed or imposed, such as a fine, a debt or a tax) (e:ngun talen khat na ~ ding hi) (r:11.20.39/40.17.24) (q:draft)
lok = (t:v) (w:shake) (d:shake something strongly; lok gawp is shake violently, make tremble) (e:Topa in Kadesh gamlak ~ hi) (r:19.29.8/30.9.9) (q:draft)
lopipi = (t:part) (d:stronger form of lopi after a verb, used as lopipi-in: even though not; ut lopipi-in means unwillingly, against the will, and a kilawm lopipi-in in a way that is not fitting at all) (e:amah in ut ~-in amaute sawlkhia ding hi) (b:lopi) (r:2.6.1/45.1.28) (q:draft)
losak = (t:part) (d:negative lo with causative sak after a verb: make someone not do or not be, as lungkim losak displease and pau thei losak make unable to speak) (e:hih thugenna in amah lungkim ~ hi) (b:lo) (r:9.18.8/2.4.11) (q:draft)
lumletin = (t:v) (w:overturn/overthrow) (d:lumlet with the linking ending in: overturning) (e:zan khat thu-in amaute ~ susia gawp hi) (b:lumlet) (r:18.34.25) (q:draft)
lumletin = (t:v) (w:distort/pervert/unsettle) (d:lumlet with the linking ending in: turning a teaching, justice or a mind upside down) (e:Lai Siangtho khiatna ~ amau pumpi uh) (b:lumlet) (r:61.3.16/30.5.7) (q:draft)
lungkhamnate = (t:n) (w:troubles/distresses/anxieties) (e:na ~ khempeuh uh ama kiang tunpih un) (b:lungkhamna) (r:60.5.7/47.6.4) (q:draft)
lungman = (t:v) (w:be troubled/be perplexed/be amazed) (d:form of lungmang written with an apostrophe before na; lungman’na is trouble of heart, anxiety or amazement) (e:a ~’na leh dahna a kipan hi) (r:41.14.33/44.3.10) (q:draft)
lupkhawm = (t:v) (w:lie together/sleep with/have sexual relations) (d:lup lie down with khawm together, tawh marks the partner) (e:a sanggampa’ zi tawh a ~ ciangin) (b:lup) (r:1.38.9/3.15.18) (q:draft)
maban = (t:n) (w:continuation/what lies ahead/the rest) (d:the part still ahead of a work or course already begun; maban zom is carry on what others began, maban sem is go on with the work ahead) (e:i pu i pate’ ~ zomto vet un) (r:40.23.32/20.4.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
mahun = (t:part) (d:emphatic mah with the ending un, placed after a phrase where the doers are several: right, just, the very; a suah tung mahun, from the very time of birth) (e:A suah tung ~ lam khial pah uh a) (b:mah) (r:19.58.3/23.1.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
maikhingin = (t:adv) (w:with a downcast face/gloomily/sullenly) (d:maikhing with in: with a face that shows sorrow, shame or displeasure) (e:~ vak kawikawi hi) (r:11.21.27/42.24.17) (q:draft)
maiman = (t:v) (w:perish/vanish/be blotted out) (d:form of maimang written with an apostrophe before loh, nadingin and na; maiman’na is destruction) (e:Ama min Israel tungah a ~’ loh nadingin) (r:5.25.6/23.51.19) (q:draft)
maimangta = (t:v) (w:have vanished/be gone/disappear) (d:maimang with ta, which marks a change that has now come about) (e:a omna uh panin ~ hi) (b:maimang) (r:66.6.14/58.8.13) (q:draft)
maipuk = (t:v) (w:fall facedown/bow with face to the ground) (d:go down with the face to the ground, in a fall or to show respect) (e:lei lakah amah ~ hi) (r:9.17.49/9.25.23) (q:draft)
makna = (t:n) (w:divorce) (d:the putting away of a wife; makna lai is a certificate of divorce) (e:a zi tungah ~ lai pia ta hen) (r:40.5.31/39.2.16) (q:draft)
mancip = (t:v) (w:seize/grip/hold fast) (d:man seize with cip tightly; said of anguish, fear or trembling taking hold of people) (e:Leinuai sihna in kei hong ~ a) (b:man) (r:19.116.3/2.15.14) (q:draft)
manlah = (t:v) (w:be busy/be occupied) (d:be taken up with work, with no time left for other things) (e:a tawntungin ~ den hi) (r:20.31.27/37.1.9) (q:draft)
meite = (t:n) (w:tails) (d:plural of mei in the sense tail) (e:A ~ uh gul tawh kibang uh a) (b:mei) (r:66.9.19/7.15.4) (q:draft)
meite = (t:n) (w:fires/fire) (d:plural of mei in the sense fire) (e:amaute’ adingin na geelsa ~) (b:mei) (r:23.26.11) (q:draft)
mineute = (t:n) (w:the lowly/the small/common people) (d:plural of mineu, people of low standing, the opposite of miliante) (e:miliante leh ~ a si ding uh a) (b:mineu) (r:24.16.6/19.62.9) (q:draft)
minthuhna = (t:n) (w:seal/signet) (d:a seal for stamping a name on a document; minthuhna zungbuh is a signet ring) (e:kumpipa’ ~ zungbuh tawh thuh in) (r:17.8.8/17.3.10) (q:draft)
mittawtna = (t:n) (w:blindness) (e:Hih mite ~ tawh vatgawp in) (r:12.6.18/5.28.28) (q:draft)
mohte = (t:n) (w:cakes/loaves) (d:plural of moh; thei mohte are cakes of pressed figs) (e:sathau tawh a kihel silngo sawhloh ~) (b:moh) (r:2.29.2/13.12.40) (q:draft)
moipen = (t:adj) (w:youngest) (d:moi with pen, most; a moipen is the youngest one, the opposite of a hampen, the oldest) (e:a hampen panin kipanin a ~ tawh tawp a) (b:moi) (r:1.44.12/12.3.21) (q:draft)
molhtumte = (t:n) (w:clubs/cudgels) (d:plural of molhtum; kulh sukkhap nading molhtumte are battering rams) (e:namsau leh ~ tawi-in amau tawh hong tonkhawm) (b:molhtum) (r:40.26.47/26.4.2) (q:draft)
mopawi = (t:n) (w:wedding feast/wedding banquet/wedding) (e:~ siim dingin a khohsa mite) (r:40.22.3/42.14.8) (q:draft)
mutkhiat = (t:v) (w:blow away/blow off) (d:form of mutkhia used before ciangin and before a noun, said of wind) (e:huihpi in a ~ buhsi bangin) (r:18.21.18/66.6.13) (q:draft)
nambat = (t:n) (w:number) (d:a number as a figure or a count, from English number) (e:Tua ~ in zaguk sawmguk-guk ahi hi) (r:66.13.18/66.9.16) (q:draft)
naptui = (t:n) (w:nasal mucus) (d:used in the pair khitui naptui, tears and running nose, for bitter weeping) (e:khitui ~ tawh Pasian’ inn mai-ah kunin) (r:15.10.1/44.20.19) (q:draft)
nattun = (t:n) (w:fever) (d:also used as a verb, have a fever; often written with an apostrophe) (e:a lawn’ ciangin a ~’ dam a) (r:40.8.15/25.5.10) (q:draft)
nawhtat = (t:v) (w:hurry/hasten/be urgent) (d:act in haste or press someone to make haste; of a task, be urgent) (e:Izipt mite ~ mahmah uh hi) (r:2.12.33/9.21.8) (q:draft)
nawkkha = (t:v) (w:pass by/come past) (d:come past a place or a person on the way) (e:hih inn a ~ khempeuh in lamdangsa-in) (r:14.7.21/20.24.30) (q:draft)
neem = (t:adj) (w:soft/gentle/weak) (d:not hard or strong: tha neem is become weak, kam neem a gentle word, mit-hah neem weak eyes) (e:ka pumpi a tha ~ hi) (r:19.32.3/20.15.1) (q:draft)
neihzah = (t:n) (w:all that one has/as much as one has) (d:neih, form of nei, have, with zah, amount: the whole amount that one has; a aw neihzah tawh is at the top of his voice, na tha neihzah tawh with all your strength) (e:na tha ~ tawh sem in) (r:21.9.10/44.16.28) (q:draft)
nektum = (t:v) (w:eat up/consume/devour) (d:nek, form of ne, eat, with tum, wholly: eat until nothing is left, said of moths, locusts and disease) (e:nget in puan a ~ bangin) (r:23.51.8/18.19.26) (q:draft)
ngahpa = (t:n) (w:receiver/finder/one who gets) (d:ngah with pa, the man: the man who receives, gets or finds something, cidamna a ngahpa is the man who was healed) (e:cidamna a ~ in kua ahi hiam) (b:ngah) (r:43.5.13/19.119.162) (q:draft)
ngahzawh = (t:v) (w:win/gain/obtain/manage to get) (d:ngah, get, with zawh, form of zo, be able: succeed in getting; this form is used before nading and nak-uhleh) (e:thaman na ~ nadingun na tai un) (r:46.9.24/46.9.19) (q:draft)
ngapi = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:great fish/huge fish/whale) (d:nga, fish, with pi, big: the great fish that swallowed Jonah) (e:Jonah in tua ~ gil sung panin) (b:nga) (r:32.2.1/32.1.17) (q:draft)
nisat = (t:n) (w:heat of the day/heat of the sun) (d:form of nisa; sun nisat hun is the hot part of the day around noon, nisat hun the hot season) (e:sun ~ dong Ammonte vat tuk uh) (b:nisa) (r:9.11.11/10.4.5) (q:draft)
nisawm = (t:n) (w:ten days) (d:ni, day, with sawm, ten; nisawm-le-nih is twelve days, and with ni after it the day of the month, nisawm leh nili ni the fourteenth day) (e:~ sung etcik dingin a thukim hi) (r:27.1.14/27.1.15) (q:draft)
nitawp = (t:n) (w:last day/end time) (d:ni, day, with tawp, end; nearly always nitawp ni, the last day, the day of resurrection and judgment) (e:~ ni ciangin ka hingsak ding hi) (r:43.6.54/55.3.1) (q:draft)
nungngatin = (t:v) (w:turn one's back on/face away from) (d:nungngat with the linking ending in: with the back turned to someone, the opposite of maingat, to face; also said of God turning away from his people) (e:kei hong ~ hong maingat lo uh a) (b:nungngat) (r:24.32.33/1.21.16) (q:draft)
omkhak = (t:v) (w:happen to be/chance to be) (d:form of omkha used before leh, loh and pen: be or exist by chance, mostly in if-clauses and warnings) (e:a phamawh a ~ zenzen leh) (b:omkha) (r:15.7.20/58.3.12) (q:draft)
omkhawmin = (t:v) (w:be with/stay with/live with) (d:omkhawm with the linking ending in: being together with someone, tawh marks the companion) (e:tu-in note tawh ~ ka kam pauna) (b:omkhawm) (r:48.4.20/43.14.17) (q:draft)
omlaiteng = (t:n) (w:the rest/remainder/all that remain) (d:omlai, remain, with teng, all: everyone or everything that is still left) (e:mi a ~ kaikhawm inla) (b:omlai) (r:10.12.28/26.48.18) (q:draft)
omlaiteng = (t:conj) (w:as long as) (d:after a noun and a, for as long as that thing still exists) (e:Ni le kha a ~, khang tawntungin) (b:omlai) (r:19.72.5/18.14.12) (q:draft)
omngei = (t:v) (w:have been/once was/used to be) (d:om with ngei, of something that existed or was present at an earlier time; a omngei bangin means as it was before) (e:Nidangin ~ a, ahi zongin tu-in) (r:66.17.11/26.33.33) (q:draft)
ompihin = (t:v) (w:be with/stand by/accompany) (d:ompih with the linking ending in: being with someone to help and support) (e:kamsangte in amaute ~ huh uh hi) (b:ompih) (r:15.5.2/1.39.21) (q:draft)
omsakkik = (t:v) (w:restore/reestablish/bring back) (d:omsak with kik, again: cause to be as before, put back in its place; ki-omsakkik is the passive) (e:amaute a gam uhah ka ~ ciangin) (b:omsak) (r:24.31.23/24.33.7) (q:draft)
op = (t:v) (w:brood/sit on eggs/hatch) (d:of a bird, sit on eggs or cover the young) (e:a ~ sim vasa tawh kibang hi) (r:24.17.11/5.22.6) (q:draft)
op = (t:n) (w:deposit/scum/rust) (d:only in kang-op, the burnt crust stuck inside a cooking pot) (e:a kang-~ nin teng kangtumin) (r:26.24.11/26.24.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
paikawmun = (t:v) (w:as they go/while going/on the way) (d:pai with kawm, while, and the plural ending un: as they went along, doing something else at the same time) (e:A ~ hih thupiangte kikumkum uh hi) (r:42.24.14/9.6.12) (q:draft)
painasa = (t:v) (w:have gone/have passed through) (d:pai with na and sa, already, used before a noun of place: the place where someone has gone; a painasa-ah means where it has passed, in its wake) (e:Israel khempeuh tawh ka ~ mun khempeuh) (b:pai) (r:13.17.6/4.14.7) (q:draft)
pakin = (t:adv) (w:quickly/suddenly/at once) (d:pak with the ending in, after a verb: happening fast or all at once) (e:tuate bei ~, kote ka maimang uh hi) (b:pak) (r:19.90.10/18.9.23) (q:draft)
pakte = (t:n) (w:flowers/blossoms) (d:plural of pak; also the flower ornaments of the lampstand) (e:a nunte leh a ~ tawh a om) (b:pak) (r:2.25.34/18.15.33) (q:draft)
pamah = (t:prep) (w:beside/alongside/around) (d:pam, side or edge, with ah: at or along the side of something; a kiim a pamah means all around, round about) (e:A kiim a ~ a pai mi khempeuh) (b:pam) (r:25.1.12/44.27.8) (q:draft)
panmunte = (t:n) (w:posts/positions/stations) (d:plural of panmun, the place where one stands to serve or fight: the duties of priests and Levites, and gal panmunte, defences or strongholds) (e:siampite amau’ ~ ah seh a) (b:panmun) (r:14.35.2/36.3.6) (q:draft)
pannate = (t:n) (w:testimonies/statutes) (d:plural of panna, found only in teci pannate, the testimonies of God, what he has borne witness to as his will) (e:na teci ~ ka deih hi) (b:panna) (r:19.119.119/19.119.88) (q:draft)
pauthei = (t:v) (w:be able to speak/can talk) (d:pau, speak, with thei, be able; pauthei lo means mute, unable to speak) (e:Zekhariah hong ~ kik a, Pasian a phat hi) (b:pau) (r:42.1.64/41.9.25) (q:draft)
pawlpawl = (t:adj) (w:various/of every kind/all kinds of) (d:pawl, group or kind, doubled: of many different kinds, in every way; often written a pawlpawl after the noun) (e:cinatna ~ a neite khempeuh) (r:42.4.40/45.3.2) (q:draft)
phatkik = (t:v) (w:praise again) (d:phat, praise, with kik, again) (e:ka Pasian ka ~ na ding hi) (b:phat) (r:19.43.5/19.42.11) (q:draft)
phatkik = (t:v) (w:make good again/restore/repair) (d:after bawl or puah: phat, form of pha, good, with kik, again: put back into a good state) (e:ka puah ~ theih nadingin) (r:16.2.5/20.29.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
phiatkhiat = (t:v) (w:blot out/wipe out/cut off) (d:form of phiatkhia used before sak, ding and ciangin: wipe away or remove completely, of sins, a name or enemies) (e:Israel min a ~ ding Topa in) (b:phiatkhia) (r:12.14.27/19.51.9) (q:draft)
phukham = (t:v) (w:burst/break open/break through) (d:break something by force or pressure, as a door, a wineskin or an enemy line; of a rash, break out on the skin) (e:a savun um ~ ding a) (r:42.5.37/10.5.20) (q:draft)
phukhia = (t:v) (w:break out/break through/erupt) (d:phu, push against, with khia, out: force a way out or through; of a skin disease, break out on the skin) (e:meimatum sung tawnin hong ~ ahi hi) (b:phu) (r:3.13.20/12.3.26) (q:draft)
phulkhia = (t:v) (w:gush out/burst forth/spring out) (d:of water, come out with force from rock or ground) (e:suangpi hong a, tui ~ hi) (b:phul) (r:19.105.41/23.35.6) (q:draft)
phunphun = (t:v) (w:complain/grumble/murmur) (d:phun doubled: keep on complaining or muttering; zi phunphun is a nagging wife) (e:bang hanga ~ ding i hi hiam) (r:25.3.39/20.19.13) (q:draft)
piakhin = (t:v) (w:have given/have granted) (d:pia with khin, already: the giving is done) (e:deihna nang in na ~ a) (b:pia) (r:19.21.2/62.2.20) (q:draft)
pianma = (t:adv) (w:before the birth of/before the creation of/before it happens) (d:pian, form of piang, be born or come about, with ma, before: before something was born, made or took place; leitung pianma is before the world was made) (e:hihte khempeuh hong ~-in keima hangin) (r:42.21.12/49.1.4) (q:draft)
puantungsilhte = (t:n) (w:tunics/coats) (d:plural of puantungsilh, the outer garment worn by the priests) (e:amaute ~ na silhsak ding a) (b:puantungsilh) (r:2.40.14/2.28.40) (q:draft)
puato = (t:v) (w:carry up/bring up/take up) (d:pua, carry, with to, upward: carry to a higher place) (e:Levi mite in tuate ~ uh hi) (b:pua) (r:14.5.5/11.17.19) (q:draft)
pumtangin = (t:adv) (w:with the whole body/all over the body) (d:pumtang, the whole body, with the ending in: in or over the entire body) (e:mizawng khat in a ~ meima vei a) (r:42.16.20/40.5.30) (q:draft)
saangin = (t:v) (w:receive/accept/take) (d:saang with the linking ending in: taking what is handed over, or accepting a plea) (e:Pasian in ama kutna ~, a thuumna ngai hi) (b:saang) (r:14.33.13/23.37.14) (q:draft)
sanggampate = (t:n) (w:brothers/kinsmen) (d:plural of sanggampa, male siblings; also fellow countrymen) (e:ka sanggamnute, ka ~, leh amaute tawh) (b:sanggampa) (r:6.2.13/5.15.3) (q:draft)
sawmin = (t:num) (w:by tens/ten times) (d:sawm, ten, with the ending in: a tul sawmin is by tens of thousands, a zah sawmin is ten times as much) (e:David in a tul ~ that) (b:sawm) (r:9.18.7/27.1.20) (q:draft)
seekin = (t:v) (w:forge/hammer out/chisel/shape) (d:seek with the linking ending in: shaping metal by hammering, cutting stone tablets, or forming bricks from clay) (e:A masa-a bangin suangpeek nih ~) (b:seek) (r:5.10.1/1.11.3) (q:draft)
seelcip = (t:v) (w:hide/conceal/cover up/keep hidden) (d:seel with cip, tightly: hide completely so that it stays out of sight) (e:a topa’ sum a ~ hi) (b:seel) (r:40.25.18/58.11.23) (q:draft)
seem = (t:v) (w:blow/blow on/fan) (d:of wind, blow over or upon something; of a fire, blow or fan it so that it burns) (e:huih in amah ~-in beimang a) (r:19.103.16/26.24.10) (q:draft)
seem = (t:v) (w:work/do/serve) (d:spelling of sem, work, used with na, work or task: na seem is do work, be at work) (e:kei hong sawlpa’ na i ~ ding hi) (r:43.9.4/47.4.12) (q:draft)
sehnih = (t:num) (w:two parts/two-tenths) (d:seh, part or share, with nih, two; sehsawm suah sehnih is two parts out of ten, two-tenths) (e:a tuutal tawh sehsawm suah ~) (r:4.29.9/4.28.28) (q:draft)
sekpi = (t:n) (w:hammer/sledgehammer/war club) (d:sek, hammer, with pi, big: a heavy hammer; also a picture of a power that smashes nations) (e:ka ~ leh ka galhiam na hi a) (b:sek) (r:24.51.20/23.41.7) (q:draft)
septheih = (t:v) (w:be able to do/be able to work) (d:sep, work or do, with theih, be able, used before nading: so that one can do or carry out) (e:na hoih na phate a ~ nadingun) (b:sep) (r:56.3.14/55.3.16) (q:draft)
siahdongpa = (t:n) (w:tax collector/publican) (d:siahdong with pa, the man: a man who collects taxes) (e:Thomas le ~ Matthai) (b:siahdong) (r:40.10.3/42.18.10) (q:draft)
siangte = (t:adj) (w:clean/pure) (d:siang with plural te: those that are clean or pure, of animals that may be eaten, people who are ritually clean, and pure gold) (e:ganhing a ~ khempeuh na ne thei) (b:siang) (r:5.14.20/5.12.22) (q:draft)
siangthosakin = (t:v) (w:sanctify/consecrate/make holy/purify) (d:siangthosak with the ending in, which links to the next verb or, at the end of a sentence, gives a command) (e:zingciang sung teng amaute ~) (b:siangthosak) (r:2.19.10/43.17.17) (q:draft)
siasakin = (t:v) (w:destroy/ruin/bring down) (d:siasak with the linking ending in) (e:Keimah in na khuapite uh ~) (b:siasak) (r:3.26.31/20.7.26) (q:draft)
sihin = (t:v) (w:die/when one dies/at death) (d:sih, form of si, die, with the ending in: at the time of dying, or dying in a certain state; a sihin kum za is he was a hundred years old when he died) (e:Hor Mual-ah Aaron a ~ kum za) (b:sih) (r:4.33.39/14.24.15) (q:draft)
siik = (t:v) (w:exact/demand payment/collect a debt) (d:require a debtor to pay back what he owes, leiba siik) (e:Gam dang mite tung pan na ~ thei) (r:5.15.3) (q:draft)
siik = (t:n) (w:side/corner) (d:a siik kikim means with equal sides, squared, said of doorposts) (e:kongkhak khuamte pen a ~ kikim vive) (r:26.41.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
siklukhu = (t:n) (w:helmet) (d:sik, iron, with lukhu, hat: a metal helmet worn in battle) (e:a lu tungah sumngo ~ nei-in) (r:9.17.5/26.38.5) (q:draft)
simun = (t:conj) (w:whenever/every time/as often as) (d:sim, every, after a verb, with the plural ending un: each time that they or you do something) (e:hih hai na dawn ~, Topa hong paikik matengin) (r:46.11.26/26.39.15) (q:draft)
singteh = (t:n) (w:leaf/leaves) (d:sing, tree, with teh, leaf: the leaf of a tree) (e:Kote khempeuh ~ bangin ka vul uh a) (r:23.64.6/20.11.28) (q:draft)
suangngo = (t:n) (c:stone) (w:alabaster/marble) (d:suang, stone, with ngo, white: a white stone; suangngo thawl is an alabaster jar) (e:paknamtui ~ thawl khat paipih a) (r:42.7.37/22.5.15) (q:draft)
sungte = (t:n) (w:insides/interiors/rooms) (d:sung, inside, with plural te: the inner parts of several things, inn sungte the rooms of a house; with ah or panin, into or from inside them) (e:ka vankoihna inn ~ panin amaute) (b:sung) (r:12.20.15/13.9.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
suntangpi = (t:n) (w:broad daylight/daytime/midday) (d:suntang, daytime, with pi, great: the full light of day; suntangpi-in means in broad daylight) (e:muh dingin ~-in ka hih ding hi) (r:10.12.12/18.5.14) (q:draft)
supai = (t:v) (w:tear down/demolish/smash/break down) (d:knock down something that was built, such as towers, walls, altars and sacred pillars) (e:Kulhte ~-in inn hoihpipite satthang gawp) (r:26.26.12/14.14.3) (q:draft)
supna = (t:n) (w:loss) (d:what is lost or given up, the opposite of phattuamna, gain; supna thuak is suffer loss) (e:tua ~ keimahmah in ka thuak hi) (r:1.31.39/50.3.7) (q:draft)
sutte = (t:n) (w:robbers/swindlers/extortioners) (d:sut, take by force, with plural te: those who seize what belongs to others; zawhthawh bawla sutte are those who take by force or fraud) (e:Zawhthawh thu tawh mi’ na a ~ in) (b:sut) (r:20.1.19/46.6.10) (q:draft)
taangkona = (t:n) (w:proclamation/announcement/decree) (d:a public announcement made aloud through a land; taangkona bawl is make a proclamation) (e:nakpitakin ~ khat kibawl a) (b:taangko) (r:27.3.4/14.36.22) (q:draft)
taiina = (t:n) (w:rebuke/discipline/correction/reproof) (d:taii, rebuke, with na: words or acts that correct someone) (e:keima ~ tawh tuipi ka keusak a) (b:taii) (r:23.50.2/18.5.17) (q:draft)
taisim = (t:v) (w:flee/run away/escape) (d:tai, run, with sim, secretly: slip away from danger or from a person) (e:lau-in Izipt gamah a ~ hi) (r:24.26.21/24.48.44) (q:draft)
taktakna = (t:n) (w:genuineness/sincerity/reality) (d:taktak, truly, with na, placed after a verb or adjective to make a noun: the fact of truly doing or being so, as in it taktakna, true love, and lungkim taktakna, full conviction) (e:note ka hong it ~ thu) (b:taktak) (r:50.1.8/52.1.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
tangguak = (t:adj) (w:naked/bare/stripped) (d:without clothes; tangguakin is the adverb, and tangguak kheguak means naked and barefoot) (e:ka nasempa Isaiah ~ leh kheguak tawh) (r:23.20.3/21.5.15) (q:draft)
tawhna = (t:n) (w:digging/quarrying) (d:tawh, form of to, dig, with na: the act or place of digging a pit or well, or of cutting stone from the ground; kan tawhna is a siege ramp) (e:hih tuikhuk ka ~ thu-ah nang in) (r:1.21.30/20.26.27) (q:draft)
tawhsa = (t:v) (w:dug/have dug) (d:tawh, form of to, dig, with sa, already: placed before a noun, the pit or well that someone has dug) (e:ama ~ gum sung mah ah amah kia) (r:19.7.15/1.26.32) (q:draft)
tawmzaw = (t:adj) (w:less/fewer/smaller/scarcer) (d:tawm with zaw, more: the comparative; sangin marks what it is compared with) (e:a zawngte in ~ pia lo ding hi) (b:tawm) (r:2.30.15/23.13.12) (q:draft)
tehpih = (t:v) (w:compare/liken/match) (d:teh, measure, with pih, together with: set beside another to compare; tehpih theih ding om lo means nothing can be compared, without equal) (e:Amah ~ theih ding leitungah bangmah om lo) (b:teh) (r:18.41.33/20.8.11) (q:draft)
thamanin = (t:adv) (w:as a reward/as wages/in return for) (d:thaman with the ending in: as payment or gain for work done, the work is named before it) (e:a nasepna ~ an ne tui dawnin) (b:thaman) (r:21.2.24/1.29.27) (q:draft)
thazaw = (t:v) (w:be weak/grow weak/fail/lose heart) (d:tha, strength, with zaw, weak: have no strength left, said of eyes, hands and courage; thazaw sak is weaken or discourage) (e:Na khut ~ sak kei in) (b:tha) (r:36.3.16/19.119.82) (q:draft)
theihsakna = (t:n) (w:signal/alarm/sign/notice) (d:theihsak, make known, with na: something that gives notice, such as a trumpet blast or a smoke signal; theihsakna lim is a sign) (e:Bethhakkherim khua-ah ~ meikhu suaksak un) (b:theihsak) (r:24.6.1/4.10.7) (q:draft)
themthum = (t:adv) (w:again and again/repeatedly/constantly/back and forth) (d:after a verb, doing the action over and over or changing from one thing to another) (e:inn khatah kawm ~ kei un) (r:42.10.7/47.1.18) (q:draft)
thokiksak = (t:v) (w:raise/raise up/bring back to life) (d:thokik with causative sak: make someone rise again from death) (e:Pasian in misite a ~ ding hi) (b:thokik) (r:44.26.8/44.5.30) (q:draft)
thuahin = (t:adv) (w:in addition/on top/besides/more) (d:thuah with the ending in, after a verb: doing it over or on top of what is there already, adding a further layer or more of the same) (e:Jerusalem ah zi nei ~ tapate leh tanute) (b:thuah) (r:13.14.3/51.3.14) (q:draft)
thuciamtehpa = (t:n) (w:recorder/chronicler) (d:thuciamteh with pa, the man: the court official who keeps the records) (e:Ahilud’ tapa Jehoshafat in ~ hi) (b:thuciamteh) (r:10.8.16/23.36.3) (q:draft)
thukzaw = (t:adj) (w:deeper) (d:thuk, deep, with zaw, more: a vun sangin thukzaw means deeper than the skin) (e:a vun sangin a ~ loin a kimuh leh) (r:3.13.34/3.13.30) (q:draft)
thumong = (t:n) (w:fate/destiny/lot/end) (d:thu, matter, with mong, end: what a person comes to in the end, the outcome of a life) (e:Hih in mihingte’ ~ ahi hi) (r:21.5.18/21.9.2) (q:draft)
thungetnate = (t:n) (w:prayers/pleas) (d:plural of thungetna) (e:Jessi’ tapa David’ ~ bei ta hi) (b:thungetna) (r:19.72.20/19.109.7) (q:draft)
thutanna = (t:n) (w:judgment/condemnation/verdict/sentence) (d:the deciding of a case and the sentence given; mawhna thutanna is condemnation, thutanna thuak is suffer judgment) (e:sung bekinah ~ na thuak ta hi) (r:66.18.10/47.3.9) (q:draft)
thuthei = (t:adj) (w:knowledgeable/learned/understanding/prudent) (d:knowing or understanding matters, from thu and thei know; thuthei mi is a man of learning or insight, thuthei lopi-in is without knowledge) (e:no ~ mite aw) (b:thu) (r:18.34.2/13.27.32) (q:draft)
thuumnate = (t:n) (w:supplications/pleas/cries for mercy) (d:plural of thuumna, often paired with thungetna prayer) (e:ka ~ hong ngai hi) (b:thuumna) (r:19.116.1/14.6.39) (q:draft)
tuaka = (t:adv) (w:each/both) (d:tuak with the ending -a, used after pang side: pang tuaka is on each side or on both sides) (e:gun pang ~ ding mi nih) (b:tuak) (r:27.12.5/26.41.2) (q:draft)
tuaksak = (t:v) (w:inflict/make suffer/bring upon) (d:cause someone to meet with or undergo something, usually trouble or punishment) (e:Gimna lianpipite hong ~ nangmah in) (b:tuak) (r:19.71.20/15.9.13) (q:draft)
tualpi = (t:n) (w:square/open square/public square) (d:large open space of a town, from tual with -pi large) (e:Tui Kongpi mai-a om ~ lam) (b:tual) (r:16.8.3/17.4.6) (q:draft)
tualpi = (t:n) (w:robe) (d:in puan tualpi, a long outer garment or robe, also written as one word puantualpi) (e:saihadial puan ~ silh a) (r:13.15.27/27.3.21) (q:draft, low confidence)
tuamsak = (t:v) (w:bind up/wrap/cover/blindfold) (d:wrap or cover something, as bandaging a wound or a broken arm, or covering the eyes) (e:amau’ meimate ~ hi) (b:tuam) (r:19.147.3/42.22.64) (q:draft)
tuksak = (t:v) (w:make stumble/cause to fall/cast down/strike down) (e:bangmah in amaute ~ zo lo hi) (b:tuk) (r:19.119.165/19.73.18) (q:draft)
tup = (t:v) (w:intend/aim/purpose) (d:tup lohpi is unintentionally; a tup is what one aims at) (e:~ lohpi leh theih lohna hangin) (r:26.45.20/20.12.27) (q:draft)
tup = (t:v) (w:knock/strike/hit) (d:with khiat, knock out) (e:a ha a ~ khiat leh) (r:2.21.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
ututin = (t:adv) (w:as one pleases/freely/at will) (d:doing whatever one wants, without restraint or hindrance) (e:a ~ a gamta ding uh hi) (r:27.11.16/44.28.31) (q:draft)
vangikpi = (t:n) (w:heavy burden/burden/heavy load) (d:vangik with -pi great; with suan, lay a heavy burden on someone) (e:mite tungah ~ suan uh a) (b:vangik) (r:16.5.15/19.66.11) (q:draft)
vangsak = (t:v) (w:make successful/prosper/grant success) (d:used with ma or lampi, the way ahead: make a journey or undertaking succeed) (e:tu ni-in ka ma hong ~ in) (b:vang) (r:1.24.12/1.24.40) (q:draft)
velval = (t:adv) (w:bitterly/severely) (d:follows na pain, na sa feel pain, na sak cause pain or kha bitter: with intense, sharp suffering) (e:tumin na sak ~ ding hi) (r:4.5.24/26.5.16) (q:draft)
vulin = (t:v) (w:wither/fade/wilt) (d:vul with the linking ending -in: withering, and so) (e:nitak ciangin ~ keu uh hi) (b:vul) (r:19.90.6/23.24.4) (q:draft)
zahta = (t:adv) (w:so much/this much/such) (d:follows hih or tua: to such an extent, in such an amount) (e:sisan tua ~ luangsak na hih manin) (b:zah) (r:13.22.8/18.6.10) (q:draft)
zaksak = (t:v) (w:tell/report/proclaim/make known) (d:cause to hear) (e:nungzui dangte a ~ uh hangin) (b:zak) (r:41.16.13/42.4.19) (q:draft)
zattheih = (t:v) (w:can be used/be usable/be able to use) (d:zat use with theih can, mostly before ding or nading: so that it can be used, fit for use) (e:~ ding hi nawn lo hi) (b:zat) (r:24.13.7/45.6.13) (q:draft)
zawlai = (t:adv) (w:even more/still more/more) (d:comparative zaw with lai still, placed after a verb or descriptive word) (e:mihaipa adingin lametna om ~ hi) (r:20.29.20/14.28.22) (q:draft)
zawngkhalna = (t:n) (w:infirmity/sickness/weakness) (d:weakness of body; of crops, ankung zawngkhalna is blight or mildew) (e:ankung ~ ahi a, kauphe ahi a) (b:zawngkhal) (r:11.8.37/42.7.21) (q:draft)
zawngkhalna = (t:n) (w:poverty) (d:state of being poor and powerless) (e:a hau napi-in ~ a thuakna tawh) (b:zawngkhal) (r:47.8.9) (q:draft)
zinei = (t:v) (w:marry/take a wife) (d:of a man, have or take a wife, from zi wife and nei have; zinei thak pa is the bridegroom, zinei pasalnei is marrying and being given in marriage) (e:~ pasalnei cih om lo ding uh hi) (r:41.12.25/24.25.10) (q:draft)
zingciang = (t:adv) (w:tomorrow/the next day) (d:also the day after an event: a zingciang ni) (e:tu ni leh ~ sung teng) (r:2.19.10/6.5.11) (q:draft)
zonna = (t:n) (w:seeking/search) (d:the act of seeking or looking for something; with ding, a means or purpose of seeking) (e:pilna ~ ding sum tampi) (b:zon) (r:20.17.16/12.5.7) (q:draft)
zote = (t:n) (w:those who are able/those who manage) (d:zo be able or succeed with plural -te, after a verb: those who manage to do it, as a thuak zote, those who endure) (e:A tawp dongin a thuak ~ in) (b:zo) (r:41.13.13/20.18.22) (q:draft)
zozo = (t:v) (w:overcome/prevail/tame) (d:reduplicated zo, win or be able; with a negative, cannot manage at all) (e:lunghimawh kei un, leitung ka ~ hi) (b:zo) (r:43.16.33/59.3.8) (q:draft)
zuikha = (t:v) (w:follow/be led to follow) (d:zui follow with kha happen to: follow by mistake or be drawn into following, often in warnings) (e:Tua bang mite’ nung ~ kei un) (r:42.21.8/61.3.17) (q:draft)
zukhamte = (t:n) (w:drunkards) (e:No ~ aw, tho un la kap un) (b:zukham) (r:29.1.5/19.69.12) (q:draft)
zuksak = (t:v) (w:make rain/send rain/bring rain) (d:cause rain to fall, used with guah rain) (e:Leilu lam huih in guah a ~ bangin) (b:zuk) (r:20.25.23/26.22.24) (q:draft)
zulhtat = (t:adj) (w:unruly/undisciplined/disorderly) (d:lacking restraint; khuaval zulhtat lo is sober or self-controlled, thadah zulhtat mite are the idle and disorderly) (e:khuaval ~ lo mi, a dik mi) (r:56.1.8/52.5.14) (q:draft)
zune = (t:v) (w:drink/feast) (d:drink liquor, from zu and ne; mostly in the pair anne zune, eat and drink) (e:Anne ~ dingin mite tu uh a) (r:46.10.7/21.10.16) (q:draft)
zungbuhte = (t:n) (w:rings) (d:plural of zungbuh finger ring; min gelhna zungbuhte are signet rings) (e:min gelhna ~ leh nakbuhte) (b:zungbuh) (r:23.3.21/42.15.22) (q:draft)
zunglot = (t:v) (w:uproot/pluck up/root out) (d:pull out by the roots; of people, remove them completely from their land) (e:leitang panin nang hong ~ ding hi) (r:19.52.5/5.29.28) (q:draft)
zusakin = (t:v) (w:rain down/send rain/make fall) (d:zusak cause to fall or rain with the linking ending -in: sending down, and so) (e:amau tungah manna an ~) (b:zusak) (r:19.78.24/26.13.13) (q:draft)
Adin = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Adin) (r:16.10.16/15.8.6) (q:draft)
Assir = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Assir) (r:2.6.24/13.6.22) (q:draft)
Biakinnpi = (t:n) (w:Temple/sanctuary) (d:capitalised form of biakinnpi, the Temple in Jerusalem) (e:a ~ nangawn a susia hi) (b:biakinnpi) (r:25.2.1/25.1.4) (q:draft)
Dor = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Dor) (r:7.1.27/6.17.11) (q:draft)
Hathak = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Hathak) (r:17.4.5/17.4.9) (q:draft)
Imlah = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Imlah) (d:father of the prophet Micaiah) (r:11.22.8/14.18.8) (q:draft)
Kadesh-barnea = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Kadesh Barnea) (r:4.32.8/6.10.41) (q:draft)
Kana = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Cana) (d:town in Galilee) (e:Galile gam ~ khua-ah a paikik hi) (r:43.4.46/43.2.1) (q:draft)
Leihawm = (t:n) (w:the Pit/pit) (d:capitalised form of leihawm, the pit as the place of the dead) (e:~ sunga pai khinsate lak panin) (b:leihawm) (r:19.30.3/23.14.15) (q:draft)
Lod = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Lod) (r:16.11.35/13.8.12) (q:draft)
Mangpa = (t:n) (w:official/governor/lord) (d:capitalised form of mangpa used as a title: the Ethiopian official of Acts 8, the governor Festus, and Christ as the author or prince of life) (e:Festas ~ tua gamah) (b:mangpa) (r:44.25.1/44.8.38) (q:draft)
Melkhi = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Melki) (r:42.3.24/42.3.28) (q:draft)
Munah = (t:n) (w:in the Place) (d:capitalised mun place with the locative ending -ah, in titles such as Siangthopen Munah, in or into the Most Holy Place) (e:Siangthopen ~ zong lut thei lo ding uh hi) (b:munah) (r:26.44.13/58.9.8) (q:draft)
Ngasa = (t:n) (w:Fish) (d:capitalised form of ngasa fish, in the name Ngasa Kongpi, the Fish Gate of Jerusalem) (e:tapate in ~ Kongpi bawl uh hi) (b:ngasa) (r:16.3.3/16.12.39) (q:draft)
Nin = (t:n) (w:Dung) (d:capitalised form of nin dirt or filth, in the name Nin Kongpi, the Dung Gate of Jerusalem) (e:Malkhijah in ~ Kongpi puah hi) (b:nin) (r:16.3.14/16.2.13) (q:draft)
O = (t:intj) (w:O/oh) (d:exclamation placed before a name in address or lament, as English O) (e:~ Moab! gimna na ngah hi) (r:4.21.29/10.7.20) (q:draft)
Oboth = (t:name) (c:place) (w:Oboth) (d:camping place of Israel in the wilderness) (r:4.21.10/4.33.43) (q:draft)
Paddan-aram = (t:name) (c:land) (w:Paddan Aram) (r:1.28.2/1.35.26) (q:draft)
Sela = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Sela) (d:town of Edom) (r:12.14.7/23.16.1) (q:draft)
Silngo = (t:n) (w:Yeast/leaven) (d:capitalised form of silngo in the festival name Silngo Sawh loh Anlum Pawi, the Festival of Unleavened Bread) (e:~ Sawh loh Anlum Pawi hun hong naita hi) (b:silngo) (r:42.22.1/14.35.17) (q:draft)
Soko = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Soko) (r:14.11.7/14.28.18) (q:draft)
Tuu = (t:n) (w:Sheep) (d:capitalised form of tuu sheep, in the name Tuu Kongpi, the Sheep Gate of Jerusalem) (e:nasep kipanin ~ Kongpi bawl uh hi) (b:tuu) (r:16.3.1/16.12.39) (q:draft)
Ukpa = (t:n) (w:Ruler/Chief/Overseer/Prince) (d:capitalised form of ukpa as a title of Christ: Siampi Ukpa is the high priest, Tuucing Ukpa the Chief Shepherd) (e:Tuucing ~ hong kilat ciangin) (b:ukpa) (r:60.5.4/44.5.31) (q:draft)
Ulam = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Ulam) (r:13.7.16/13.8.39) (q:draft)
Uriel = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Uriel) (r:13.15.5/14.13.2) (q:draft)
Veng = (t:n) (w:Quarter/district) (d:capitalised form of veng, a quarter or section of a town, in Veng Nihna, the Second or New Quarter of Jerusalem) (e:tua khuapi ~ Nihna sungah mite’ kahna) (b:veng) (r:36.1.10/12.22.14) (q:draft)
aituam = (t:adj) (w:own/personal/private) (d:follows a possessor: ama aituam is his own, ama aituam dingin is for himself) (e:ama ~ dingin sakolte tampi) (r:5.17.16/22.8.12) (q:draft)
akilawm = (t:adj) (w:fitting/proper/deserving/reasonable) (d:kilawm with the prefix a- written as one word: that which is fitting or deserved) (e:Na khempeuh ~ akituakin na hih un) (b:kilawm) (r:46.14.40/44.25.25) (q:draft)
alna = (t:n) (w:saltiness/salty taste) (d:al salty with -na) (e:hangin a ~ mang leh) (b:al) (r:41.9.50/40.5.13) (q:draft)
angsung = (t:n) (w:self-interest/own good) (d:literally the inside of the bosom; angsung ding bek is only for oneself) (e:note’ ~ ding bek zong kei unla) (r:46.10.24/36.3.4) (q:draft)
angsung = (t:n) (w:bosom/breast) (d:the bosom where a child is held or nursed) (e:~ panin a kilakhia) (r:23.28.9/23.49.22) (q:draft)
anhuan = (t:v) (w:cook/bake) (d:an food with huan cook; anhuan pa is a cook or baker) (e:~ ding leh an em dingin) (r:9.8.13/1.40.1) (q:draft)
awkpih = (t:v) (w:be trapped by/be ensnared by) (d:awk be caught with -pih: be caught by means of something, usually one's own words or deeds) (e:amau kampau mah ~ uh hi) (b:awk) (r:20.18.7/20.12.13) (q:draft)
awle = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:crocodile/sea monster/Leviathan) (d:large water creature; the verses use it for the monster of the Nile and for Leviathan) (e:Gun sungah a om, ~ lianpi ahi) (r:26.29.3/18.3.8) (q:draft)
bak = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:bat) (e:huihtun leh ~ ahi hi) (r:3.11.19/5.14.18) (q:draft)
bak = (t:n) (w:piece/portion) (d:counting word for a piece of meat: sa bak khat, one piece of meat) (e:anlum lum khat, sa ~ khat) (r:13.16.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
bak = (t:v) (w:hold up to/put to) (d:hold something up against the mouth) (e:ama kamah a ~ uh hi) (r:43.19.29) (q:draft, low confidence)
bansau = (t:adj) (w:long-sleeved) (d:ban arm with sau long; puantualpi bansau is the long-sleeved robe of Joseph and of Tamar, the ornate robe of the NIV) (e:adingin puantualpi ~ khat bawlsak hi) (r:1.37.3/10.13.19) (q:draft)
bawlbawl = (t:v) (w:keep doing/go on doing/continue) (d:reduplicated bawl do or make: keep on doing; in some verses be doing or preparing) (e:mawhna ~ ding ihi hiam) (b:bawl) (r:45.6.1/28.4.18) (q:draft)
beba = (t:adv) (w:wide open/gaping) (d:describes the mouth opened wide, after kamkat or kam ka) (e:kei hong kamkat ~ uh hi) (r:19.22.13/23.5.14) (q:draft)
behpa = (t:n) (w:kinsman/relative) (d:beh clan with -pa, a male member of the same clan or family) (e:amah tawh a kinai a ~ hong pai-in) (b:beh) (r:3.25.25/1.14.14) (q:draft)
beka = (t:adv) (w:only/merely) (d:bek only with the ending -a, linking to the following word: pualam beka is only outward) (e:note tung ~ hong tung ahi hiam) (b:bek) (r:46.14.36/45.2.28) (q:draft)
beka = (t:n) (w:beka) (d:measure of weight, half a shekel) (e:mi khat ciangin ~ khat) (r:2.38.26) (q:draft)
biakpih = (t:v) (w:worship/join in worshipping) (d:biak worship with -pih along with: worship, in the verses always the idols or gods of others) (e:amau’ pasiante ka ~ kei ding hi) (b:biak) (r:19.16.4/26.23.7) (q:draft)
biang = (t:n) (w:cheek) (e:ka ~ ciangah ka tawi a) (r:28.11.4/47.11.20) (q:draft)
bukno = (t:n) (w:hut/shelter/booth) (d:buk hut with -no small; galvilna bukno is a watchtower) (e:ama ading ~ khat a lam hi) (b:buk) (r:32.4.5/12.18.8) (q:draft)
bupin = (t:adv) (w:wholly/entirely/as a whole) (d:bup whole with -in; a minam bupin is the whole nation, a bupin hal is burn it whole) (e:A minam ~ Jordan a galkah khit) (b:bup) (r:6.4.1/2.29.18) (q:draft)
ciahsakkik = (t:v) (w:send back/let return/send away) (d:ciahsak send home with kik back, again) (e:a guak ~ uh hi) (b:ciahsak) (r:41.12.3/24.23.3) (q:draft)
ciahto = (t:v) (w:go up/go back up/come up) (d:ciah return with to upward: return or go home to a higher place) (e:Gibeah-a a inn-ah Saul zong ~ hi) (b:ciah) (r:9.15.34/43.6.62) (q:draft)
cialte = (t:n) (w:hired men/mercenaries/hired workers) (d:cial hire with plural -te: those who are hired; galkap cialte are mercenaries) (e:A galkap ~ nangawn amau lakah) (b:cial) (r:24.46.21/40.20.9) (q:draft)
cialte = (t:n) (w:levels/storeys) (d:plural of cial step or level, of the floors of a building) (e:a tunga ~ pen a nuai-ate sangin) (b:cial) (r:26.42.3) (q:draft)
ciangkhutte = (t:n) (w:staffs/rods) (e:Aaron’ ciangkhut in amau’ ~ valh tum hi) (b:ciangkhut) (r:2.7.12/4.17.7) (q:draft)
cici = (t:v) (w:keep saying/say again and again/urge) (d:reduplicated ci say; hong cici kei in is do not keep telling me) (e:nading ahi zongin hong ~ kei in) (r:8.1.16/19.70.4) (q:draft)
cihtaklohna = (t:n) (w:unfaithfulness/faithlessness) (d:not being faithful, to God or to a spouse: cihtak faithful with loh not and -na) (e:Kei tungah na ~ thuneu lua sa a) (r:26.16.20/15.9.4) (q:draft)
cilphuan = (t:n) (w:foam/froth/saliva) (d:foam or running spittle at the mouth; cilphuan bua is to foam at the mouth) (e:a kam sung pan ~ bua a) (r:41.9.18/9.21.13) (q:draft)
cinapa = (t:n) (w:sick man/invalid/patient) (d:cina, sick, with -pa marking a man: the man who is sick) (e:~ in an ne zo lo a) (b:cina) (r:18.33.20/43.5.7) (q:draft)
cisa = (t:n) (w:fever) (d:heat of the body in illness; cisa natna is a fever sickness, cisa-in is feverishly) (e:~ natna kong tung sak ding hi) (r:3.26.16/5.28.22) (q:draft)
cite = (t:n) (w:those who say) (d:ci, say, with plural -te: the people who say something, placed after the words spoken, usually as a cite) (e:a ~ kua ahi hiam) (b:ci) (r:9.11.12/19.70.3) (q:draft)
damdamin = (t:adv) (w:slowly/gradually/little by little) (e:~ kong makaih ding hi) (b:damdam) (r:1.33.14/44.27.7) (q:draft)
damkikzo = (t:v) (w:recover/be able to recover) (d:damkik, get well again, with zo, be able: manage to recover from an illness or injury) (e:na ~ kei ding hi) (b:damkik) (r:12.20.1/12.8.8) (q:draft)
dampah = (t:v) (w:be healed at once/recover immediately) (d:dam, be well, with pah, at once: become well immediately) (e:a naupang thakhatin a ~ hi) (r:40.17.18/40.8.15) (q:draft)
deidan = (t:v) (w:show favoritism/discriminate/be partial) (d:treat people unequally, favouring some over others; mi deidan is to show partiality) (e:Pasian in kuamah ~ loin) (r:45.2.11/59.2.9) (q:draft)
dekdek = (t:adv) (w:almost/nearly/about to) (d:placed after a verb, the action is on the point of happening or has just barely happened) (e:teembaw a kisia ~ hi) (r:32.1.4/24.14.2) (q:draft)
diam = (t:part) (d:sentence-final question word, short for ding hiam: will it be so, would you) (e:na ci lailai ~) (r:26.28.9/19.11.3) (q:draft)
diam = (t:adv) (w:all together) (d:placed after a verb of gathering, the whole group comes together as one) (e:amaute hong kituah ~ uh hi) (r:15.3.1/16.8.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
dikpa = (t:n) (w:innocent man/righteous man/just person) (d:dik, righteous, with -pa marking a man: the one who is in the right, set against mawhpa, the guilty one) (e:a ~ khahin a mawhpa lelsak a) (b:dik) (r:5.25.1/2.23.7) (q:draft)
dimna = (t:n) (w:being full/full of) (d:dim, full, with -na: used as a dimna between a noun and the place it describes, the place where that thing is in plenty, as mihing a dimna khuapi, an inhabited town) (e:mangbuhham a ~ leitang khat om a) (b:dim) (r:13.11.13/26.12.20) (q:draft)
dimtakin = (t:adv) (w:fully/to the full/full) (d:dim, full, with takin: so as to be full, in full measure) (e:ngasa a ~ guang uh ahih manin) (b:dim) (r:42.5.7/20.24.4) (q:draft)
dongsak = (t:v) (w:ask/inquire/have someone ask) (d:dong, ask, with sak: put a question to someone, or send someone to ask on one's behalf) (e:ci-in a ~ uh hi) (b:dong) (r:40.22.17/42.7.20) (q:draft)
donin = (t:v) (w:heed/care for/pay attention to) (d:form of don, heed, with the linking suffix in: heeding or caring for and then going on to the next action) (e:~ ka kem ding hi) (b:don) (r:26.34.12/23.19.22) (q:draft)
gakna = (t:n) (w:band/fastening/waistband) (d:gak, fasten, with -na: the thing used to fasten or bind round, such as a band on a post or the waistband of a garment) (e:ngun tawh kibawl ~ tawh kigak) (b:gak) (r:2.27.17/2.29.5) (q:draft)
galdaihna = (t:n) (w:peace/rest from war) (d:gal, war or enemy, with daihna, calm: freedom from enemies and fighting) (e:ama kiimah ~ pia hi) (r:14.20.30/14.15.15) (q:draft)
gamhluahna = (t:n) (w:inheritance/heritage/property) (d:the land or place that a person or tribe has inherited) (e:amau’ ~ ciatah ciah uh hi) (b:gamhluah) (r:7.21.24/8.4.10) (q:draft)
gamsial = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:wild ox) (d:gam, wild country, with sial, the mithun: a strong wild ox, in older English Bibles the unicorn) (e:~ tha bang hatna nei uh hi) (r:4.23.22/5.33.17) (q:draft)
gamtatsiate = (t:n) (w:evildoers/the wicked) (d:gamtatsia, of bad conduct, with plural -te: people who do evil) (e:Mi ~ ahih leh cithei bek loin) (b:gamtatsia) (r:39.3.15/19.94.4) (q:draft)
gamtatsiate = (t:n) (w:evil deeds/wrongdoings) (d:gamtatsia, bad conduct, with plural -te) (b:gamtatsia) (r:15.9.13) (q:draft, low confidence)
gawng = (t:adj) (w:lean/thin/gaunt) (d:thin from lack of flesh, said of animals and of a wasted body) (e:a gulhgawng bawngpi ~ sagihte) (r:1.41.4/1.41.20) (q:draft)
giatte = (t:num) (w:the eight/eight) (d:giat, eight, with plural -te: the eight persons or things; also ends larger numbers such as sawm-le-giatte, the eighteen) (e:hih mihing ~ nei hi) (b:giat) (r:1.22.23/42.13.4) (q:draft)
hagawi = (t:v) (w:gnash the teeth/grind the teeth) (d:grind the teeth together in pain or in anger) (e:amaute kapin a ~ ding uh hi) (r:40.13.42/25.2.16) (q:draft)
haknaw = (t:n) (w:lead) (d:the heavy soft metal) (e:tui sungah ~ bangin amaute tum uh) (r:2.15.10/4.31.22) (q:draft)
haksate = (t:adj) (w:hard/difficult/harsh) (d:haksa, hard, with plural -te, placed after a plural noun: thudotna haksate, hard questions) (e:thudotna ~ tawh amah a ze-et dingin) (b:haksa) (r:11.10.1/11.12.4) (q:draft)
hanciamte = (t:n) (w:those who strive/those who seek) (d:hanciam, strive, with plural -te: people who make an effort for something, used as a hanciamte) (e:siatna a ~ in siatna mah ngah hi) (b:hanciam) (r:20.11.27/20.11.19) (q:draft)
hawlkhiatsak = (t:v) (w:drive out/cast out for someone) (d:hawlkhiat, drive out, with sak: drive out on behalf of someone, or have something driven out) (e:dawi a ~ nadingin a hong thum hi) (b:hawlkhiat) (r:41.7.26/36.3.15) (q:draft)
hawmguakin = (t:adv) (w:empty/empty-handed/desolate) (d:hawmguak, empty, with -in: in an empty state; khut hawmguakin is empty-handed, and of a land it is left desolate) (e:khut ~ a ciahsak uh hi) (r:42.20.10/23.34.10) (q:draft)
heek = (t:v) (w:wring/twist) (d:twist round with force, as the neck of a bird or of an enemy) (e:a lu ~ ding a) (r:3.5.8/1.49.8) (q:draft)
heek = (t:n) (w:wink) (d:in the compound mit-heek, a wink of the eye; mit-heek pia is to wink at someone) (e:a mit-~ hong pia-in) (r:20.6.13/19.35.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
hehnemin = (t:v) (w:comfort/encourage/console) (d:form of hehnem, comfort, with the linking suffix in: comforting and then going on to the next action) (e:thu hoih tawh note hong ~) (b:hehnem) (r:18.16.5/43.11.31) (q:draft)
heuhna = (t:n) (w:pruning/trimming) (d:heuh, prune, with -na: the cutting back of branches; singhiang heuhna temkawi is a pruning hook or pruning knife) (e:singhiang ~ temkawi tawh a selte atkhia) (r:23.18.5/23.2.4) (q:draft)
hiangpa = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:plane tree/fir) (d:a kind of tree, used in the Bible for the plane tree and the fir; said with kung or sing, tree) (e:~ sing leh taak sing ka suankhawm ding) (r:23.41.19/1.30.37) (q:draft, low confidence)
hilhpa = (t:n) (w:teacher/instructor/speaker) (d:hilh, teach or tell, with -pa marking a man: the man who teaches or tells, used as a hilhpa) (e:a ~ tungah a hoihna a om khempeuh) (b:hilh) (r:48.6.6/46.14.11) (q:draft)
hingkhia = (t:v) (w:give birth/bring forth/deliver) (d:hing, alive, with khia, out: bring a child out alive, be delivered of a child; also used as a figure of speech) (e:zuauthu a ~ hi) (b:hing) (r:19.7.14/23.37.3) (q:draft)
hinglai = (t:adj) (w:still alive/living/surviving) (d:hing, alive, with lai, still: a hinglai mite are the living, those still alive) (e:A ~ mite sangin a si khinsa) (r:21.4.2/5.4.4) (q:draft)
hitaseleh = (t:conj) (w:although/even though/yet) (d:though it is so; after a statement it means although, and tua hitaseleh or tua bang hitaseleh opens a sentence as yet or nevertheless) (e:lampi tom pen ~) (r:2.13.17/43.1.12) (q:draft)
hiuhiau = (t:adv) (w:strikingly/brightly) (d:placed after a describing word such as hoih, beautiful, or san, red, to picture a striking, shining look) (e:Lebanon tausang bangin hoih ~ hi) (r:22.7.4/22.7.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
hoihlamin = (t:adv) (w:favorably/for good/well) (d:hoihlam, the good side, with -in: in a good way, in favour; a hoihlamin gen is to speak favorably) (e:a ~ gen in) (r:11.22.13/47.7.9) (q:draft)
huanna = (t:n) (w:cooking/place for cooking) (d:huan, cook or boil, with -na: the cooking of food; a huanna mun is the place where something is cooked, a huanna anbuk a kitchen) (e:a kipia sate a ~ mun) (r:26.46.20/26.46.24) (q:draft)
huante = (t:n) (w:gardens/groves) (d:huan, garden, with plural -te; oliv huante are olive groves) (e:gun gei-a om ~ tawh kibang hi) (b:huan) (r:4.24.6/30.4.9) (q:draft)
huihnung = (t:n) (w:wind/breeze) (d:huih, wind, with nung, blow: wind that is blowing) (e:~ tawpa a dai pah hi) (r:41.4.39/19.78.39) (q:draft)
huihte = (t:n) (w:winds) (e:Kua in a khut sungah ~ lomcip a) (b:huih) (r:20.30.4/19.104.4) (q:draft)
iikte = (t:n) (w:breasts) (d:iik, the breast of an animal, with plural -te; in the offerings the part that is waved before the Lord) (e:amaute in a ~ tungah koihin) (b:iik) (r:3.9.20/3.9.21) (q:draft)
innkuankuanin = (t:adv) (w:family by family/by families/by clans) (d:innkuankuan, each family in turn, with -in) (e:a beh tawh kizui-in a ~) (b:innkuankuan) (r:4.2.34/4.3.15) (q:draft)
innsate = (t:n) (w:livestock/cattle/domestic animals) (d:innsa, animal kept at the house, with plural -te; set against gamsate, the wild animals) (e:Gamsate leh ~ khempeuh) (b:innsa) (r:19.148.10/1.7.21) (q:draft)
innsungmang = (t:n) (w:court official/eunuch/palace officer) (d:an official who serves inside the royal house, in the Bible often a eunuch) (e:kumpipa’ ~ Hegai’ kep dingin) (r:17.2.3/27.1.3) (q:draft)
innsungmangte = (t:n) (w:court officials/eunuchs/attendants) (e:kumpipa’ ~ hong pai a) (b:innsungmang) (r:17.6.14/17.1.12) (q:draft)
kamsangnu = (t:n) (w:prophetess) (d:kamsang, prophet, with -nu marking a woman) (e:~ Huldah kiangah pai uh hi) (b:kamsang) (r:12.22.14/16.6.14) (q:draft)
kanin = (t:v) (w:search/investigate/seek out) (d:form of kan, search, with the linking suffix in: searching or inquiring into and then going on to the next action) (e:Topa’ thu ~ vak kawikawi ding uh a) (b:kan) (r:30.8.12/7.6.29) (q:draft)
katna = (t:n) (w:burning/fire/flames) (d:kat, burn, with -na: mei katna is the burning of a fire) (e:mei ~ pan a pusuak meikhu) (b:kat) (r:66.18.9/46.3.15) (q:draft)
katna = (t:n) (w:fork/branching/parting) (d:kat, be split, with -na: the place where a road divides in two) (e:Tua lampi a ~ munah ciamtehna khat phut) (b:kat) (r:26.21.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kawngah = (t:n) (w:on the waist/around the waist) (d:kawng, waist, with the place ending -ah: on or round the waist) (e:a ~ puanhampi teng a) (b:kawng) (r:1.37.34/12.1.8) (q:draft)
keelnote = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:young goats/kids) (e:tuunote leh ~ tul sawmthum ciang dong) (b:keelno) (r:14.35.7/1.27.14) (q:draft)
kek = (t:v) (w:draw/bend) (d:pull back a bow ready to shoot) (e:Amah in a thalpi ~ a) (r:25.3.12) (q:draft, low confidence)
kek = (t:adv) (w:apart/to pieces) (d:placed after a verb of cutting, scratching or chasing, the action is carried through with force so as to tear or break up) (e:A khutte uh kui ~ uh a) (r:24.48.37/25.3.66) (q:draft, low confidence)
kek = (t:n) (w:thunderstorm/thunderbolt) (d:seen once, in a phrase for the path of the thunderstorm) (e:~’ lampi ding sialsak ahi hiam) (r:18.38.25) (q:draft, low confidence)
khahkhiatna = (t:n) (w:deliverance/rescue/release) (d:khahkhiat, set free or let go, with -na: the act of setting free; also the sending out of something) (e:note ~ ding thahatna nei lo) (b:khahkhiat) (r:23.50.2/2.18.9) (q:draft)
khalna = (t:n) (w:discipline/correction/chastening) (d:khal, discipline, with -na: the correcting of a person, as a father corrects his son) (e:~ leh hilhnate in nuntak nading lampi) (b:khal) (r:20.6.23/5.8.5) (q:draft)
khalna = (t:n) (w:hardship/affliction/distress) (d:in the compound zawn’ khalna, hardship or suffering that a person goes through, also great poverty) (e:a zawn’ ~ hanga ze-etna tampi) (r:47.8.2/47.12.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
khanghamna = (t:n) (w:old age/age) (d:khangham, old, with -na: the state of being old) (e:mitte a ~ hangin mang a) (b:khangham) (r:1.48.10/18.32.9) (q:draft)
khangkhawm = (t:v) (w:grow up together/grow together) (d:khang, grow, with khawm, together; amah tawh a khangkhawm are those who grew up with him) (e:a nam nihin ~ tadih hen) (b:khang) (r:40.13.30/11.12.8) (q:draft)
khawmte = (t:n) (w:those together with/companions/fellow) (d:khawm, together, with plural -te, placed after a verb: the people who do the action together, as an ne khawmte, those eating together) (e:Amah tawh an ne ~ in) (b:khawm) (r:42.7.49/58.3.14) (q:draft)
khawngah = (t:ppm) (w:on/about on/around) (d:khawng, thereabouts, with the place marker -ah: at or on such places, here and there on, as inn tung khawngah, up on the houses) (e:kulh tung ~ tai zaizai uh hi) (b:khawng) (r:29.2.9/58.11.38) (q:draft)
kheelsak = (t:v) (w:change/transform) (d:kheel, change, with sak: make something change, as when a person is given a new name) (e:a min Zedekiah-in ~ hi) (b:kheel) (r:12.24.17/50.3.21) (q:draft)
khengakna = (t:n) (w:footstool) (d:khe, foot, with ngakna, rest: the place where the feet rest) (e:kham a kibawl ~ khat nei-in) (r:14.9.18/19.99.5) (q:draft)
khente = (t:n) (w:divisions/groups) (d:khen, divide, with plural -te: the groups into which people are divided, as the divisions of the priests or of the army) (e:siampite leh Levi mi a ~) (b:khen) (r:13.28.13/13.27.1) (q:draft)
khialhsak = (t:v) (w:cause to sin/cause to stumble/lead astray) (d:khialh, do wrong, with sak: make someone do wrong) (e:Na khe in hong ~ leh sattan in) (b:khialh) (r:41.9.45/40.5.19) (q:draft)
khialkha = (t:v) (w:sin/err/go astray) (d:khial, do wrong, with kha, happen to: fall into sin or make a mistake, often without meaning to) (e:tua hehna hangin ~ kei unla) (r:49.4.26/21.5.6) (q:draft)
khopna = (t:n) (w:being together/union) (d:khop, together, with -na, placed after a verb: the doing of it together, as kipawl khopna, an alliance, and lup khopna, lying together as man and wife) (e:tua kipawl ~ kip lo ding a) (b:khop) (r:27.11.6/2.21.10) (q:draft)
khopna = (t:n) (w:gathering/collecting) (d:khop, gather, with -na: the gathering in of a harvest) (e:na pawi lohna munah na ~) (b:khop) (r:40.25.24) (q:draft, low confidence)
khua-ul = (t:n) (w:sweat/perspiration) (d:khua-ul kai is to sweat) (e:na maitang-ah ~ tawh an na ne ding) (r:1.3.19/42.22.44) (q:draft)
khuainun = (t:n) (w:wax/beeswax) (d:the wax made by bees, which melts before the fire) (e:mei mai-ah ~ a tui bangin) (r:19.68.2/19.97.5) (q:draft)
khualzinte = (t:n) (w:travelers/wayfarers/strangers) (d:khualzin, travel, with plural -te: people on a journey) (e:Ka inn-ah ~ ka tungsak a) (b:khualzin) (r:18.31.32/7.5.6) (q:draft)
khuavakin = (t:adv) (w:as light/as a light) (d:khuavak, light, with -in: in the form of light) (e:kei ~ leitungah kong pai hi) (b:khuavak) (r:43.12.46/43.3.19) (q:draft)
khuavakin = (t:adv) (w:all night long/through the night) (d:in the phrase zan khuavakin, the whole night through until daylight comes) (e:Amah zan ~ kap a) (b:khuavak) (r:25.1.2/21.10.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
khuhin = (t:v) (w:cover/spread over) (d:form of khuh, cover, with the linking suffix in: covering and then going on to the next action; also catching by covering with a net) (e:tua tungah puan a dum tawh ~) (b:khuh) (r:4.4.6/35.1.15) (q:draft)
khungin = (t:v) (w:lay across/stretch out/set in place) (d:form of khung with the linking suffix in: laying or stretching something long across, such as a beam, a chain or a measuring line) (e:amaute in a zawlte ~ a kongkhakte) (b:khung) (r:16.3.3/23.44.13) (q:draft)
khutdawh = (t:n) (w:alms/begging) (d:what is asked for with the hand held out; khutdawh ngen is to beg) (e:mittaw khat in ~ ngenin lam geiah) (r:42.18.35/44.3.2) (q:draft)
khute = (t:n) (w:smoke/clouds of smoke) (d:khu, smoke, with plural -te: smoke or a rising cloud, as of incense or of dust) (e:paknamtui hal ~ van lamah kahto biaibuai) (b:khu) (r:26.8.11/26.26.10) (q:draft)
khute = (t:n) (w:smoking ones/smoldering) (d:khu, give off smoke, with plural -te: the things that are smoking, used as a khute) (e:sing tumbang nih a ~ tawh kibang) (b:khu) (r:23.7.4) (q:draft, low confidence)
khutmeno = (t:n) (w:little finger/finger) (d:khutme, finger, with no, small: the smallest finger) (e:Ka ~ in ka pa’ kawng sangin) (b:khutme) (r:11.12.10/40.23.4) (q:draft)
khutsiampa = (t:n) (w:craftsman/carpenter/skilled workman) (d:khutsiam, skilled with the hands, with -pa marking a man) (e:~ in a hei tawh milimin a bawl hi) (b:khutsiam) (r:24.10.3/40.13.55) (q:draft)
kibawlin = (t:v) (w:be made/be prepared) (d:form of kibawl, be made, with the linking suffix in: being made, and then going on to what follows) (e:Salem khua sungah ama omna ~) (b:kibawl) (r:19.76.2/2.28.8) (q:draft)
kibawlsak = (t:v) (w:be made for/be prepared for) (d:kibawl, be made, with sak: be made or done on behalf of someone, as atonement made for the people) (e:nangma adingin na suah ni-in hong ~ hi) (b:kibawl) (r:26.28.13/3.16.34) (q:draft)
kibawlsia = (t:v) (w:be persecuted/be mistreated/be harmed) (d:bawlsia, mistreat, with ki-: be treated badly by others) (e:lo dangah nang hong ~ ding hi) (b:bawlsia) (r:8.2.22/40.24.9) (q:draft)
kibawlsia = (t:v) (w:hurt each other/wrong one another) (d:bawlsia, mistreat, with ki- in its sense of each other) (e:khat leh khat na ~ uh hiam) (b:bawlsia) (r:44.7.26) (q:draft)
kibuakna = (t:n) (w:place of pouring out/dump/heap) (d:kibuak, be poured out, with -na: the place where something is poured or thrown out; vut kibuakna is the ash heap) (e:vutte a ~ kuam buppi leh) (b:kibuak) (r:24.31.40/3.4.12) (q:draft)
kidenglum = (t:v) (w:be stoned to death/be stoned) (d:denglum, kill by throwing, with ki-: be killed by having stones thrown) (e:suang tawh amaute ~ ding hi) (b:denglum) (r:3.20.27/2.21.28) (q:draft)
kigal = (t:v) (w:be at enmity/be enemies) (d:be enemies of each other; kigal neihna is enmity or ill will held against someone) (e:a vengpa tawh ~ neihna nei lo) (b:gal) (r:5.19.6/5.19.5) (q:draft)
kigal = (t:adv) (w:opposite/facing each other) (d:across from one another; kigal sai is to stand or be placed facing each other) (e:amaute tawh ~ sai-in nasem uh hi) (r:16.12.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
kigelhte = (t:n) (w:writings/things written/engravings) (d:what is written or engraved, kigelh with plural -te used as a noun) (e:Moses’ thukham laibu sunga ~ khempeuh) (b:kigelh) (r:6.23.6/2.32.16) (q:draft)
kigual = (t:v) (w:line up/be arrayed/draw up in ranks) (d:stand in rows, as an army drawn up for battle or people walking in procession; kigual deudau is in long lines) (e:Filistia mite ~ uh a) (b:gual) (r:9.4.2/19.55.18) (q:draft)
kihanthawnin = (t:v) (w:taking courage/encouraging oneself/encouraging one another) (d:form of kihanthawn with -in, leading on to the next action) (e:Israel mite ~ a ni masa) (b:kihanthawn) (r:7.20.22/14.25.11) (q:draft)
kihelin = (t:v) (w:mingling/joining/being included) (d:form of kihel with -in; with tawh it is mixing with or joining someone) (e:Minam dangte tawh ~) (b:kihel) (r:19.106.35/18.2.1) (q:draft)
kihing = (t:v) (w:be kept alive/be made alive) (d:passive of hing; kihing khawi is to be spared and allowed to live, kihing kiksak is to be raised to life again) (e:a ni thum ni-in ~ kiksak ding hi) (b:hing) (r:40.17.23/2.19.13) (q:draft)
kihongin = (t:v) (w:opening/being opened) (d:form of kihong with -in, followed by what happens next) (e:lei ~ Dathan valhtum a) (b:kihong) (r:19.106.17/41.7.35) (q:draft)
kihtaktak = (t:v) (w:dread/fear greatly) (d:kihtak with its last syllable repeated; a kihtaktak is the very thing that someone fears) (e:na ~ uh namsau in Izipt gamah) (b:kihtak) (r:24.42.16/20.10.24) (q:draft)
kihuan = (t:v) (w:be cooked/be boiled) (d:passive of huan, to cook; before a noun it means cooked, as in a kihuan an, cooked food) (e:tau beel tawh a ~ ahih leh) (r:3.6.28/3.2.7) (q:draft)
kihuhna = (t:n) (w:help/aid/mutual help) (d:help that is given to someone, or helping one another) (e:tung panin eite hong ~ hong pai hi) (b:huhna) (r:19.124.8/49.4.2) (q:draft)
kikheem = (t:v) (w:be deceived/deceive oneself) (e:Na ~ kei un) (b:kheem) (r:46.15.33/62.1.8) (q:draft)
kikhopnate = (t:n) (w:assemblies/meetings/convocations) (e:a siangtho biak ~ ahi hi) (b:kikhopna) (r:3.23.4/23.1.13) (q:draft)
kikhuhna = (t:n) (w:covering/veil) (d:something to cover oneself with; kikhuhna puan is a veil or shawl) (e:a ~ puan la-in kikhuh hi) (b:kikhuh) (r:1.24.65/1.38.19) (q:draft)
kilahna = (t:n) (w:appearing/showing/manifestation) (d:the act of showing oneself or of being shown; kilahna mun is the place where someone appeared, and lim kilahna is an example shown to others) (e:David tungah Topa a ~ mun) (b:kilah) (r:14.3.1/46.10.6) (q:draft)
kilhna = (t:n) (w:clasp/hook/fastener) (d:a small hook or pin that holds two pieces together) (e:kham ~ sawmnga bawlin) (r:2.36.13/2.26.6) (q:draft)
kiliahna = (t:n) (w:veil/covering/screen) (d:something that screens or hides; kiliahna puan is a veil over the face) (e:~ puan tawh a maitang khuhkik hi) (b:kiliah) (r:2.34.35/2.34.33) (q:draft)
kilkel = (t:adv) (d:intensifier after a descriptive word, with the sense of clear, fresh or gleaming: vot kilkel is cool and clear, hing kilkel is fresh and green, kipuah kilkel is polished bright) (e:a vot ~ luite kang ngei) (r:24.18.14/23.66.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
kilui = (t:v) (w:be served/be set before) (d:of food, be laid out in front of someone to eat) (e:nek dingin a mai-ah an ~ hi) (r:1.24.33/46.10.27) (q:draft)
kimante = (t:n) (w:captives/those captured/prisoners) (d:those who have been taken, kiman with plural -te; sal-a kimante are people taken captive, and after a battle it is also the plunder taken) (e:sal-a a ~ tungah suahtakna thu) (b:kiman) (r:23.61.1/4.31.27) (q:draft)
kimatna = (t:n) (w:capture/arrest/seizure) (d:the fact of being caught or taken) (e:Johan’ ~ thu Zeisu in a zak ciangin) (b:kimat) (r:40.4.12/9.4.19) (q:draft)
kinawhin = (t:adv) (w:quickly/in haste/hurriedly) (d:form of kinawh with -in, hurrying to do the next action) (e:Tua ciangin Abigail ~) (b:kinawh) (r:9.25.18/19.119.60) (q:draft)
kinawtngil = (t:adj) (w:polished/burnished) (d:rubbed until it shines, said of metal) (e:a ~ sumngo tawh kibang uh hi) (r:26.1.7/23.49.2) (q:draft)
kingai = (t:v) (w:be betrothed/be lovers/court) (d:love each other as man and woman, be promised to each other in marriage; with tawh for the partner) (e:Mari in Josef tawh ~ a) (r:40.1.18/24.3.1) (q:draft)
kingai = (t:v) (w:be heard/be listened to) (d:passive of ngai, listen) (e:na thungetna uh hong ~ ding) (b:ngai) (r:23.58.4) (q:draft)
kingaihna = (t:n) (w:love/courtship) (d:the love of a man and a woman for each other) (e:nungak leh tangval a ~ zia) (r:20.30.19/22.2.7) (q:draft)
kingaihsunin = (t:v) (w:considering oneself/thinking oneself) (d:form of kingaihsun with -in; after a phrase with bangin or -in it is regarding oneself as such) (e:Pasian tawh a kikim bangin ~) (b:kingaihsun) (r:41.2.7/19.49.18) (q:draft)
kingaihsunin = (t:v) (w:being remembered/being called to mind) (e:mawhnate kum simin ~ a om hi) (b:kingaihsun) (r:58.10.3) (q:draft, low confidence)
kiniamsak = (t:v) (w:humble oneself/submit/be humble) (d:make oneself low before another) (e:ama khut vanglian nuai-ah na ~ un) (b:niamsak) (r:60.5.6/49.5.21) (q:draft)
kiniamsakna = (t:n) (w:humility/lowliness/humiliation) (e:Na khempeuh panin ~ tawh) (b:kiniamsak) (r:49.4.2/59.1.10) (q:draft)
kipakta = (t:v) (w:be approved/be honoured/be esteemed) (d:be well regarded by others, passive of pakta) (e:ama gamah ~ ngei lo hi) (b:pakta) (r:43.4.44/47.10.18) (q:draft)
kiphumna = (t:n) (w:burial/grave) (d:being buried; kiphumna mun and kiphumna hankhuk are the place where someone is buried) (e:amah a ~ mun kuamah in thei lo hi) (b:kiphum) (r:5.34.6/26.37.13) (q:draft)
kiphumna = (t:n) (w:plunging in/meddling) (d:throwing oneself into something, such as a quarrel of other people) (e:lo kitotna sunga va ~ in) (b:kiphum) (r:20.26.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
kipiasa = (t:v) (w:given/already given) (d:kipia with -sa for a completed action; what has been given, often before a noun) (e:hong ~ bek ahih manin) (b:kipia) (r:46.4.7/3.10.17) (q:draft)
kisamkhia = (t:v) (w:be summoned/be called out/be called up) (d:be called to come out and gather, as men for war) (e:a zui dingin Abiezer mite ~ hi) (b:kisam) (r:7.6.34/9.13.4) (q:draft)
kisehkhia = (t:v) (w:be set apart/be measured off/be allotted) (d:of land or a share, be marked off from the rest for a purpose) (e:Hih a ~ mun sung teng pen) (b:kiseh) (r:26.45.4/26.45.3) (q:draft)
kiselna = (t:n) (w:dispute/argument/strife) (d:arguing against one another; kam kiselna is a quarrel in words) (e:nungzuite lakah ~ khat hong om hi) (b:kisel) (r:42.9.46/19.55.9) (q:draft)
kisiansak = (t:v) (w:purify oneself/be cleansed/be pronounced clean) (d:make oneself or be made ritually clean) (e:amah a ~ khit ciangin) (b:siansak) (r:3.13.35/4.19.12) (q:draft)
kisiansak = (t:v) (w:be refined) (d:of silver or gold, be made pure in the furnace) (e:meikhukah ngun a ~ bangin) (b:siansak) (r:38.13.9/23.48.10) (q:draft)
kisiansuahna = (t:n) (w:purification/ceremonial cleansing) (d:the act or rite of making oneself ritually clean) (e:Amah in ~ ni a cin mateng) (b:kisiansuah) (r:3.12.4/44.21.26) (q:draft)
kisuahtak = (t:v) (w:escape/get away/save oneself) (d:form of suahtak with ki-, often before thei or zo, be able to escape) (e:a tai hatte nangawn ~ zo lo ding a) (b:suahtak) (r:30.2.15/24.51.6) (q:draft)
kisui = (t:v) (w:be carved/be hewn/be graven) (d:shaped by cutting; a kisui milim is a carved image, named beside a kisung milim, a cast image) (e:A ~ milimte muangin) (b:sui) (r:23.42.17/19.144.12) (q:draft)
kisuzan = (t:v) (w:be broken in pieces/be crushed/be shattered) (d:passive of suzan; of olives, be pressed or beaten for oil) (e:a biak milim ~ ding hi) (r:28.8.6/2.27.20) (q:draft)
kitanin = (t:v) (w:being broken off/being cut off/snapping) (d:form of kitan with -in, followed by the result, as in kitanin kia, break off and fall) (e:a ngawng ~ si hi) (b:kitan) (r:9.4.18/30.3.14) (q:draft)
kitawh = (t:v) (w:be kindled/be lit) (d:of fire or anger, be set alight; kitawh kuang is be kindled and burn) (e:ka hehna ~ kuang a) (b:tawh) (r:24.15.14/24.17.4) (q:draft)
kitawh = (t:v) (w:be dug/be dug out/be quarried) (d:of a pit, be dug; kitawh khiatna is the place something is dug out from, a mine or quarry) (e:Ngun a ~ khiatna ngunkhuk om a) (r:18.28.1/19.94.12) (q:draft)
kitawito = (t:v) (w:be raised up/be elevated/be held high) (d:be built up or lifted higher than what is around, said of a base, a terrace or the head) (e:Biakinn kimkot teng a lei ~ a) (b:kitawi) (r:26.41.8/22.7.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
kitengsak = (t:v) (w:give in marriage/marry off/be given in marriage) (d:cause two people to marry; with tawh for the partner) (e:amau’ tapate tawh ~ kei un) (b:kiteng) (r:15.9.10/1.38.14) (q:draft)
kithatte = (t:n) (w:the slain/those killed) (d:people who have been killed, kithat with plural -te used as a noun) (e:Gal sunga a ~ tawh si khawm ding) (b:kithat) (r:26.32.20/13.10.8) (q:draft)
kituancil = (t:v) (w:be trampled/be trodden underfoot) (e:tua kumpi lukhu ~ ding hi) (b:tuancil) (r:23.28.3/23.5.5) (q:draft)
kiuh = (t:v) (w:knock) (d:form of kiu used before ciangin, leh and similar words) (e:Piter in kong a ~ ciangin) (b:kiu) (r:44.12.13/40.7.7) (q:draft)
kiveii = (t:v) (w:be waved) (d:passive of veii; a kiveii sa-iik is the breast that was waved before the Lord as an offering) (e:a ~ sa-iik leh a taklam phei) (b:veii) (r:4.18.18/4.6.20) (q:draft)
kizal = (t:v) (w:be spread out/be outstretched) (d:of wings or a covering, stretched out wide; a kizal is also a thing spread overhead, a canopy) (e:kherubte’ khate ~ a) (b:zal) (r:11.6.27/23.8.8) (q:draft)
kizat = (t:v) (w:be used) (d:form of kizang used before nading, ciangin and similar words; kizat nading is what a thing is to be used for) (e:sisan a ~ ciangin thu suak thei pan) (b:zat) (r:58.9.18/23.54.16) (q:draft)
kizatna = (t:n) (w:use/usage) (d:the use made of something, or the thing in which a material is used) (e:savun a ~ na khatpeuh peuh tungah) (b:kizat) (r:3.13.51/18.4.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
kizeel = (t:v) (w:spread/spread abroad) (d:of news or a smell, go out over a whole area) (e:ka paknamtui hong ~ hi) (r:22.1.12/41.1.28) (q:draft)
kolh = (t:adj) (w:bald/bare) (d:bare of hair or of growth; tal kolh is a bald forehead and mual kolh a bare hilltop; of plants or forest it is stripped bare) (e:amah a tal ~ hi a) (r:3.13.41/23.13.2) (q:draft)
kongte = (t:n) (w:doors/doorways/gates) (e:na ~ uh khak un) (b:kong) (r:23.26.20/19.78.23) (q:draft)
kuahawm = (t:n) (w:pit/den/cave) (d:a hollow in the ground or in rock; kuahawm thukpi, the very deep pit, is the Abyss) (e:~ thukpi sung panin a hong paikhia) (r:66.11.7/19.10.9) (q:draft)
kuamsung = (t:n) (w:valley/plain) (d:the inside of a valley, low ground between hills, set against mualtung, the hilltop) (e:Refaim ~ dim uh hi) (r:10.5.18/11.20.28) (q:draft)
kuansuk = (t:v) (w:go down/come down/march down) (d:kuan, set out, with suk, downward; often of going down to battle) (e:Jehoshafat Kuam-ah hong ~ uh hen) (b:kuan) (r:29.3.12/7.7.24) (q:draft)
kumkumin = (t:adv) (w:yearly/year after year/annually) (d:usually as a kumkumin, every year) (e:A ~ Adar kha ni sawm le li) (r:17.9.21/9.1.7) (q:draft)
kumsim = (t:adj) (w:annual/yearly) (d:kum, year, with sim, every; placed before the noun, as in kumsim pawi, the yearly feast) (e:Topa ading ~ pawi khamna om hi) (r:7.21.19/9.20.6) (q:draft)
lahsa = (t:v) (w:shown/have shown) (d:lah with -sa for a completed action; before a noun, that which was shown) (e:Topa in Moses tungah a ~ lim tawh) (b:lah) (r:4.8.4/58.8.5) (q:draft)
lakpa = (t:n) (w:one who shows) (d:the one who shows, lak with -pa marking a male person; lam a lakpa, one who shows the way, is a guide or adviser) (e:itna kip a ~ ka hi hi) (r:5.5.10/11.4.5) (q:draft)
lamlakte = (t:n) (w:advisers/counsellors/guides) (d:those who show the way, lamlak with plural -te; thu lamlakte are advisers) (e:a thu ~ in) (b:lamlak) (r:15.7.15/23.19.11) (q:draft)
langnih = (t:n) (w:both sides/two sides) (d:lang, side, with nih, two; langnih a hiam is sharp on both sides, double-edged; of a pair, as feet or parties, it means both) (e:~ a hiam namsau khat) (r:66.1.16/10.9.13) (q:draft)
langpanin = (t:v) (w:opposing/against/defying) (d:form of langpan with -in; after its object it can be translated against) (e:Saul in Topa’ nungzuite ~ tawng a) (b:langpan) (r:44.9.1/24.48.26) (q:draft)
lawhte = (t:n) (w:tenants/hired workers) (d:in lo khawh lawhte, those who work the field of another) (e:Tua lo khawh ~ in a nasemte) (r:40.21.35/40.21.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
lawhte = (t:n) (w:baskets) (d:lawh, a basket or measure of grain, with plural -te) (e:Na ~ uh leh na annel meekna) (r:5.28.17) (q:draft, low confidence)
lawpin = (t:v) (w:hoping/in hope/expecting) (d:form of lawp with -in; looking forward eagerly to something) (e:ci-in ~ ka om hi) (b:lawp) (r:46.16.11/45.12.12) (q:draft)
leengla = (t:n) (w:guest/visitor) (d:often paired as zin le leengla, guests and strangers; zin le leengla do is to show hospitality) (e:zin le ~ do a siam mi) (r:54.3.2/40.22.10) (q:draft)
leilam = (t:adv) (w:toward the ground/to the ground/downward) (d:lei, ground, with lam, direction; with ngat, as in a mai leilam ngatin, with the face to the ground) (e:a mai ~ ngatin David tungah) (r:13.21.21/11.18.39) (q:draft)
leipi = (t:n) (w:earth/the whole earth) (d:lei, earth, with -pi, great; paired with vanpi, the heavens) (e:vanpi leh ~ liing damdam hi) (b:lei) (r:29.3.16/37.2.6) (q:draft)
leizangah = (t:adv) (w:on the plains/in the plain) (d:leizang with -ah, at or in) (e:Jordan kiang Moab ~ Topa in) (b:leizang) (r:4.33.50/4.33.48) (q:draft)
lenggah = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:grape) (d:shorter spelling of leenggah; lenggah lo is a vineyard) (e:a lote uhah ~ a om nawn kei) (r:24.8.13/24.12.10) (q:draft)
liamte = (t:n) (w:the wounded/the injured) (d:those who are wounded, liam with plural -te used as a noun) (e:a ~ a liamna tuamsakin) (b:liam) (r:26.34.16/24.51.52) (q:draft)
liimah = (t:adv) (w:in the shadow/in the shade) (d:liim, shadow, with -ah, in or at; inn liimah is at the porch or gateway of a house) (e:na kha ~ kong bu ding hi) (b:liim) (r:19.57.1/40.26.71) (q:draft)
limcipen = (t:adj) (w:best/choicest/fattest) (d:limci with -pen, most; said of the finest animals or produce) (e:i bawngno ~ hong go unla) (b:limci) (r:42.15.23/9.15.15) (q:draft)
lingnei = (t:adj) (w:thorny/barbed/spiked) (d:ling, thorn, with nei, have; ciang lingnei is a rod with spikes, the scorpions of 1 Kings 12, and teipi lingnei is a barbed spear) (e:keimah in ciang ~ tawh note kong thuhilh) (r:11.12.11/18.41.7) (q:draft)
lingsak = (t:v) (w:shake/make tremble/cause to quake) (d:liing, tremble, with -sak, cause) (e:Pasian in mualte ~ a) (r:18.9.5/19.60.2) (q:draft)
liveina = (t:n) (w:fourth time) (d:li, four, with vei, time, and -na; a liveina hangin is for the fourth time, for the fourth offence) (e:a ~ hangin pel loin amaute gim) (r:30.1.13/30.2.1) (q:draft)
lohkik = (t:v) (w:repay/pay back) (d:loh, pay, with kik, back) (e:Topa in a cingin amaute tungah ~ ding hi) (b:loh) (r:20.19.17/19.37.21) (q:draft)
lompi = (t:n) (w:heap/mass/pile) (d:lom, a lump or heap, with -pi, great: a large heap or the whole mass, as of dough, water, smoke or stones) (e:a tungah suangtum ~ ciang uh a) (b:lom) (r:6.8.29/45.11.16) (q:draft)
luate = (t:n) (d:lua, too or very, with plural -te; after a descriptive word it means those that are too much so, as in a hat luate, those who are too strong, and a tom luate, those that are too short) (e:ama adinga a hat ~ kiang panin) (b:lua) (r:19.35.10/3.22.23) (q:draft, low confidence)
lungdamte = (t:n) (w:those who rejoice/the joyful) (d:lungdam with plural -te used as a noun) (e:Mi ~ tawh kibangin na lungdam khawm un) (b:lungdam) (r:45.12.15/46.7.30) (q:draft)
lungkiasak = (t:v) (w:discourage/dishearten) (d:lungkia, lose heart, with -sak, cause) (e:ka sanggamte in mite ~ uh) (b:lungkia) (r:6.14.8/4.32.7) (q:draft)
lungli = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:poplar/balsam tree/mulberry tree) (d:a kind of tree, named with kung as lungli kung; English versions differ on which tree is meant) (e:~ kungte gal panin amaute hih in) (r:10.5.23/13.14.14) (q:draft)
lungtom = (t:adj) (w:short-tempered/impatient/quick-tempered) (d:lung heart with tom short; easily angered or losing patience) (e:a ~ mite tawh kikhawl kei in) (r:20.22.24/18.21.4) (q:draft)
maisiat = (t:v) (w:set the face against/turn against/oppose) (d:show displeasure toward someone, said of God turning against a wrongdoer) (e:tua mipa ka ~ ding a) (r:3.20.3/3.26.17) (q:draft)
mangbuhte = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:wheat/grain) (d:wheat as a crop or as a stock of grain, with the plural ending te) (e:a sunga ~ a lawnkhia uh hi) (b:mangbuh) (r:44.27.38/23.28.25) (q:draft)
manmanin = (t:adv) (w:regularly/at the proper time/continually) (d:at every set time without a break, as of daily meals or regular offerings) (e:a ~ an ne hi) (r:12.25.29/12.25.30) (q:draft)
manthan = (t:v) (w:vanish/disappear/pass away) (d:form of mangthang used before another word, as in a manthan bangin, as it vanishes) (e:Ka ~ hun matengin) (r:19.39.13/18.7.9) (q:draft)
mapai = (t:v) (w:go ahead/go before/go in advance) (d:ma before with pai go; go ahead of someone else) (e:Saul mai-ah na ~ uh hi) (r:9.23.24/12.4.31) (q:draft)
mapite = (t:n) (w:overseers/foremen/leaders) (d:those who stand in front and direct the work of others; nasem mapite, foremen over the workers) (e:nasem ukte leh nasem ~ paikhia-in) (b:mapi) (r:2.5.10/2.5.6) (q:draft)
mate = (t:n) (w:wounds/injuries) (d:ma wound with the plural ending te; also of breaks or cracks in the ground) (e:amah a liamsakna ~ Jezre-el ah) (r:12.8.29/19.60.2) (q:draft)
mate = (t:n) (d:those who divorce, from ma divorce or send away a spouse, with the plural ending te) (e:zi a ~ in midang tawh) (r:40.5.32) (q:draft, low confidence)
meeng = (t:v) (w:sprout/bud/put out shoots) (d:of a tree or branch, to come out with new tender growth) (e:Theikung a hiang ~ a) (r:41.13.28/28.14.6) (q:draft)
meetna = (t:n) (w:gain/profit/benefit) (d:what one gets out of something, in the verses often dishonest gain) (e:~ lamah kihei uh hi) (b:meet) (r:9.8.3/1.37.26) (q:draft)
milipun = (t:pron) (w:each one/every one/all of them) (d:milip everyone with the plural ending un; usually a milipun, each and every one of them) (e:a ~ a paknamtui beel ciat uh) (b:milip) (r:4.16.18/1.42.35) (q:draft)
minsia = (t:n) (w:bad name/disgrace/ill repute) (d:min name with sia bad; minsia tun is to bring a bad name on someone and minsia sak is to disgrace) (e:Israel nungak tungah ~ tun’ hi) (r:5.22.19/19.40.14) (q:draft)
mohphengte = (t:n) (w:thin cakes/wafers/flat loaves) (d:thin flat cakes of bread, moh being a cake or loaf) (e:a bawlsa ~ la-in inndei sung) (b:mohpheng) (r:10.13.10/2.29.2) (q:draft)
mote = (t:n) (w:daughters-in-law) (d:women married into a family, the wives of the sons) (e:~ in a teeknu uh lang neih) (b:mo) (r:33.7.6/28.4.14) (q:draft)
mualdawn = (t:n) (w:hilltop/mountain top/high place) (d:mual hill with dawn top; also the high places where offerings were made) (e:tua hunin Gibeon ~ ah om lai hi) (r:13.21.29/2.34.2) (q:draft)
mualneute = (t:n) (w:hills/small hills) (d:the lower hills, set beside mualliante the great mountains) (e:~ tuuno bangin a diang uh hi) (r:19.114.4/24.4.24) (q:draft)
musanete = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:vultures/eagles) (d:large birds that gather to feed on dead bodies) (e:Sapul omna peuhah ~ hong kikhawm ding) (b:musane) (r:40.24.28/20.30.17) (q:draft)
muthei = (t:v) (w:be able to see/can see/see) (d:mu see with thei can; khua muthei is to have sight) (e:thakhatin khua ~ pah a) (b:mu) (r:42.18.43/44.22.13) (q:draft)
naina = (t:n) (w:nearness/approach) (d:the fact of being near or having come close, said of a time or an event) (e:amau adingin siatna a ~ thu thei lo) (r:7.20.34/26.12.23) (q:draft)
nainai = (t:adv) (w:closer and closer/more and more) (d:placed after a verb to show an action that presses in or keeps building up) (e:Mi tampi in kei hong langpan’ ~ hi) (r:19.3.1/24.12.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
nakbah = (t:n) (w:nose ring/ring) (d:nak nose with bah ring; an ornament worn in the nose) (e:a nak tungah ~ ka batsak a) (r:1.24.47/20.11.22) (q:draft)
namkhat = (t:n) (w:one nation/a nation/one people) (d:nam nation with khat one; namkhat leh namkhat, nation against nation) (e:Mi ~ leh ~) (r:42.21.10/41.13.8) (q:draft)
namkhat = (t:n) (w:one kind/a kind/one sort) (d:nam kind with khat one, said of each kind in a list) (e:Mihing’ sa ~, ganhing’ sa ~) (r:46.15.39) (q:draft)
namtuam = (t:adj) (w:different kind/foreign/strange) (d:nam kind with tuam different; pau namtuam is another kind of speech, a tongue not understood by the hearers) (e:Pau ~ tawh thu ka nget leh) (r:46.14.14/46.14.13) (q:draft)
namtuite = (t:adj) (w:fragrant/sweet-smelling) (d:namtui with the plural ending te, placed after a noun; sing namtuite fragrant plants or spices, gim namtuite pleasing aromas) (e:henna leh nard sing ~ a po hi) (b:namtui) (r:22.4.13/3.26.31) (q:draft)
nangawnun = (t:adv) (w:even) (d:nangawn even with the plural ending un, stressing an extreme or unexpected case) (e:gimna a thuak ciang ~ ama huh) (b:nangawn) (r:18.36.13/5.23.3) (q:draft)
nasa = (t:part) (d:the endings na and sa together on a verb, written after an apostrophe or hyphen, marking the place where something was or was done before; teen’nasa mun, the place once lived in) (e:a teen’~ mun-ah ama gui zom ding) (r:18.18.19/6.4.9) (q:draft)
nausuah = (t:v) (w:give birth/bear a child) (d:nau child with suah bring out; also names childbirth, as in nausuah natna, birth pains) (e:a ~ ding hun hong tung hi) (r:42.2.6/66.12.2) (q:draft)
nautang = (t:n) (w:common people/lay people/ordinary people) (d:used after mi as mi nautang, the people at large as distinct from priests and leaders) (e:mi ~ khempeuh kiangah tuate manlang takin) (r:14.35.13/16.5.1) (q:draft)
nawkgawp = (t:v) (w:batter/beat against/lash) (d:nawk strike against with gawp violently, said of wind and flood) (e:tua inn a ~ uh hangin) (b:nawk) (r:40.7.25/18.40.23) (q:draft)
neihsateng = (t:n) (w:all possessions/all one has/whole property) (d:neihsa possessions with teng all) (e:a ~ a uk dingin) (b:neihsa) (r:42.16.1/31.1.11) (q:draft)
neisa = (t:adj) (w:having/possessing) (d:nei have with sa already; pasal neisa numei is a woman who has a husband, zi neisa a man who has a wife) (e:pasal ~ numei khatpeuh hangin) (b:nei) (r:3.21.4/2.21.3) (q:draft)
neizaw = (t:v) (w:have more/have greater) (d:nei have with zaw more, used with sangin than) (e:vangliatna a ~ ding hi) (b:nei) (r:47.3.11/10.19.43) (q:draft)
nel = (t:adj) (w:fine/powdery/smooth) (d:ground or rubbed fine, as dust or flour) (e:Izipt gam khempeuhah leivui ~ suakin) (r:2.9.9/23.41.7) (q:draft)
nel = (t:n) (w:flour/fine flour) (d:finely ground grain, as in mangbuh nel wheat flour and an nel) (e:mangbuh ~ tawh na bawl ding hi) (r:2.29.2/2.29.40) (q:draft, low confidence)
neusak = (t:v) (w:make small/humble/bring low) (d:neu small with sak cause; lessen in number or in standing) (e:minamte lakah note kong ~ ding a) (b:neu) (r:31.1.2/27.4.37) (q:draft)
ngaihsutte = (t:n) (d:those who think of or regard something in a certain way; a thupi ngaihsutte, those who regard something as important) (e:Mawkna milim a thupi ~ na mudah hi) (b:ngaihsut) (r:19.31.6) (q:draft)
ngaihsutte = (t:n) (d:the things that people think or take to be so) (e:ci-in a ~ pen sihna lampi) (b:ngaihsut) (r:20.14.12/46.3.19) (q:draft)
ngaihte = (t:n) (w:lovers/beloved ones) (d:used after lawm friend as lawm ngaihte, lovers, also said of allies) (e:Na lawm ~ in nang hong paaikhia uh) (b:ngaih) (r:24.4.30/26.23.5) (q:draft)
ngakte = (t:n) (w:those who wait/those who hope) (d:people who wait for someone or put their hope in him) (e:Topa a ~ in leitung luah ding) (b:ngak) (r:19.37.9/19.25.3) (q:draft)
ngeekte = (t:adj) (w:tender/newborn/very young) (d:with the plural ending te, of what is very young and soft; ta ngeekte newborn babies, lopa ngeekte tender grass) (e:a ta ~ uh a sih nadingin) (b:ngeek) (r:44.7.19/23.37.26) (q:draft)
niamte = (t:adj) (w:lowly/humble/low) (d:with the plural ending te; mi niamte, the humble or lowly people) (e:Amah in mi ~ sangkoih a) (b:niam) (r:18.5.11/10.22.28) (q:draft)
ninbulomtang = (t:n) (w:heap of rubble/heap of ruins/rubbish heap) (d:what is left of a destroyed town or house) (e:a sawt loin ~ suak ding hi) (r:18.15.28/23.17.1) (q:draft)
nuama = (t:v) (w:wanting/wishing) (d:nuam want with the linking ending a, joined to the verb before it; that nuama, wanting to kill) (e:Naupang that ~ a zongte) (b:nuam) (r:40.2.20) (q:draft)
nuama = (t:adj) (w:at ease/comfortable/pleasant) (d:nuam with the linking ending a, describing how one lives) (e:Zion-ah nuntak ~ a om hithiat) (b:nuam) (r:30.6.1) (q:draft, low confidence)
nuama = (t:adj) (d:second part of thu-nuama, of fellowship or peace, as in thu-nuama biakna the fellowship offering) (e:meihal biaknate leh thu-~ biaknate a piak) (b:nuam) (r:13.16.2/14.29.35) (q:draft)
nuamah = (t:adj) (w:pleasant/good/level) (d:nuam pleasant with the place marker ah; gam nuamah in the pleasant land, lam nuamah on an easy path) (e:gam ~ teeng in la thumanin) (b:nuam) (r:19.37.3/24.31.9) (q:draft)
nuamzaw = (t:v) (w:prefer/would rather) (d:nuam want with zaw more, used with sangin than) (e:ka thuak sangin ka si ~ hi) (b:nuam) (r:18.7.15/19.84.10) (q:draft)
nuamzaw = (t:adj) (w:better/more pleasant/more comfortable) (d:nuam pleasant with zaw more) (e:ka om sangin ama kiang ~ ding hi) (b:nuam) (r:28.2.7) (q:draft)
nungakin = (t:adv) (w:as a young woman/as a maiden) (d:nungak young unmarried woman with the ending in, telling the state someone is in; nungakin a om, while still an unmarried girl) (e:a pa inn sungah ~ a om) (b:nungak) (r:4.30.16/26.23.21) (q:draft)
nunungte = (t:n) (w:the last/last ones) (d:those who come last; also after a noun, as in kam nunungte, last words) (e:A tum ~ in nai khat bek) (b:nunung) (r:40.20.12/10.23.1) (q:draft)
nusiate = (t:n) (w:those who forsake/those who leave) (d:people who have left or abandoned someone or something) (e:Topa a ~ pen kibeimangsak ding hi) (b:nusia) (r:23.1.28/40.19.29) (q:draft)
ok = (t:v) (w:wear around the neck/hang around the neck/bind on) (d:put something on the neck as a chain or necklace) (e:na ngawng-ah tuate ~ in) (r:20.3.3/19.73.6) (q:draft)
omnasa = (t:n) (w:former place/former site) (d:the place where someone or something was before; often followed by mun place) (e:a puanbuk ~ mun Bethel le Ai) (b:om) (r:1.13.3/24.30.18) (q:draft)
paatsa = (t:adj) (w:worn-out/old/tattered) (d:of sacks, wineskins, sandals and clothes that are old and falling apart) (e:a ~ puante tawh pai uh hi) (b:paat) (r:6.9.5/6.9.4) (q:draft)
paipah = (t:v) (w:go at once/hurry/go quickly) (d:pai go with pah at once) (e:humpinelkai kikhumna-ah a va ~ hi) (r:27.6.19/42.1.39) (q:draft)
paisuaksak = (t:v) (w:let through/make pass through/let pass) (d:paisuak go right through with sak cause or allow) (e:mong khat dongin a zawl laita ~ hi) (b:paisuak) (r:2.36.33/16.2.7) (q:draft)
paisuaksak = (t:v) (w:make continue/make last) (d:paisuak in its sense of going on without end, with sak cause; keep someone in a state for good) (e:khang tawntungin siampi hi ~ ding hi) (b:paisuak) (r:2.40.15/58.10.14) (q:draft, low confidence)
paisukte = (t:n) (w:those who go down) (d:often of the dead who go down to the pit) (e:Leihawm sunga ~ tawh a kibang) (b:paisuk) (r:19.28.1/23.14.19) (q:draft)
paitohna = (t:n) (w:ascent/way up/going up) (d:the act of going up or the place where one goes up; Bethhoron paitohna lampi, the road going up to Beth Horon) (e:Bethhoron ~ lampi-ah amaute delhin) (b:paitoh) (r:6.10.10/19.122.3) (q:draft)
paukhia = (t:v) (w:speak out/speak up/utter) (d:pau speak with khia out; break silence and say something aloud) (e:Tua ciangin ka ~ a) (b:pau) (r:19.39.3/19.50.1) (q:draft)
paunakte = (t:n) (w:proverbs/sayings) (e:Israel kumpi Solomon’ ~) (b:paunak) (r:20.1.1/20.1.6) (q:draft)
peemte = (t:n) (w:foreigners/sojourners/resident aliens) (d:used after mi as mi peemte, people who have moved in and live in a land not their own) (e:Izipt gamah mi ~ na hi uh hi) (b:peem) (r:5.10.19/5.10.18) (q:draft)
peisan = (t:v) (w:shake at/toss at/wag at) (d:used with lu head; lu peisan is to shake or toss the head at someone in scorn) (e:a lu hong ~ uh hi) (b:pei) (r:19.22.7/12.19.21) (q:draft)
phahin = (t:v) (w:spread/lay/set out) (d:phah spread or lay with the linking ending in; sabuai phahin, setting the table) (e:a lano tungah a puan uh ~) (b:phah) (r:41.11.7/23.21.5) (q:draft)
phawkkhia = (t:v) (w:discover/find out/see through) (d:phawk notice with khia out; come to realise something by looking into it) (e:a banbanin thu ka ~ hi) (b:phawk) (r:21.7.27/20.28.11) (q:draft)
pheite = (t:n) (w:thighs/legs) (e:a gil leh a ~ sumngo tawh) (b:phei) (r:27.2.32/3.9.21) (q:draft)
pheite = (t:n) (w:woof/weft threads) (d:the cross threads of woven cloth, set beside tung the warp) (e:a tung leh a ~ tung hita leh) (b:phei) (r:3.13.48) (q:draft)
phunnate = (t:n) (w:grumblings/complaints/murmurings) (e:Israel mite’ ~ ka za khin hi) (b:phunna) (r:2.16.12/2.16.8) (q:draft)
piakkik = (t:v) (w:give back/restore/give again) (d:piak give with kik again or back; thu piakkik, give a further order or word) (e:Keimah in thu kong ~ mateng) (b:piak) (r:15.4.21/19.14.7) (q:draft)
piaksate = (t:n) (w:things given/those given) (d:what has been given, also of orders given and loans made) (e:Ta’ khut sungah na ~ khempeuh) (b:piaksa) (r:43.17.2/6.11.15) (q:draft)
pialsak = (t:v) (w:lead astray/cause to stray/mislead) (d:pial turn aside with sak cause; lam pialsak, lead off the right way) (e:na thupiaknate panin kei hong ~ kei in) (b:pial) (r:19.119.10/20.12.26) (q:draft)
piangsa = (t:adj) (w:happened/past) (d:piang happen with sa already; a piangsa thu, what has happened) (e:a ~ thu khempeuh khat leh khat) (b:piang) (r:42.24.14/44.5.7) (q:draft)
pianpih = (t:adj) (w:inborn/natural/from birth) (d:what one is born with; a pianpih mittaw, blind from birth, pianpih lungsim, the natural mind or instinct) (e:a ~ mittaw mi khat a mu hi) (b:pian) (r:43.9.1/49.2.3) (q:draft)
piau = (t:n) (w:bank/riverbank/edge) (d:the side of a river; a piau khempeuh, all its banks) (e:Jordan a ~ khempeuh a dimlet laitak) (r:13.12.15/23.8.7) (q:draft)
pilzaw = (t:adj) (w:wiser) (d:pil wise with zaw more, used with sangin than) (e:mite’ pilna sangin a ~ hi) (b:pil) (r:46.1.25/21.1.16) (q:draft)
puaksak = (t:v) (w:send by/have carry/let carry) (d:puak carry or send with sak cause; have someone take something to another) (e:Saul kiangah tuate a tapa David ~ hi) (b:puak) (r:9.16.20/10.18.19) (q:draft)
puaksak = (t:v) (d:with min name, make something bear a name, name it after oneself) (e:leitangte amau min a ~ hangun) (b:puak) (r:19.49.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
pukkhak = (t:v) (w:fall/stumble/fall away) (d:fall by mishap, in the verses of falling away from faith; mostly in pukkhak loh nadingin, so as not to fall) (e:Note na ~ loh nadingun) (r:43.16.1/46.10.12) (q:draft)
puteekpa = (t:n) (w:old man/aged man) (d:the ending pa marks a man) (e:Tua ciangin ~ in) (b:puteek) (r:7.19.20/3.19.32) (q:draft)
saki = (t:n) (w:horn/ram horn/trumpet) (d:the horn of an animal, also a horn blown as a trumpet) (e:Ka khuadak leh ~ li ka mu hi) (r:38.1.18/10.6.15) (q:draft)
