tuibeem = (t:n) (w:cistern/pool/reservoir) (d:a place or vessel where water is collected and stored) (e:tuinak leh ~ ahih leh siang ding hi) (r:3.11.36/34.2.8) (q:draft)
tuinakte = (t:n) (w:springs/fountains) (e:leh a ~ uh a kangsak ding hi) (b:tuinak) (r:28.13.15/14.32.3) (q:draft)
tungte = (t:n) (w:tops/heights) (d:plural of tung in the sense top or upper surface; mual tungte ah is on the mountains) (e:Israel mual ~ ah a hawkna) (b:tung) (r:26.19.9/23.13.4) (q:draft)
tungte = (t:n) (w:arrivals/those who arrive) (d:tung arrive with te, the people who arrive or have come) (e:gal sung panin hong ~’ lang khatah pang a) (b:tung) (r:14.28.12) (q:draft)
tunma = (t:adv) (w:before coming/before arriving) (d:tun arrive with ma before; hong tunma-in is before someone or something came) (e:tua khua-ah a hong ~-in Peter in) (r:48.2.12/44.2.20) (q:draft)
tunpihkik = (t:v) (w:bring back/lead back) (d:tunpih with kik back, bring someone back to a place or person) (e:Jerusalem khua sungah ka ~ ding hi) (b:tunpih) (r:38.8.8/42.1.16) (q:draft)
tuucin = (t:n) (w:shepherd/shepherding) (d:shortened form of tuucing written with an apostrophe before a following word, of a shepherd or of tending sheep) (e:suangmai tang nga tengin a ~’ thung-ip) (r:9.17.40/38.11.12) (q:draft)
ukzawhna = (t:n) (w:control/mastery/rule) (d:the power to rule over something; ki-ukzawhna or pumpi ki-ukzawhna is self-control) (e:khuapi khat ~ sangin) (b:ukzawh) (r:20.16.32/48.5.23) (q:draft)
ututun = (t:adv) (w:as one pleases/at will/freely) (d:a ututun is just as they wish, said of more than one person) (e:mi pawlkhatte in a ~ amah a bawl uh hi) (r:41.9.13/46.10.25) (q:draft)
vaksuk = (t:v) (w:go about/go to and fro) (d:used in the pair vaksuk vakto, walk down and up, go here and there through a place) (e:amaute va kuankhia-in ~ vakto-in) (r:6.18.4/3.19.16) (q:draft)
vangah = (t:n) (w:in the hole/at the opening) (d:vang opening with ah, at or into the opening; phim vangah is through the eye of a needle and han kong vangah at the mouth of the tomb) (e:Sai khat phim ~ a khumhak sangin) (b:vang) (r:42.18.25/40.27.60) (q:draft)
vankinusiate = (t:n) (w:plunder/spoils/loot) (d:goods left behind by a defeated enemy and taken by the victors) (e:Gal sungah a ngah ~ sung panin) (r:13.26.27/9.15.19) (q:draft)
vawhsak = (t:v) (w:saddle) (d:in laa van vawhsak, put the gear on a donkey for someone, saddle it) (e:Kei adingin laa van hong ~ un) (r:11.13.13/11.13.23) (q:draft)
vawhte = (t:n) (w:sowers/those who sow) (d:vawh sow with te, the people who sow seed) (e:Thuman lo khaici a ~ in lungkhamna tuak a) (b:vawh) (r:20.22.8/47.9.6) (q:draft)
vute = (t:n) (w:ashes) (e:Bawngla ~ a khawm mipa in) (r:4.19.10/12.23.4) (q:draft)
vutluahna = (t:n) (w:firepan/censer) (d:a pan for taking up ashes or carrying burning coals at the altar) (e:sikkate le ~ peekte a bawl hi) (r:2.38.3/11.7.50) (q:draft)
zaam = (t:v) (w:spread/climb/creep) (d:of a vine or its branches, grow out along or over something) (e:a hiangte kulh tungah ~ hi) (r:1.49.22/26.17.6) (q:draft)
zahun = (t:conj) (w:as much as/as far as/to the extent that) (d:zah, amount, with the plural ending un, after a clause whose subject is plural: na hih zawh zahun is as far as you are able) (e:na hih zawh ~ mi khempeuh tawh) (b:zah) (r:45.12.18/52.3.12) (q:draft)
zate = (t:n) (w:hearers/those who heard) (d:za, hear, with plural te: a zate is those who heard) (e:Tua thu a ~ in) (b:za) (r:42.18.26/44.5.11) (q:draft)
zinling = (t:n) (w:earthquake/quake) (d:zin, earthquake, and ling, shake; also written apart as a clause, zin hong ling is the earth quaked) (e:~ khit ciangin meikuang om a) (r:11.19.12/23.29.6) (q:draft)
zonzon = (t:v) (w:keep searching/search and search/look for) (d:zon, form of zong seek, doubled to show continued or repeated searching) (e:ka ~ hangin ka mu zo kei hi) (r:22.3.2/19.37.36) (q:draft)
zuautheite = (t:n) (w:liars/false ones) (d:zuauthei, liar, with plural te; after a noun it means false: kamsang zuautheite is false prophets) (e:Kamsang ~ hong piang ding uh a) (r:40.24.11/20.17.4) (q:draft)
zukhamin = (t:adv) (w:drunk/in a drunken state) (d:zukham, drunk, with the linking ending in) (e:hih mite in ~ a om kei) (b:zukham) (r:44.2.15/9.1.13) (q:draft)
zukhamna = (t:n) (w:drunkenness/intoxication) (d:the state of being drunk; zukhamna pan a pilvan is to wake from a drunken sleep) (e:~ pen haina ahi hi) (b:zukham) (r:20.20.1/1.9.24) (q:draft)
Beth-aven = (t:name) (c:city) (w:Beth Aven) (e:~ khua-ah pataukohna gingsak un) (r:28.5.8/6.7.2) (q:draft)
Eite = (t:pron) (w:we/us/our) (d:eite written with a capital at the start of a line or a quotation; whether English has we, us or our depends on its place in the sentence) (e:~ mai-ah a lamdang hi) (b:eite) (r:41.12.11/45.9.29) (q:draft)
Elio-enai = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Elioenai) (e:~, Hizkiah, leh Azrikam) (r:13.3.23/15.10.27) (q:draft)
Huhpa = (t:n) (w:Advocate/Helper/Comforter) (d:huhpa, helper, written with a capital as a title of the Holy Spirit) (e:~ a kici Kha Siangtho in) (b:huhpa) (r:43.14.26/43.16.7) (q:draft)
Lipkhaphuai = (t:adj) (w:dreadful/horrifying/abominable) (d:lipkhaphuai written with a capital in Lipkhaphuai na, the dreadful thing, for the abomination that causes desolation in Daniel) (e:~ na a suang ding uh hi) (b:lipkhaphuai) (r:27.11.31/27.12.11) (q:draft)
Lui = (t:n) (w:Wadi/stream/ravine/brook) (d:lui, stream, written with a capital as part of a place name: Izipt Lui is the Wadi of Egypt) (e:Izipt ~ panin Eufrates gun dong) (b:lui) (r:12.24.7/4.34.5) (q:draft)
Ma-akath = (t:name) (c:people) (w:Maakathite/Maakah) (d:in Ma-akath mite, the Maakathites, the people of Maakah; the place and the personal name Maakah are written Ma-akah) (e:Geshur mite leh ~ mite) (r:6.13.13/5.3.14) (q:draft)
Min = (t:n) (w:Name) (d:min, name, written with a capital for the name of God: Min Siangtho is the holy Name) (e:~ Siangtho gensia-in samsia hi) (b:min) (r:3.24.11/23.30.27) (q:draft)
Nangma = (t:det) (w:your/you) (d:nangma written with a capital, for God or at the start of a line; your before a noun, you before sungah, hang and the like) (e:Pa aw, ~ min siangtho ta hen) (b:nangma) (r:42.11.2/19.3.8) (q:draft)
Sia = (t:n) (w:Teacher/teacher) (d:sia, teacher, written with a capital as a title or a form of address: Sia aw is Teacher, when speaking to him) (e:note Topa leh ~ ka hi napi-in) (b:sia) (r:43.13.14/59.3.1) (q:draft)
Sia = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Sia) (d:head of a family of temple servants who returned from exile) (e:Keros’ suante, ~’ suante, Padon’ suante) (r:16.7.47) (q:draft)
Siangthopen = (t:adj) (w:Most Holy/holiest) (d:siangthopen written with a capital in Siangthopen Mun, the Most Holy Place of the temple) (e:Hih lai in ~ Mun ahi hi) (b:siangthopen) (r:26.41.4/26.41.23) (q:draft)
Thukhen = (t:n) (w:judgment) (d:thukhen written with a capital in fixed terms: Thukhen Ni is the Day of Judgment, Thukhen zum is the court of law) (e:~ Ni ciangin Taia le Sidon) (b:thukhen) (r:42.10.14/61.2.9) (q:draft)
Thukhen = (t:n) (w:Judge) (d:in Thukhen pa, the Judge, as a title of God) (e:Topa, ~ pa in Israel mite) (b:thukhen) (r:7.11.27) (q:draft)
To = (t:name) (c:male) (w:Tou) (d:first part of the name of a king of Hamath, written To-i in 2 Samuel and To-u in 1 Chronicles) (e:Hamath kumpipa ~-i in Hadadezer’ galkap) (r:10.8.9/13.18.9) (q:draft)
Uk = (t:n) (w:kingdom/reign/rule) (d:uk, rule, written with a capital for the reign of God: Pasian’ Uk ding hun is the time when God will rule, the kingdom of God) (e:Pasian’ ~ ding hun zong a lamen) (b:uk) (r:41.15.43/61.1.11) (q:draft)
Za = (t:num) (w:hundred) (d:za, hundred, written with a capital in the name Mi Za Khat Tausang, the Tower of the Hundred) (e:Mi ~ Khat Tausang) (b:za) (r:16.12.39) (q:draft)
Za = (t:name) (d:first part of hyphenated Hebrew names: Za-avan is Zaavan, a man, and Za-anannim is Zaanannim, a place) (e:Bilhan, ~-avan leh Akan ahi uh hi) (r:1.36.27/6.19.33) (q:draft)
ahite = (t:n) (w:those who are/the ones that are) (d:ahi, be, with plural te, turning the words before it into a noun: innkuan lutang ahite is those who are heads of families, kham ahite is the things that are of gold) (e:Pasian’ ta ~ peuhmah in leitung nate) (b:ahi) (r:62.5.4/6.22.14) (q:draft)
aloes = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:aloes) (d:loan from English, a fragrant wood and the perfume made from it) (e:~ paknamtui kungte tawh kibang a) (r:4.24.6/20.7.17) (q:draft)
ankan = (t:n) (w:roasted grain/parched grain) (d:grain roasted dry, eaten as ready food) (e:Hih ~ seu khat leh hih anlum) (r:9.17.17/6.5.11) (q:draft)
anlimte = (t:n) (w:delicacies/dainties) (d:anlim, tasty food, with plural te) (e:amah in kumpi ~ bawl ding hi) (b:anlim) (r:1.49.20/19.141.4) (q:draft)
antanna = (t:n) (w:fasting/fast) (d:going without food as a religious act) (e:Kei’ deih ~ hih bang pawl ahi hi) (b:antan) (r:23.58.6/40.17.21) (q:draft)
apte = (t:n) (w:things handed over/things entrusted/pledges) (d:ap, hand over or entrust, with plural te: khapna van a apte is the things given in pledge, ka apte is what I handed over) (e:khapna van a ~ zong pia kik hi) (b:ap) (r:26.18.7/15.8.26) (q:draft)
awngkhia = (t:v) (w:shout out/cry aloud/raise a shout) (d:awng, shout, with khia, out) (e:lungdamin ~ unla, phatna la sa un) (b:awng) (r:19.98.4/23.42.13) (q:draft)
bal = (t:v) (w:tear/rend/tear apart) (d:tear with the hands or teeth; bal khia is tear away, bal nen is break into small pieces, crumble) (e:a samatsa uh a ~ gawpgawp ngia hon) (r:26.22.27/9.15.28) (q:draft)
banna = (t:n) (w:affected part/place reached) (d:ban, reach, with na: the thing or place that something has got onto; natna a banna is the article or stone affected by the disease or mold) (e:natna a ~ suang lakhia-in) (b:ban) (r:3.14.40/3.13.54) (q:draft, low confidence)
bawla = (t:v) (w:making/having made/doing) (d:bawl, make or do, with the linking ending a; another verb follows) (e:buan ~ ka mitah a nuh khit ciangin) (b:bawl) (r:43.9.11/24.33.2) (q:draft)
bawlkhin = (t:v) (w:have made/have done) (d:bawl, make or do, with khin, already and completely) (e:kiciamna ka ~ hi) (b:bawl) (r:18.31.1/23.46.4) (q:draft)
bawlzo = (t:v) (w:have made/have done) (d:bawl, make or do, with zo marking an act as carried through) (e:Ka teelpa tawh thuciamna ka ~ a) (b:bawl) (r:19.89.3/9.21.2) (q:draft)
bawlzo = (t:v) (w:be able to do/manage to do) (d:bawl with zo in its sense of be able: a bawlzo nawn lo is no longer able to do) (e:siatna a ~ nawn lo dingin) (b:bawl) (r:19.10.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
beelpi = (t:n) (w:large pot/cauldron/vat) (d:beel, pot, with pi, big; leenggahzu kholna beelpi is a wine vat) (e:beel sung, ~ sung, leh sikbeel daite) (b:beel) (r:14.35.13/37.2.16) (q:draft)
bekun = (t:adv) (w:only/just/merely) (d:bek, only, with the ending un used when the subject is plural) (e:na guh guak ~ na om ding) (b:bek) (r:20.5.11/30.2.6) (q:draft)
bing = (t:n) (w:jar/flask/hin) (d:small container for oil, also used as a liquid measure where the English has hin) (e:sathau ~ dim khat tawh kizuisak ding hi) (r:26.46.7/26.45.24) (q:draft)
bing = (t:v) (w:be closed/be stopped up/be deaf) (d:of the ears, be unable to hear) (e:a bil uh ~ a, khua za thei) (r:24.6.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
bualtuite = (t:n) (w:pools/ponds) (d:bualtui, pool of standing water, with plural te) (e:sehnel gam pen ~ suaksak a) (b:bualtui) (r:19.107.35/23.42.15) (q:draft)
bute = (t:n) (w:officers/commanders) (d:bu, officer, with plural te: palik bute is the officers who serve the magistrates, galkapte le a bute is the soldiers and their officers) (e:Palik ~ in hih thu) (r:44.16.38/43.18.12) (q:draft)
bute = (t:n) (w:those who hide/those in hiding) (d:bu, hide, with plural te) (e:leihawm sunga ~ khempeuh pulnatna tawh si) (b:bu) (r:26.33.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
ciahpihin = (t:v) (w:taking home/bringing back/carrying off) (d:ciahpih, take home with one, with the linking ending in; another verb follows) (e:a inn-ah amaute ~ an a pia hi) (b:ciahpih) (r:44.16.34/9.23.5) (q:draft)
ciamnuihna = (t:n) (w:laughingstock/object of ridicule/byword) (d:a person or people that others make fun of) (e:leitung bup in ~-in a hong nei) (b:ciamnuih) (r:25.3.14/5.28.37) (q:draft)
ciamnuihna = (t:n) (w:joke/jest) (d:something said or done in fun: ka ciamnuihna hi is I was only joking) (e:ka ~ hi, a cipa pen) (b:ciamnuih) (r:20.26.18) (q:draft)
ciamsiatna = (t:n) (w:curse) (d:a curse or an oath that brings harm; ciamsiatna ngah is be cursed) (e:Kanaan in ~ ngah ta hen la) (r:1.9.25/1.3.14) (q:draft)
cihcih = (t:v) (w:keep saying/say again and again) (d:cih, form of ci say, doubled to show repeated or continued saying) (e:hong ~ sung teng, sun leh zanin) (r:19.42.3/43.16.18) (q:draft)
cihsan = (t:v) (w:say to/say at/reply) (d:cih, form of ci say, with san, at or toward someone: say something at a person, often to mock or to dismiss them) (e:na ~ lel uh hi) (b:cih) (r:44.12.15/19.22.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
cilesa = (t:n) (w:flesh/body/flesh and blood) (d:the flesh of the body; of kin, eima cilesa is our own flesh and blood) (e:naupangno ~ bangin a ngei bangkikin) (r:12.5.14/1.37.27) (q:draft)
cilphih = (t:v) (w:spit on/spit at) (d:from cil, saliva) (e:a maitang ~ uh a) (r:40.26.67/41.15.19) (q:draft)
cinna = (t:n) (w:guarding/watch/keeping) (d:the act or place of guarding, from cing, guard: cinna inndei is a guardroom) (e:~ inndei sungah tuate koihkik uh hi) (r:14.12.11) (q:draft)
cinna = (t:n) (w:tending/growing/keeping) (d:the place where plants or water are kept and tended: anteh cinna huan is a vegetable garden, singno cinna lo is a plot for young trees, tui lipi cinna phung is a dam that holds a pond) (e:singno ~ lo zong ka nei a) (b:cin) (r:21.2.5/5.11.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
cipa = (t:n) (w:the one who says/he who says) (d:ci, say, with pa, a male person: a cipa is the man who says) (e:hong ~ in keimah ka hi hi) (b:ci) (r:23.41.13/20.28.24) (q:draft)
cipa = (t:adv) (w:fast/tightly) (d:cip, tightly, joined to the linking a: kikalh cipa a om is being kept locked up) (e:thong huang sungah kikalh ~ a om) (b:cip) (r:24.39.15) (q:draft, low confidence)
daang = (t:v) (w:turn pale/be pale) (d:of the face or the blood, lose colour from fear) (e:a mel ~ semsem a) (r:27.5.9/27.5.6) (q:draft)
dahpih = (t:v) (w:mourn with/grieve for/sympathize with) (d:dah, mourn, with pih, together with: share in the sorrow of someone) (e:a dah mite ~ un) (b:dah) (r:45.12.15/18.30.25) (q:draft)
dak = (t:v) (w:look/look out/look around/peer) (d:lift the eyes to look: khua dak is look around, van dak is look up to the sky) (e:Balaam khua ~ a) (r:4.24.2/24.31.26) (q:draft)
dak = (t:n) (w:gong) (d:a metal gong that is struck) (e:a ging thei ~, a ging thei daltuah) (r:46.13.1) (q:draft)
damtakin = (t:adv) (w:gently/quietly/softly) (d:in a gentle, quiet or unhurried way; takin makes an adverb, like English -ly) (e:mipil pa in ~ a gen hiathiat) (r:21.9.17/44.27.13) (q:draft)
damzo = (t:v) (w:be healed/be able to recover) (d:dam, get well, with zo, be able) (e:a ~ ding hi nawn lo hi) (b:dam) (r:24.51.9/24.51.8) (q:draft)
damzo = (t:v) (w:subside/be turned away) (d:of anger, cool down: ama hehna damzo nai lo is his anger has not yet turned away) (e:ama hehna ~ nai lo a) (b:dam) (r:23.10.4/23.9.12) (q:draft)
dawilawm = (t:n) (w:demon/evil spirit) (d:dawilawm nei is having a demon, demon-possessed) (e:Keimah in ~ nei ka hi kei hi) (r:43.8.49/43.10.20) (q:draft)
dawnkhawm = (t:v) (w:drink together/drink with) (d:dawn, drink, with khawm, together; often paired with nekhawm, eat together) (e:an nekhawm tui ~ na hi uh hiam) (b:dawn) (r:42.5.30/24.16.8) (q:draft)
delhmang = (t:v) (w:chase away/drive off/frighten away) (d:chase something until it is gone) (e:tuate a ~ ding kuamah om lo) (r:24.7.33/24.50.17) (q:draft)
deuh = (t:adv) (w:rather/somewhat/a little more) (d:placed after a descriptive word or after zaw, more, to show a slightly greater degree: gamla zaw deuh is a little farther, ma deuh is a little before) (e:hong khauh kik zaw ~ hi) (r:27.10.18/23.18.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
diksakna = (t:n) (w:justification/vindication) (d:being declared or shown to be in the right; diksakna ngah is be justified, be proved right) (e:Pasian kiang panin ~ ngah ding hi) (b:diksak) (r:19.24.5/45.4.6) (q:draft)
dinginah = (t:ppm) (w:in order to/so as to) (d:dingin, in order to, with ah: placed after a verb to state the purpose of the main action) (e:A bia ~ ka hong pai uh hi) (b:dingin) (r:40.2.2/54.2.6) (q:draft)
dongkik = (t:v) (w:ask again/ask further/ask in return) (d:dong, ask, with kik, again or back) (e:ci-in a ~ uh hi) (b:dong) (r:43.1.25/9.10.22) (q:draft)
duhgawh = (t:v) (w:crave/covet/desire greedily) (d:want food or the goods of others too strongly) (e:mite’ neihsa na ~ kei ding uh hi) (r:52.4.12/19.141.4) (q:draft)
elna = (t:n) (w:malice/ill will/envy) (d:hostile feeling toward someone; elna tawh is maliciously) (e:Ka galte in ~ tawh keima thu gen) (b:el) (r:19.41.5/2.23.1) (q:draft)
enna = (t:n) (w:envy/jealousy) (d:ill feeling at the good of another, not from en, look; enna lungsim is an envious mind) (e:~ le huaihamna a om nakleh) (r:59.3.16/41.7.22) (q:draft)
gamdangah = (t:adv) (w:in a foreign land/to another land/among the nations) (d:gamdang, foreign land, with ah, in or to) (e:i muh bangin amaute ~ lawn hi) (b:gamdang) (r:5.29.28/26.4.13) (q:draft)
gawizan = (t:v) (w:crush/grind/thresh/trample) (d:crush or tread something until it is broken small, as grain is threshed or grapes are trodden) (e:leivui bangin a neel dongin ka ~ hi) (r:5.9.21/23.41.15) (q:draft)
gawmin = (t:v) (w:joining/combining/putting together) (d:gawm, join or combine, with the linking ending in; often rendered together or all together) (e:amaute neihsa khempeuh ~ a zangkhawm uh hi) (b:gawm) (r:44.2.44/6.11.5) (q:draft)
gawsem = (t:n) (w:harp) (d:a musical instrument, rendered harp in Revelation, where tamngai is the pipe; gawsem tumte is those who play it; in everyday use perhaps the gourd mouth organ, a wind instrument) (e:~ tumte, la siamte, tamngai tumte) (r:66.18.22/66.14.2) (q:draft, low confidence)
gendai = (t:v) (w:slander/revile/blaspheme) (d:speak evil of someone; gendai-mawhna is the sin of speaking against God, blasphemy) (e:mi a ~ thei mi) (r:55.3.3/16.9.18) (q:draft)
genkholhnate = (t:n) (w:prophecies/predictions/visions) (d:genkholhna, a thing told beforehand, with plural te; also of warnings and threats made in advance) (e:~ a tung om lo hi) (b:genkholhna) (r:26.12.22/66.22.10) (q:draft)
genkholhsa = (t:v) (w:foretold/said beforehand) (d:genkholh, tell beforehand, with sa, already done: a genkholhsa bangin is as he had foretold) (e:Topa in a ~ bangin Babilon kumpipa in) (b:genkholh) (r:12.24.12/40.21.4) (q:draft)
genzo = (t:v) (w:have said/have spoken/have told) (d:gen, tell, with zo marking an act as carried through) (e:Topa in thu a ~ hi) (b:gen) (r:24.13.15/43.5.33) (q:draft)
