paisukna = (t:n) (w:way down/descent/slope) (d:paisuk go down with the noun ending na, the place where a road goes down) (e:Oliv Mual tung pan a ~ mun) (b:paisuk) (r:42.19.37/12.12.20) (q:draft)
paitheih = (t:v) (w:be able to come/be able to go) (d:pai go or come with theih can; mostly in paitheih nading, so that one may come) (e:note kiangah ka hong ~ nading) (b:pai) (r:45.1.10/49.3.12) (q:draft)
palai = (t:n) (w:envoy/mediator/go-between/ambassador) (d:palai sem is to act as an envoy or mediator) (e:kilemna ding ~ semte nakpitakin kap uh hi) (r:23.33.7) (q:draft)
palai = (t:v) (w:intervene/mediate) (e:Finehas dingin hong ~ a) (r:19.106.30) (q:draft)
pama = (t:adv) (w:around/nearby/beside) (d:pam side or vicinity with the place ending a; usually paired with kim or kiim, a kim a pama, all around) (e:Kiim le ~ minam dangte’ kiang pan) (b:pam) (r:16.5.17/25.1.12) (q:draft)
pawmin = (t:v) (w:join/side with/rally around) (d:pawm hold to or embrace with the linking ending in; taking someone's side) (e:mite in Jefthah ~ amah tawh) (b:pawm) (r:7.11.3/16.10.29) (q:draft)
pawmsak = (t:v) (w:make swell/leaven/make rise) (d:pawm swell with causative sak, said of yeast in dough and of a swelling body) (e:a annel lom khempeuh a ~ hi) (b:pawm) (r:42.13.21/4.5.21) (q:draft)
peekpi = (t:n) (w:expanse/sheet/broad flat surface) (d:peek flat piece with pi great; van peekpi is the expanse of the sky, limlang peekpi a great sheet of glass) (e:limlang ~ kiphah tuipi tawh a kibang) (b:peek) (r:66.15.2/18.37.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
peh = (t:v) (w:graft/graft in) (d:join a branch or shoot onto another plant) (e:Pasian in amaute khatvei a ~ kik thei hi) (r:45.11.23/45.11.19) (q:draft)
phawkzo = (t:v) (w:be able to notice/be able to remember/perceive) (d:phawk notice or remember with zo, be able or manage to) (e:ka thuciamna ka ~ hi) (b:phawk) (r:2.6.5/18.14.21) (q:draft)
phelkhap = (t:v) (w:split/divide/cut through) (d:said of rivers or waters dividing the land) (e:Tuipi tawh leitung na ~ hi) (r:35.3.9/23.18.7) (q:draft)
phialphiah = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:swallow/swift) (d:a small fast-flying bird) (e:a leengsuk a leengto ~ tawh kibang) (r:20.26.2/19.84.3) (q:draft)
phinin = (t:v) (w:provoke/arouse to anger) (d:phin with the linking ending in, provoking) (e:Topa ~ na hehsak uh hi) (b:phin) (r:5.9.22/7.2.12) (q:draft)
phinna = (t:n) (w:provocation/taunt) (d:phin provoke with the noun ending na) (e:amau’ hong ~ in hong lungzingsak hi) (b:phin) (r:18.17.2/12.23.26) (q:draft)
phongin = (t:v) (w:wake/rouse) (d:phong wake someone with the linking ending in) (e:A nungzuite in amah ~) (b:phong) (r:41.4.38/44.12.7) (q:draft)
phongin = (t:n) (w:raft) (d:phong raft with the ending in, as rafts, said of logs floated by sea) (e:~ tuipi tungah Joppa dong) (r:14.2.16/11.5.9) (q:draft, low confidence)
phop = (t:v) (w:mend/patch/sew) (d:repair cloth by sewing a piece on) (e:puan lui a ~ kei hi) (r:40.9.16/21.3.7) (q:draft)
phualte = (t:n) (w:places/sites/camps) (d:biakna phualte are places of worship, galpanna phualte are siege camps) (e:biakna ~-ah numei-pasal paktat pawlte) (b:phual) (r:11.14.24/26.4.2) (q:draft)
phuang = (t:v) (w:start/stir up/strike up) (d:set something going, as war, gal phuang, or a song, la phuang) (e:gal ~ ngitnget uh hi) (r:19.140.2/19.81.2) (q:draft)
phuansak = (t:v) (w:make foam/churn up) (d:phuan foam with causative sak, said of the sea) (e:tuipi ~ pheuphau hi) (b:phuan) (r:18.41.32/65.1.13) (q:draft)
phukpai = (t:v) (w:cut down/hew down/fell) (d:phuk fell with pai away, said of idols and sacred poles) (e:amau’ Asherah milimte na ~ ding hi) (r:2.34.13/5.12.3) (q:draft)
phulak = (t:v) (w:avenge/take vengeance) (d:pay back a wrong done; phulak ni is the day of vengeance) (e:keima khut tawh ~ nading panin) (r:9.25.33/23.34.8) (q:draft)
phumcip = (t:v) (w:bury/submerge/swallow up) (d:put completely under earth or water; phum with cip, tightly, completely) (e:Lei sungah amaute ~ in la) (b:phum) (r:18.40.13/22.8.7) (q:draft)
piakkhawm = (t:v) (w:give together with/offer along with) (d:give one thing together with another, of the grain offering that goes with an animal offering; piak, give, with khawm, together) (e:tuutal khat tawh ~ dingin) (b:piak) (r:4.15.6/26.46.11) (q:draft)
piakkhiat = (t:v) (w:give out/give up/lay down) (d:give away from oneself; nuntakna piakkhiat is lay down the life) (e:Ka nuntakna ~ theih nading) (b:piak) (r:43.10.18/15.7.16) (q:draft)
piakkhop = (t:v) (w:give together with/offer along with) (d:give one thing along with another; another form of piakkhawm) (e:tuunote tawh ~ ding pen) (r:26.46.7/26.46.5) (q:draft)
piaknop = (t:v) (w:want to give/be willing to give) (d:piak, give, with nop, want; ama piaknop zahzah is as much as he wants to give) (e:ka ~ peuhpeuh tungah ka pia thei) (r:42.4.6/26.46.5) (q:draft)
piakpa = (t:n) (w:the one given to) (d:the man to whom something is given; piak, give, with pa marking a male person. Topa thupha piakpa is the one blessed by the Lord) (e:amah thupha ka ~ kua ahi hiam) (b:piak) (r:1.27.33/43.13.26) (q:draft)
piankhiatna = (t:n) (w:origin/source/place of origin) (d:where a person or thing comes from) (e:hih mipa hong ~ i theih hi a) (r:43.7.27/62.4.7) (q:draft)
piikpeek = (t:adv) (w:completely/fully/utterly) (d:placed after a verb or descriptive word to show that something is complete or full to the limit) (e:galhiam kicing ~ tawh a kuankhia ding) (r:27.11.13/25.2.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
puahsak = (t:v) (w:repair/restore/set right) (d:puah, repair, with sak: have something repaired, or repair it for someone) (e:a sia khempeuh kong ~ kik ding hi) (b:puah) (r:26.36.33/12.12.5) (q:draft)
puakkham = (t:v) (w:burst/break out) (d:burst open, as a wineskin; of boils, break out on the skin) (e:leenggahtui um bangin ka ~ ding hi) (r:18.32.19/2.9.10) (q:draft)
puanhoih = (t:n) (w:fine clothes/beautiful robe) (d:puan, cloth or garment, with hoih, good) (e:~ a silhpa enin) (r:59.2.2/6.7.21) (q:draft)
puantualpite = (t:n) (w:robes) (d:long outer garments, of a king or a bride) (e:na ~ nong silh ding hi) (b:puantualpi) (r:14.18.29/19.45.8) (q:draft)
puanungah = (t:adv) (w:outside/in the outer part) (d:puanung, outer, with the place marker ah; tual puanungah is in or to the outer court) (e:tual ~ hong pusuahpih a) (b:puanung) (r:26.46.21/26.42.1) (q:draft)
pukkhawm = (t:v) (w:fall together) (d:puk, fall, with khawm, together) (e:a nihun a ~ uh hi) (b:puk) (r:24.46.12/14.25.19) (q:draft)
pulepate = (t:n) (w:ancestors/forefathers/fathers) (d:pu le pa, grandfather and father, with plural te) (e:amau’ ~ tawh ka thuciamna) (r:3.26.45/6.21.43) (q:draft)
saang = (t:v) (w:accept/receive/take) (d:take what is offered or said, also accept as true and approve) (e:a neipa in tua kiciamna ~ ding a) (r:2.22.11/5.26.4) (q:draft)
sabengpa = (t:n) (w:hunter) (d:a man who hunts animals; sabeng with pa marking a male person) (e:a vanglian ~ zong ahi hi) (r:1.10.9/20.6.5) (q:draft)
sagawh = (t:n) (w:sacrifice/animal sacrifice) (d:killing of an animal as an offering, used in sagawh biakna, sacrifice) (e:~ biakna sangin hehpihna ka deih zaw) (r:40.9.13/41.12.33) (q:draft)
sakhite = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:deer/gazelles) (d:plural of sakhi; the Bible uses it for deer, gazelles and does, and in Psalm 104 for the hyrax) (e:~ a suah laitakin nau va dom) (b:sakhi) (r:18.39.1/11.4.23) (q:draft)
sakzaw = (t:adj) (w:harder) (d:sak, hard, with zaw, more) (e:Suang khempeuh sangin a ~) (r:26.3.9/24.5.3) (q:draft)
sakzaw = (t:part) (d:sak, cause, with zaw, more, placed after a verb: cause to be more so; lungdam sakzaw is please more) (e:Topa lungdam ~ ding hi) (b:sak) (r:19.69.31) (q:draft, low confidence)
samsiatsak = (t:v) (w:curse for/put a curse on) (d:curse someone on behalf of another; samsiat with sak) (e:hih mite hong ~ in) (b:samsiat) (r:4.22.17/4.23.13) (q:draft)
sangun = (t:prep) (w:than) (d:sang, than, in a comparison, with un marking a plural subject; the same as sangin) (e:na pu na pate ~ na siahuai) (r:24.16.12/37.2.19) (q:draft)
sante = (t:adj) (w:red) (d:san, red, with plural te: the red ones; sakol sante are red horses, lo-uih sante are red onions) (e:lo-uih neute, lo-uih ~) (b:san) (r:4.11.5/38.6.6) (q:draft)
sapsap = (t:v) (w:call again and again/keep calling) (d:sap, call, doubled to show repeated action) (e:Ka kipawl pihte ka ~ hangin) (r:25.1.19) (q:draft)
sapsap = (t:adv) (w:quivering) (d:after ling or liing, tremble: shaking with quick small movements) (e:ka muk liing ~ hi) (r:35.3.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
