sehkhatte = (t:n) (w:one part/portions) (d:sehkhat, one part, with plural te: the people or things that make up one part; seh thum ah sehkhatte is a third of them, sehsawm suah sehkhatte are tithes) (e:Tua a suakta ~ pen) (b:sehkhat) (r:38.13.9/16.12.44) (q:draft)
semkik = (t:v) (w:work again/do again/resume) (d:sem, work, with kik, again: take up a work once more) (e:ka nasep ngei ~ dingin) (b:sem) (r:27.8.27/38.11.15) (q:draft)
seng = (t:v) (w:store/put away/stow) (d:put goods into a place for keeping) (e:ka neih khempeuh ka ~ ding hi) (r:42.12.18/14.5.1) (q:draft)
sese = (t:adv) (w:ever/at all) (d:adds force to a question with bang hangin, why: why ever, why of all things) (e:mi khem hatte gualzo ~ ahi hiam) (r:24.12.1/24.20.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
siahdong = (t:n) (w:tax collector/publican) (d:siah, tax, with dong, ask or demand) (e:Thomas leh ~ Mattiu) (r:40.10.3/42.19.2) (q:draft)
siamlawngpi = (t:n) (w:weaver's beam/weaver's rod) (d:the large beam of a loom, used as a picture of a very thick spear shaft) (e:a teipi kung ~ cia a pha) (r:13.20.5/13.11.23) (q:draft)
siathei = (t:adj) (w:perishable/corruptible) (d:sia, spoil or go bad, with thei, able; a siathei lo is imperishable. A siathei tawpin is as badly as they can) (e:a ~ pumpi pen a ~ lo pumpi) (b:sia) (r:46.15.50/60.1.7) (q:draft)
sihkhawm = (t:v) (w:die together/die with) (d:sih, die, with khawm, together) (e:Khrih tawh i ~ leh amah tawh) (b:sih) (r:45.6.8/41.14.31) (q:draft)
sihtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to die/may die) (d:sih, die, with theih, can; a sihtheih nadingin is so that he may die) (e:a ~ nadingin ama kiang panin nungkik un) (b:sih) (r:10.11.15/66.9.6) (q:draft)
sikcipsak = (t:v) (w:trample down/tread down) (d:sikcip, tread firmly on, with sak: tread down for someone) (e:i galte hong ~ dingpa ahi hi) (r:19.60.12/19.108.13) (q:draft)
sikin = (t:v) (w:treading/trampling/stepping on) (d:sik, tread, with in linking to the next verb) (e:ama tung ~ pai uh a) (b:sik) (r:12.7.17/66.10.2) (q:draft)
siklong = (t:n) (w:bell) (d:small metal bell, of the gold bells on the hem of the priestly robe) (e:amaute’ kikal-ah kham ~ bawlin) (r:2.28.33/2.39.26) (q:draft)
siklukhute = (t:n) (w:helmets) (d:sik lukhu, iron head covering, with plural te) (e:Lumte leh ~ tawh kidalin) (b:siklukhu) (r:26.23.24/14.26.14) (q:draft)
sikseekpa = (t:n) (w:blacksmith/smith/metalworker) (d:a man who forges metal; sik, iron, and seek, forge, with pa marking a male person) (e:hiam a bawl ~ ka piangsak khin hi) (r:23.54.16/23.44.12) (q:draft)
sikseekte = (t:n) (w:smiths/metalworkers/artisans) (d:plural of sikseek, one who forges metal) (e:khutsiamte leh ~ khempeuh ciahpih hi) (r:12.24.14/24.29.2) (q:draft)
sikte = (t:n) (w:iron/metals) (d:sik, iron, with plural te: iron things; in Malachi 3.2 the metals that are refined) (e:~ a siangthosak mei) (b:sik) (r:39.3.2/18.41.27) (q:draft)
silesa = (t:n) (w:flesh/body/flesh and blood) (d:the human body; leitung silesa is the earthly body, human nature or human descent) (e:ka pumpi ~ zong kiamgawp khinta hi) (r:19.109.24/45.1.3) (q:draft)
simmawhsak = (t:v) (w:make despised/let be scorned) (d:simmawh, despise, with sak: make or let others despise someone) (e:mite kong ~ ding hi) (b:simmawh) (r:24.49.15/46.16.11) (q:draft)
